  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: Create a polished FRONTEND-ONLY prototype for an Indian \342\200\234Crowd-Sourced Civic Issue Reporting & Resolution Platform\342\200\235.\n\nThe prototype has TWO completely different interfaces:\n\n1. CITIZEN / CUSTOMER APPLICATION\n2. GOVERNMENT / MUNICIPAL ADMINISTRATION DASHBOARD\n\nThe purpose of this prototype is to demonstrate the complete user experience and operational workflow to hackathon judges.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Frontend only.\n- Use realistic mock data.\n- No real backend required.\n- Simulate all interactions with local state/mock JSON.\n- Make the prototype fully navigable.\n- Buttons should visibly work where possible.\n- Use realistic Indian civic examples.\n- Do not make it look like a generic CRM.\n- Do not overload the citizen interface.\n- Make the government interface information-dense and operational.\n- Maintain a clean, professional, modern civic-tech aesthetic.\n- Use consistent spacing, alignment, typography, cards, borders and component sizing.\n- Desktop-first for the government dashboard.\n- Responsive mobile-first design for the citizen application.\n- Use a professional light theme with subtle civic/technology styling.\n- Avoid excessive gradients, glassmorphism, neon colors, giant illustrations, or unnecessary decorative elements.\n\n==================================================\nGLOBAL PRODUCT IDENTITY\n==================================================\n\nProduct name:\n\n\342\200\234CivicPulse\342\200\235\n\nTagline:\n\n\342\200\234Report. Resolve. Verify.\342\200\235\n\nUse a simple professional logo/icon suggesting:\nLocation + civic infrastructure + community.\n\nPrimary design language:\n- Clean\n- Trustworthy\n- Government-grade\n- Accessible\n- Modern\n- Data-driven\n\nUse a restrained color system:\n- Dark navy / charcoal for primary text\n- White / very light grey backgrounds\n- One strong accent color for primary actions\n- Red/orange for urgent issues\n- Green for resolved/verified\n- Amber for pending/warning\n- Grey for neutral states\n\nTypography:\nUse a highly legible modern sans-serif such as Inter.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 CITIZEN APPLICATION\n==================================================\n\nThe citizen side must feel extremely simple.\n\nThe core principle is:\n\n\342\200\234Anyone should be able to report a civic problem in less than one minute.\342\200\235\n\nCreate these screens:\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 1 \342\200\224 CITIZEN HOME DASHBOARD\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nHeader:\n- CivicPulse logo\n- Current city/area\n- Notification icon\n- Profile icon\n\nMain hero section:\n\n\342\200\234See a civic problem?\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Report it in a few seconds.\342\200\235\n\nLarge primary CTA:\n\n\342\200\234+ Report an Issue\342\200\235\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\n\342\200\234Track My Reports\342\200\235\n\nBelow that, show:\n\n\342\200\234Recent Issues Near You\342\200\235\n\nSmall cards showing:\n- Issue photo\n- Issue type\n- Location\n- Status\n- Date\n\nExample:\n\342\200\234Large pothole near bus stop\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Anna Nagar\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Assigned\342\200\235\n\342\200\2342 hours ago\342\200\235\n\nAlso show a compact summary:\n\nMy Reports\n- 7 Total\n- 4 Resolved\n- 2 In Progress\n- 1 Reopened\n\nBottom mobile navigation:\n- Home\n- Report\n- My Reports\n- Notifications\n- Profile\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 2 \342\200\224 REPORT ISSUE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDesign this as a very simple step-by-step flow.\n\nSTEP 1:\n\342\200\234Capture the problem\342\200\235\n\nLarge camera/upload component.\n\nButtons:\n\342\200\234Take Photo\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Upload Photo\342\200\235\n\nShow image preview after selection.\n\nSTEP 2:\n\342\200\234Where is it?\342\200\235\n\nShow:\n- Automatically detected location\n- Small map\n- Address\n- \342\200\234Adjust location\342\200\235 button\n\nExample:\n\342\200\23412, Anna Nagar Main Road\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Location detected automatically\342\200\235\n\nSTEP 3:\n\342\200\234What happened?\342\200\235\n\nLarge simple text/voice input.\n\nPlaceholder:\n\342\200\234Describe the problem in your own words\342\200\246\342\200\235\n\nButtons:\n- Type\n- \360\237\216\244 Record Voice\n\nLanguage selector:\nEnglish\n\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\nOther Indian languages\n\nSTEP 4:\nAI ASSIST\n\nDisplay a small non-intrusive panel:\n\n\342\200\234We think this is:\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Pothole\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Confidence: 96%\342\200\235\n\nAllow:\n\342\200\234Correct category\342\200\235\n\nShow detected category options if changed.\n\nSTEP 5:\nSUBMIT\n\nLarge CTA:\n\342\200\234Submit Report\342\200\235\n\nAfter submission show:\n\n\342\200\234Report Submitted\342\200\235\n\nIssue ID:\n\342\200\234CIV-10482\342\200\235\n\nMessage:\n\342\200\234We\342\200\231ve received your report. We\342\200\231ll keep you updated.\342\200\235\n\nImportant:\nShow a simple progress timeline.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 3 \342\200\224 OFFLINE REPORTING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDemonstrate offline capability in the frontend.\n\nA small banner:\n\n\342\200\234Offline mode\342\200\235\n\342\200\234No internet connection\342\200\235\n\nAllow user to continue creating a report.\n\nAfter submission:\n\n\342\200\234Saved on your device\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Your report will automatically sync when connectivity returns.\342\200\235\n\nShow:\n\342\200\2342 reports waiting to sync\342\200\235\n\nThis feature should be visually clear because it is an important requirement.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 4 \342\200\224 MY REPORTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nList the citizen\342\200\231s submitted issues.\n\nEach card should show:\n\nIssue image\nIssue ID\nIssue type\nLocation\nDate\nStatus\n\nStatus examples:\n- Submitted\n- Under Review\n- Assigned\n- In Progress\n- Resolved\n- Awaiting Verification\n- Reopened\n\nAdd filters:\nAll\nActive\nResolved\nReopened\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 5 \342\200\224 ISSUE DETAILS / TRACKING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThis is an important screen.\n\nShow:\n\nIssue #CIV-10482\n\nLarge issue image.\n\nDetails:\nType:\nPothole\n\nLocation:\nAnna Nagar Main Road\n\nReported:\n27 Aug 2026, 10:14 AM\n\nPriority:\nHigh\n\nReports supporting this issue:\n43 citizens\n\nThen show a clean vertical timeline:\n\n\342\234\223 Report submitted\n\342\234\223 AI analysis completed\n\342\234\223 Issue verified\n\342\234\223 Assigned to Roads Department\n\342\234\223 Field team assigned\n\342\234\223 Repair started\n\342\234\223 Marked resolved\n\342\206\222 Awaiting your verification\n\nEach event should have:\n- Timestamp\n- Status\n- Short description\n\nAt the bottom:\n\n\342\200\234Has this issue been resolved?\342\200\235\n\nTwo large buttons:\n\n\342\200\234\342\234\223 Confirm Resolution\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234\342\234\225 Not Resolved \342\200\224 Reopen\342\200\235\n\nIf reopened, simulate:\n\342\200\234Issue reopened and returned to Roads Department.\342\200\235\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 6 \342\200\224 RESOLUTION VERIFICATION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nWhen an issue is marked resolved:\n\nShow:\n\n\342\200\234Is the problem actually fixed?\342\200\235\n\nBefore photo\nvs\nAfter photo\n\nShow resolution evidence:\n- Completion date\n- Department\n- Field team\n- Location confirmation\n\nButtons:\n\342\200\234Confirm Resolution\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Reopen Issue\342\200\235\n\nThis should visually communicate that government cannot simply mark an issue closed without citizen verification.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 7 \342\200\224 NOTIFICATIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a clean notification center.\n\nExamples:\n\n\342\200\234Your issue CIV-10482 was assigned to the Roads Department.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Repair work has started.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Issue CIV-10482 has been marked resolved. Please verify.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Issue CIV-10482 has been reopened.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Critical road hazard reported near your area.\342\200\235\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 8 \342\200\224 CITIZEN PROFILE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSimple profile page.\n\nShow:\n- Name\n- Preferred language\n- Saved area\n- Reports submitted\n- Issues confirmed\n- Issues reopened\n\nOptional:\n\342\200\234Community contribution\342\200\235\n\nExample:\n\342\200\23427 civic reports submitted\342\200\235\n\342\200\23491% verified\342\200\235\n\nKeep this lightweight.\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 GOVERNMENT / MUNICIPAL DASHBOARD\n==================================================\n\nThis must be COMPLETELY different from the citizen UI.\n\nIt should look like a professional municipal command center.\n\nUse:\n- Desktop-first layout\n- Fixed left sidebar\n- Top header\n- Dense but readable data\n- Tables\n- Filters\n- KPI cards\n- GIS map\n- Charts\n- Issue queues\n- Detailed records\n\nSidebar navigation:\n\n1. Overview\n2. Live Issue Map\n3. Issue Queue\n4. Departments\n5. Field Operations\n6. SLA & Escalations\n7. Citizen Reports\n8. Analytics\n9. Recurring Hotspots\n10. Settings\n\nTop bar:\n- Municipality name\n- Search\n- Notifications\n- User profile\n- Date/time\n- Current operational status\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 1 \342\200\224 GOVERNMENT OVERVIEW\n==================================================\n\nHeader:\n\342\200\234Municipal Operations Overview\342\200\235\n\nTop KPI cards:\n\nTotal Open Issues\n2,481\n\nCritical\n86\n\nHigh Priority\n413\n\nIn Progress\n724\n\nResolved Today\n183\n\nSLA Breaches\n32\n\nAverage Resolution Time\n18.4 hrs\n\nCitizen Verification Rate\n87%\n\nBelow KPIs:\n\nLEFT:\nLive civic issue map.\n\nMap markers:\n- Red = Critical\n- Orange = High\n- Yellow = Medium\n- Green = Resolved\n\nShow clustered issue markers.\n\nRIGHT:\n\342\200\234Priority Queue\342\200\235\n\nTop 8 issues requiring attention.\n\nEach row:\nIssue ID\nType\nWard\nPriority\nReports\nAge\nDepartment\nSLA\n\nExample:\nCIV-10482 | Open Manhole | Ward 37 | Critical | 43 | 2h | Roads | 1h 12m remaining\n\nBelow:\nDepartment performance cards:\nRoads\nSanitation\nElectrical\nDrainage\nWater\n\nEach showing:\nOpen\nIn Progress\nResolved\nSLA compliance\n\nBottom:\n\342\200\234Recurring Problem Hotspots\342\200\235\n\nShow a small bar/heatmap-style visualization.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 2 \342\200\224 LIVE ISSUE MAP\n==================================================\n\nMake the map the main focus.\n\nLeft filter panel:\n- Issue type\n- Priority\n- Status\n- Department\n- Ward\n- Date range\n- Verification state\n\nMap:\nFull city/municipality map.\n\nMarkers should be clickable.\n\nClicking a marker opens:\n\nIssue #CIV-10482\nPothole\nCritical\n43 reports\nWard 37\nRoads Department\nSLA: 1h 12m\n\nButtons:\n\342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Assign\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Escalate\342\200\235\n\nShow clustering for nearby duplicate reports.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 3 \342\200\224 ISSUE QUEUE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a detailed operational table.\n\nColumns:\n\nPriority\nIssue ID\nIssue Type\nLocation\nWard\nReports\nConfidence\nDepartment\nAssigned Team\nAge\nSLA\nStatus\nActions\n\nExample rows:\n\nCRITICAL | CIV-10482 | Open Manhole | Ward 37 | 43 reports | 98% | Roads | Team B | 2h | 1h remaining | Assigned\n\nHIGH | CIV-10473 | Garbage | Ward 12 | 27 reports | 94% | Sanitation | Team A | 5h | 3h remaining | In Progress\n\nUse strong visual status chips.\n\nProvide:\n- Search\n- Sort\n- Filter\n- Bulk assignment\n- Export\n- Pagination\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 4 \342\200\224 ISSUE DETAIL / CASE MANAGEMENT\n==================================================\n\nThis should be the most detailed government screen.\n\nHeader:\n\n\342\200\234Civic Issue #CIV-10482\342\200\235\n\nStatus:\nCRITICAL\nASSIGNED\n\nMain layout:\n\nLEFT COLUMN:\nEvidence\n\nCitizen photos\nLocation map\nBefore photo\nAfter photo\n\nMIDDLE COLUMN:\nIssue intelligence\n\nIssue type:\nOpen Manhole\n\nAI confidence:\n97%\n\nDuplicate cluster:\n13 reports\n\nSpam risk:\nLow\n\nPriority score:\n96/100\n\nJurisdiction:\nWard 37\n\nResponsible authority:\nMunicipal Corporation\n\nDepartment:\nRoads\n\nNearby risk:\nSchool \342\200\224 120m\n\nRIGHT COLUMN:\nWorkflow\n\nCurrent owner:\nRoad Maintenance Team B\n\nSupervisor:\nOfficer Name\n\nSLA:\n1h 12m remaining\n\nAssignment:\n27 Aug 2026, 10:42 AM\n\nButtons:\nAssign\nReassign\nEscalate\nStart Work\nMark Resolved\n\nBelow all columns:\n\nTIMELINE\n\nShow the entire issue history.\n\nThen:\n\nCITIZEN REPORT CLUSTER\n\n\342\200\23443 citizen reports consolidated into this issue\342\200\235\n\nShow a list/map of supporting reports.\n\nThis screen should strongly communicate:\n\342\200\234Many reports \342\206\222 One physical issue.\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 5 \342\200\224 DEPARTMENT MANAGEMENT\n==================================================\n\nShow department cards:\n\nRoads\nSanitation\nElectrical\nDrainage\nWater\nParks\n\nEach card:\nOpen issues\nCritical\nAssigned\nOverdue\nResolved today\nSLA %\n\nClicking department opens its work queue.\n\nExample:\n\n\342\200\234Roads Department\342\200\235\n\nOpen:\n482\n\nCritical:\n31\n\nHigh:\n97\n\nOverdue:\n18\n\nAverage resolution:\n14.2 hrs\n\nBelow:\nAssigned teams and workload.\n\nExample:\n\nTeam A\n8 active\n2 critical\n\nTeam B\n12 active\n1 critical\n\nTeam C\n4 active\n\nUse workload visualization.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 6 \342\200\224 FIELD OPERATIONS\n==================================================\n\nShow field teams.\n\nFor each team:\n\nTeam name\nCurrent location\nActive jobs\nPriority jobs\nCompleted today\nCurrent assignment\n\nExample:\n\n\342\200\234Road Maintenance Team B\342\200\235\n\nActive:\n4\n\nCurrent:\nCIV-10482\n\nDistance:\n1.2 km\n\nETA:\n8 min\n\nButtons:\n\342\200\234View Route\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Open Assignment\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 7 \342\200\224 SLA & ESCALATIONS\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nSLA compliance:\n87%\n\nIssues approaching breach\nIssues already breached\nAverage response time\nAverage resolution time\n\nCreate a timeline/table:\n\nIssue\nDepartment\nAssigned\nSLA\nTime remaining\nEscalation level\n\nUse visual warning indicators.\n\nExample:\n\nCIV-10473\nSanitation\nSLA breached\n2h 41m overdue\nSupervisor escalation\n\nAllow:\nEscalate\nReassign\nExtend with reason\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 8 \342\200\224 CITIZEN REPORT MANAGEMENT\n==================================================\n\nShow raw incoming reports before/while they are processed.\n\nEach report:\n\nPhoto\nDescription\nLocation\nLanguage\nAI category\nAI confidence\nTrust score\nDuplicate probability\nSpam probability\n\nExample:\n\nReport #R10983\n\nLanguage:\nTamil\n\nAI category:\nPothole \342\200\224 94%\n\nDuplicate probability:\n91%\n\nTrust score:\n87%\n\nAction:\n\342\200\234Merge with CIV-10482\342\200\235\n\nAlso show states:\n\nLegitimate\nNeeds Review\nSpam\nDuplicate\n\nThis demonstrates how the platform reduces municipal workload.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 9 \342\200\224 ANALYTICS\n==================================================\n\nCreate an advanced analytics dashboard.\n\nSections:\n\nCITY OVERVIEW\n- Total reports\n- Unique issues\n- Resolution rate\n- Reopen rate\n- Average response time\n- Average resolution time\n\nISSUE DISTRIBUTION\nBar chart:\nPotholes\nGarbage\nStreetlights\nDrainage\nFootpaths\n\nDEPARTMENT PERFORMANCE\nCompare departments by:\n- Response time\n- Resolution time\n- SLA compliance\n- Backlog\n\nTREND ANALYSIS\nShow issue counts over time.\n\nRECURRING HOTSPOTS\nShow top locations with repeated problems.\n\nExample:\n\n\342\200\234Ward 37\342\200\235\nPotholes:\n2024 \342\200\224 18\n2025 \342\200\224 31\n2026 \342\200\224 47\n\nFlag:\n\342\200\234Recurring infrastructure problem\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 10 \342\200\224 RECURRING HOTSPOTS\n==================================================\n\nMain purpose:\nIdentify locations that repeatedly experience civic failures.\n\nShow:\n\nLocation\nIssue type\nReports over time\nNumber of repairs\nNumber of reopenings\nLast repair\nRisk level\n\nExample:\n\nRoad X\n\nPotholes:\n96\n\nRepairs:\n7\n\nReopened:\n4\n\nTrend:\nIncreasing\n\nStatus:\n\342\200\234Investigate recurring infrastructure failure\342\200\235\n\nAdd a map with hotspot intensity.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 11 \342\200\224 NOTIFICATIONS / ALERT CENTER\n==================================================\n\nMunicipal alerts:\n\n\342\200\234Critical issue detected\342\200\235\n\342\200\234SLA approaching\342\200\235\n\342\200\234SLA breached\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Citizen reopened issue\342\200\235\n\342\200\234High-volume duplicate cluster detected\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Department backlog increased\342\200\235\n\nGroup:\nCritical\nWarnings\nInformational\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 12 \342\200\224 SETTINGS / ADMIN\n==================================================\n\nShow configurable options:\n\nIssue categories\nDepartment mappings\nWard mappings\nSLA rules\nPriority rules\nNotification settings\nLanguage support\nUser roles\n\nInclude roles:\n\nMunicipal Admin\nSupervisor\nDepartment Officer\nField Staff\nAnalyst\n\n==================================================\nIMPORTANT CROSS-SCREEN FEATURES\n==================================================\n\nImplement these behaviors in the frontend prototype:\n\n1. Clicking an issue on the map opens its details.\n\n2. Clicking \342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235 from a table opens detailed case management.\n\n3. Changing status updates the visible UI.\n\n4. Assigning an issue changes:\nUnassigned \342\206\222 Assigned.\n\n5. \342\200\234Start Work\342\200\235 changes:\nAssigned \342\206\222 In Progress.\n\n6. \342\200\234Mark Resolved\342\200\235 changes:\nIn Progress \342\206\222 Awaiting Citizen Verification.\n\n7. On the citizen side:\nConfirm \342\206\222 Closed.\n\n8. Reopen \342\206\222 Reopened.\n\n9. Filters should change displayed mock data.\n\n10. Search should filter issues.\n\n11. Dashboard KPIs should look internally consistent with the mock data.\n\n==================================================\nMOCK DATA\n==================================================\n\nUse realistic Indian civic data.\n\nCities/areas:\nChennai\nCoimbatore\nMadurai\nBengaluru\nHyderabad\nDelhi\nMumbai\n\nExample issue types:\nPothole\nGarbage accumulation\nBroken streetlight\nOverflowing drain\nDamaged footpath\nWater leakage\nOpen manhole\nIllegal dumping\n\nExample departments:\nRoads\nSanitation\nElectrical\nDrainage\nWater\nParks\n\nUse realistic ward numbers, street names, timestamps, issue IDs, report counts and SLA values.\n\n==================================================\nDESIGN PRINCIPLES\n==================================================\n\nCITIZEN SIDE:\n- Minimal cognitive load\n- Large touch-friendly buttons\n- Very little text\n- Simple language\n- Local language support visible\n- Camera-first interaction\n- Clear progress\n- Extremely clear status\n\nGOVERNMENT SIDE:\n- Information dense\n- Operational\n- Fast scanning\n- Tables + maps + KPIs\n- Strong filtering\n- Clear accountability\n- Clear priorities\n- Clear ownership\n- Clear SLA status\n\nMost importantly:\n\nTHE CITIZEN SHOULD FEEL:\n\342\200\234Reporting is easy and I can see what is happening.\342\200\235\n\nTHE MUNICIPAL OFFICER SHOULD FEEL:\n\342\200\234I can see everything, prioritize work, assign teams and track whether problems are actually being resolved.\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nKEY VISUAL STORY TO COMMUNICATE\n==================================================\n\nThe frontend should visibly demonstrate the platform\'s core innovation:\n\nMANY CITIZEN REPORTS\n        \342\206\223\nAI + LOCATION + TRUST\n        \342\206\223\nONE CANONICAL CIVIC ISSUE\n        \342\206\223\nPRIORITY\n        \342\206\223\nCORRECT DEPARTMENT\n        \342\206\223\nFIELD TEAM\n        \342\206\223\nRESOLUTION EVIDENCE\n        \342\206\223\nCITIZEN VERIFICATION\n        \342\206\223\nCITY ANALYTICS\n\nInclude this concept subtly in the government dashboard.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL QUALITY REQUIREMENTS\n==================================================\n\nThe entire frontend prototype must feel like one coherent product.\n\nDo not create disconnected pages with inconsistent layouts.\n\nUse:\n- Consistent spacing\n- Consistent card radius\n- Consistent table styles\n- Consistent badge styles\n- Consistent iconography\n- Consistent typography\n- Consistent navigation\n\nAll screens should use realistic content rather than placeholder lorem ipsum.\n\nThe prototype should be visually impressive enough for a hackathon demo while remaining credible as a real municipal product.\n\nMOST IMPORTANT:\nThe citizen experience must be SIMPLE.\nThe government experience must be DETAILED.\nThe connection between them must be obvious.\n\nThe prototype should make the judges immediately understand:\n\342\200\234Citizen reports \342\206\222 platform intelligence \342\206\222 municipal action \342\206\222 verified resolution.\342\200\235\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/assets/.aistudio/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: Create a polished FRONTEND-ONLY prototype for an Indian \342\200\234Crowd-Sourced Civic Issue Reporting & Resolution Platform\342\200\235.\n\nThe prototype has TWO completely different interfaces:\n\n1. CITIZEN / CUSTOMER APPLICATION\n2. GOVERNMENT / MUNICIPAL ADMINISTRATION DASHBOARD\n\nThe purpose of this prototype is to demonstrate the complete user experience and operational workflow to hackathon judges.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Frontend only.\n- Use realistic mock data.\n- No real backend required.\n- Simulate all interactions with local state/mock JSON.\n- Make the prototype fully navigable.\n- Buttons should visibly work where possible.\n- Use realistic Indian civic examples.\n- Do not make it look like a generic CRM.\n- Do not overload the citizen interface.\n- Make the government interface information-dense and operational.\n- Maintain a clean, professional, modern civic-tech aesthetic.\n- Use consistent spacing, alignment, typography, cards, borders and component sizing.\n- Desktop-first for the government dashboard.\n- Responsive mobile-first design for the citizen application.\n- Use a professional light theme with subtle civic/technology styling.\n- Avoid excessive gradients, glassmorphism, neon colors, giant illustrations, or unnecessary decorative elements.\n\n==================================================\nGLOBAL PRODUCT IDENTITY\n==================================================\n\nProduct name:\n\n\342\200\234CivicPulse\342\200\235\n\nTagline:\n\n\342\200\234Report. Resolve. Verify.\342\200\235\n\nUse a simple professional logo/icon suggesting:\nLocation + civic infrastructure + community.\n\nPrimary design language:\n- Clean\n- Trustworthy\n- Government-grade\n- Accessible\n- Modern\n- Data-driven\n\nUse a restrained color system:\n- Dark navy / charcoal for primary text\n- White / very light grey backgrounds\n- One strong accent color for primary actions\n- Red/orange for urgent issues\n- Green for resolved/verified\n- Amber for pending/warning\n- Grey for neutral states\n\nTypography:\nUse a highly legible modern sans-serif such as Inter.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 CITIZEN APPLICATION\n==================================================\n\nThe citizen side must feel extremely simple.\n\nThe core principle is:\n\n\342\200\234Anyone should be able to report a civic problem in less than one minute.\342\200\235\n\nCreate these screens:\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 1 \342\200\224 CITIZEN HOME DASHBOARD\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nHeader:\n- CivicPulse logo\n- Current city/area\n- Notification icon\n- Profile icon\n\nMain hero section:\n\n\342\200\234See a civic problem?\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Report it in a few seconds.\342\200\235\n\nLarge primary CTA:\n\n\342\200\234+ Report an Issue\342\200\235\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\n\342\200\234Track My Reports\342\200\235\n\nBelow that, show:\n\n\342\200\234Recent Issues Near You\342\200\235\n\nSmall cards showing:\n- Issue photo\n- Issue type\n- Location\n- Status\n- Date\n\nExample:\n\342\200\234Large pothole near bus stop\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Anna Nagar\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Assigned\342\200\235\n\342\200\2342 hours ago\342\200\235\n\nAlso show a compact summary:\n\nMy Reports\n- 7 Total\n- 4 Resolved\n- 2 In Progress\n- 1 Reopened\n\nBottom mobile navigation:\n- Home\n- Report\n- My Reports\n- Notifications\n- Profile\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 2 \342\200\224 REPORT ISSUE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDesign this as a very simple step-by-step flow.\n\nSTEP 1:\n\342\200\234Capture the problem\342\200\235\n\nLarge camera/upload component.\n\nButtons:\n\342\200\234Take Photo\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Upload Photo\342\200\235\n\nShow image preview after selection.\n\nSTEP 2:\n\342\200\234Where is it?\342\200\235\n\nShow:\n- Automatically detected location\n- Small map\n- Address\n- \342\200\234Adjust location\342\200\235 button\n\nExample:\n\342\200\23412, Anna Nagar Main Road\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Location detected automatically\342\200\235\n\nSTEP 3:\n\342\200\234What happened?\342\200\235\n\nLarge simple text/voice input.\n\nPlaceholder:\n\342\200\234Describe the problem in your own words\342\200\246\342\200\235\n\nButtons:\n- Type\n- \360\237\216\244 Record Voice\n\nLanguage selector:\nEnglish\n\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\nOther Indian languages\n\nSTEP 4:\nAI ASSIST\n\nDisplay a small non-intrusive panel:\n\n\342\200\234We think this is:\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Pothole\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Confidence: 96%\342\200\235\n\nAllow:\n\342\200\234Correct category\342\200\235\n\nShow detected category options if changed.\n\nSTEP 5:\nSUBMIT\n\nLarge CTA:\n\342\200\234Submit Report\342\200\235\n\nAfter submission show:\n\n\342\200\234Report Submitted\342\200\235\n\nIssue ID:\n\342\200\234CIV-10482\342\200\235\n\nMessage:\n\342\200\234We\342\200\231ve received your report. We\342\200\231ll keep you updated.\342\200\235\n\nImportant:\nShow a simple progress timeline.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 3 \342\200\224 OFFLINE REPORTING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nDemonstrate offline capability in the frontend.\n\nA small banner:\n\n\342\200\234Offline mode\342\200\235\n\342\200\234No internet connection\342\200\235\n\nAllow user to continue creating a report.\n\nAfter submission:\n\n\342\200\234Saved on your device\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Your report will automatically sync when connectivity returns.\342\200\235\n\nShow:\n\342\200\2342 reports waiting to sync\342\200\235\n\nThis feature should be visually clear because it is an important requirement.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 4 \342\200\224 MY REPORTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nList the citizen\342\200\231s submitted issues.\n\nEach card should show:\n\nIssue image\nIssue ID\nIssue type\nLocation\nDate\nStatus\n\nStatus examples:\n- Submitted\n- Under Review\n- Assigned\n- In Progress\n- Resolved\n- Awaiting Verification\n- Reopened\n\nAdd filters:\nAll\nActive\nResolved\nReopened\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 5 \342\200\224 ISSUE DETAILS / TRACKING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThis is an important screen.\n\nShow:\n\nIssue #CIV-10482\n\nLarge issue image.\n\nDetails:\nType:\nPothole\n\nLocation:\nAnna Nagar Main Road\n\nReported:\n27 Aug 2026, 10:14 AM\n\nPriority:\nHigh\n\nReports supporting this issue:\n43 citizens\n\nThen show a clean vertical timeline:\n\n\342\234\223 Report submitted\n\342\234\223 AI analysis completed\n\342\234\223 Issue verified\n\342\234\223 Assigned to Roads Department\n\342\234\223 Field team assigned\n\342\234\223 Repair started\n\342\234\223 Marked resolved\n\342\206\222 Awaiting your verification\n\nEach event should have:\n- Timestamp\n- Status\n- Short description\n\nAt the bottom:\n\n\342\200\234Has this issue been resolved?\342\200\235\n\nTwo large buttons:\n\n\342\200\234\342\234\223 Confirm Resolution\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234\342\234\225 Not Resolved \342\200\224 Reopen\342\200\235\n\nIf reopened, simulate:\n\342\200\234Issue reopened and returned to Roads Department.\342\200\235\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 6 \342\200\224 RESOLUTION VERIFICATION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nWhen an issue is marked resolved:\n\nShow:\n\n\342\200\234Is the problem actually fixed?\342\200\235\n\nBefore photo\nvs\nAfter photo\n\nShow resolution evidence:\n- Completion date\n- Department\n- Field team\n- Location confirmation\n\nButtons:\n\342\200\234Confirm Resolution\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Reopen Issue\342\200\235\n\nThis should visually communicate that government cannot simply mark an issue closed without citizen verification.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 7 \342\200\224 NOTIFICATIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a clean notification center.\n\nExamples:\n\n\342\200\234Your issue CIV-10482 was assigned to the Roads Department.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Repair work has started.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Issue CIV-10482 has been marked resolved. Please verify.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Issue CIV-10482 has been reopened.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Critical road hazard reported near your area.\342\200\235\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSCREEN 8 \342\200\224 CITIZEN PROFILE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSimple profile page.\n\nShow:\n- Name\n- Preferred language\n- Saved area\n- Reports submitted\n- Issues confirmed\n- Issues reopened\n\nOptional:\n\342\200\234Community contribution\342\200\235\n\nExample:\n\342\200\23427 civic reports submitted\342\200\235\n\342\200\23491% verified\342\200\235\n\nKeep this lightweight.\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 GOVERNMENT / MUNICIPAL DASHBOARD\n==================================================\n\nThis must be COMPLETELY different from the citizen UI.\n\nIt should look like a professional municipal command center.\n\nUse:\n- Desktop-first layout\n- Fixed left sidebar\n- Top header\n- Dense but readable data\n- Tables\n- Filters\n- KPI cards\n- GIS map\n- Charts\n- Issue queues\n- Detailed records\n\nSidebar navigation:\n\n1. Overview\n2. Live Issue Map\n3. Issue Queue\n4. Departments\n5. Field Operations\n6. SLA & Escalations\n7. Citizen Reports\n8. Analytics\n9. Recurring Hotspots\n10. Settings\n\nTop bar:\n- Municipality name\n- Search\n- Notifications\n- User profile\n- Date/time\n- Current operational status\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 1 \342\200\224 GOVERNMENT OVERVIEW\n==================================================\n\nHeader:\n\342\200\234Municipal Operations Overview\342\200\235\n\nTop KPI cards:\n\nTotal Open Issues\n2,481\n\nCritical\n86\n\nHigh Priority\n413\n\nIn Progress\n724\n\nResolved Today\n183\n\nSLA Breaches\n32\n\nAverage Resolution Time\n18.4 hrs\n\nCitizen Verification Rate\n87%\n\nBelow KPIs:\n\nLEFT:\nLive civic issue map.\n\nMap markers:\n- Red = Critical\n- Orange = High\n- Yellow = Medium\n- Green = Resolved\n\nShow clustered issue markers.\n\nRIGHT:\n\342\200\234Priority Queue\342\200\235\n\nTop 8 issues requiring attention.\n\nEach row:\nIssue ID\nType\nWard\nPriority\nReports\nAge\nDepartment\nSLA\n\nExample:\nCIV-10482 | Open Manhole | Ward 37 | Critical | 43 | 2h | Roads | 1h 12m remaining\n\nBelow:\nDepartment performance cards:\nRoads\nSanitation\nElectrical\nDrainage\nWater\n\nEach showing:\nOpen\nIn Progress\nResolved\nSLA compliance\n\nBottom:\n\342\200\234Recurring Problem Hotspots\342\200\235\n\nShow a small bar/heatmap-style visualization.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 2 \342\200\224 LIVE ISSUE MAP\n==================================================\n\nMake the map the main focus.\n\nLeft filter panel:\n- Issue type\n- Priority\n- Status\n- Department\n- Ward\n- Date range\n- Verification state\n\nMap:\nFull city/municipality map.\n\nMarkers should be clickable.\n\nClicking a marker opens:\n\nIssue #CIV-10482\nPothole\nCritical\n43 reports\nWard 37\nRoads Department\nSLA: 1h 12m\n\nButtons:\n\342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Assign\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Escalate\342\200\235\n\nShow clustering for nearby duplicate reports.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 3 \342\200\224 ISSUE QUEUE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a detailed operational table.\n\nColumns:\n\nPriority\nIssue ID\nIssue Type\nLocation\nWard\nReports\nConfidence\nDepartment\nAssigned Team\nAge\nSLA\nStatus\nActions\n\nExample rows:\n\nCRITICAL | CIV-10482 | Open Manhole | Ward 37 | 43 reports | 98% | Roads | Team B | 2h | 1h remaining | Assigned\n\nHIGH | CIV-10473 | Garbage | Ward 12 | 27 reports | 94% | Sanitation | Team A | 5h | 3h remaining | In Progress\n\nUse strong visual status chips.\n\nProvide:\n- Search\n- Sort\n- Filter\n- Bulk assignment\n- Export\n- Pagination\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 4 \342\200\224 ISSUE DETAIL / CASE MANAGEMENT\n==================================================\n\nThis should be the most detailed government screen.\n\nHeader:\n\n\342\200\234Civic Issue #CIV-10482\342\200\235\n\nStatus:\nCRITICAL\nASSIGNED\n\nMain layout:\n\nLEFT COLUMN:\nEvidence\n\nCitizen photos\nLocation map\nBefore photo\nAfter photo\n\nMIDDLE COLUMN:\nIssue intelligence\n\nIssue type:\nOpen Manhole\n\nAI confidence:\n97%\n\nDuplicate cluster:\n13 reports\n\nSpam risk:\nLow\n\nPriority score:\n96/100\n\nJurisdiction:\nWard 37\n\nResponsible authority:\nMunicipal Corporation\n\nDepartment:\nRoads\n\nNearby risk:\nSchool \342\200\224 120m\n\nRIGHT COLUMN:\nWorkflow\n\nCurrent owner:\nRoad Maintenance Team B\n\nSupervisor:\nOfficer Name\n\nSLA:\n1h 12m remaining\n\nAssignment:\n27 Aug 2026, 10:42 AM\n\nButtons:\nAssign\nReassign\nEscalate\nStart Work\nMark Resolved\n\nBelow all columns:\n\nTIMELINE\n\nShow the entire issue history.\n\nThen:\n\nCITIZEN REPORT CLUSTER\n\n\342\200\23443 citizen reports consolidated into this issue\342\200\235\n\nShow a list/map of supporting reports.\n\nThis screen should strongly communicate:\n\342\200\234Many reports \342\206\222 One physical issue.\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 5 \342\200\224 DEPARTMENT MANAGEMENT\n==================================================\n\nShow department cards:\n\nRoads\nSanitation\nElectrical\nDrainage\nWater\nParks\n\nEach card:\nOpen issues\nCritical\nAssigned\nOverdue\nResolved today\nSLA %\n\nClicking department opens its work queue.\n\nExample:\n\n\342\200\234Roads Department\342\200\235\n\nOpen:\n482\n\nCritical:\n31\n\nHigh:\n97\n\nOverdue:\n18\n\nAverage resolution:\n14.2 hrs\n\nBelow:\nAssigned teams and workload.\n\nExample:\n\nTeam A\n8 active\n2 critical\n\nTeam B\n12 active\n1 critical\n\nTeam C\n4 active\n\nUse workload visualization.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 6 \342\200\224 FIELD OPERATIONS\n==================================================\n\nShow field teams.\n\nFor each team:\n\nTeam name\nCurrent location\nActive jobs\nPriority jobs\nCompleted today\nCurrent assignment\n\nExample:\n\n\342\200\234Road Maintenance Team B\342\200\235\n\nActive:\n4\n\nCurrent:\nCIV-10482\n\nDistance:\n1.2 km\n\nETA:\n8 min\n\nButtons:\n\342\200\234View Route\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Open Assignment\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 7 \342\200\224 SLA & ESCALATIONS\n==================================================\n\nShow:\n\nSLA compliance:\n87%\n\nIssues approaching breach\nIssues already breached\nAverage response time\nAverage resolution time\n\nCreate a timeline/table:\n\nIssue\nDepartment\nAssigned\nSLA\nTime remaining\nEscalation level\n\nUse visual warning indicators.\n\nExample:\n\nCIV-10473\nSanitation\nSLA breached\n2h 41m overdue\nSupervisor escalation\n\nAllow:\nEscalate\nReassign\nExtend with reason\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 8 \342\200\224 CITIZEN REPORT MANAGEMENT\n==================================================\n\nShow raw incoming reports before/while they are processed.\n\nEach report:\n\nPhoto\nDescription\nLocation\nLanguage\nAI category\nAI confidence\nTrust score\nDuplicate probability\nSpam probability\n\nExample:\n\nReport #R10983\n\nLanguage:\nTamil\n\nAI category:\nPothole \342\200\224 94%\n\nDuplicate probability:\n91%\n\nTrust score:\n87%\n\nAction:\n\342\200\234Merge with CIV-10482\342\200\235\n\nAlso show states:\n\nLegitimate\nNeeds Review\nSpam\nDuplicate\n\nThis demonstrates how the platform reduces municipal workload.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 9 \342\200\224 ANALYTICS\n==================================================\n\nCreate an advanced analytics dashboard.\n\nSections:\n\nCITY OVERVIEW\n- Total reports\n- Unique issues\n- Resolution rate\n- Reopen rate\n- Average response time\n- Average resolution time\n\nISSUE DISTRIBUTION\nBar chart:\nPotholes\nGarbage\nStreetlights\nDrainage\nFootpaths\n\nDEPARTMENT PERFORMANCE\nCompare departments by:\n- Response time\n- Resolution time\n- SLA compliance\n- Backlog\n\nTREND ANALYSIS\nShow issue counts over time.\n\nRECURRING HOTSPOTS\nShow top locations with repeated problems.\n\nExample:\n\n\342\200\234Ward 37\342\200\235\nPotholes:\n2024 \342\200\224 18\n2025 \342\200\224 31\n2026 \342\200\224 47\n\nFlag:\n\342\200\234Recurring infrastructure problem\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 10 \342\200\224 RECURRING HOTSPOTS\n==================================================\n\nMain purpose:\nIdentify locations that repeatedly experience civic failures.\n\nShow:\n\nLocation\nIssue type\nReports over time\nNumber of repairs\nNumber of reopenings\nLast repair\nRisk level\n\nExample:\n\nRoad X\n\nPotholes:\n96\n\nRepairs:\n7\n\nReopened:\n4\n\nTrend:\nIncreasing\n\nStatus:\n\342\200\234Investigate recurring infrastructure failure\342\200\235\n\nAdd a map with hotspot intensity.\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 11 \342\200\224 NOTIFICATIONS / ALERT CENTER\n==================================================\n\nMunicipal alerts:\n\n\342\200\234Critical issue detected\342\200\235\n\342\200\234SLA approaching\342\200\235\n\342\200\234SLA breached\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Citizen reopened issue\342\200\235\n\342\200\234High-volume duplicate cluster detected\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Department backlog increased\342\200\235\n\nGroup:\nCritical\nWarnings\nInformational\n\n==================================================\nSCREEN 12 \342\200\224 SETTINGS / ADMIN\n==================================================\n\nShow configurable options:\n\nIssue categories\nDepartment mappings\nWard mappings\nSLA rules\nPriority rules\nNotification settings\nLanguage support\nUser roles\n\nInclude roles:\n\nMunicipal Admin\nSupervisor\nDepartment Officer\nField Staff\nAnalyst\n\n==================================================\nIMPORTANT CROSS-SCREEN FEATURES\n==================================================\n\nImplement these behaviors in the frontend prototype:\n\n1. Clicking an issue on the map opens its details.\n\n2. Clicking \342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235 from a table opens detailed case management.\n\n3. Changing status updates the visible UI.\n\n4. Assigning an issue changes:\nUnassigned \342\206\222 Assigned.\n\n5. \342\200\234Start Work\342\200\235 changes:\nAssigned \342\206\222 In Progress.\n\n6. \342\200\234Mark Resolved\342\200\235 changes:\nIn Progress \342\206\222 Awaiting Citizen Verification.\n\n7. On the citizen side:\nConfirm \342\206\222 Closed.\n\n8. Reopen \342\206\222 Reopened.\n\n9. Filters should change displayed mock data.\n\n10. Search should filter issues.\n\n11. Dashboard KPIs should look internally consistent with the mock data.\n\n==================================================\nMOCK DATA\n==================================================\n\nUse realistic Indian civic data.\n\nCities/areas:\nChennai\nCoimbatore\nMadurai\nBengaluru\nHyderabad\nDelhi\nMumbai\n\nExample issue types:\nPothole\nGarbage accumulation\nBroken streetlight\nOverflowing drain\nDamaged footpath\nWater leakage\nOpen manhole\nIllegal dumping\n\nExample departments:\nRoads\nSanitation\nElectrical\nDrainage\nWater\nParks\n\nUse realistic ward numbers, street names, timestamps, issue IDs, report counts and SLA values.\n\n==================================================\nDESIGN PRINCIPLES\n==================================================\n\nCITIZEN SIDE:\n- Minimal cognitive load\n- Large touch-friendly buttons\n- Very little text\n- Simple language\n- Local language support visible\n- Camera-first interaction\n- Clear progress\n- Extremely clear status\n\nGOVERNMENT SIDE:\n- Information dense\n- Operational\n- Fast scanning\n- Tables + maps + KPIs\n- Strong filtering\n- Clear accountability\n- Clear priorities\n- Clear ownership\n- Clear SLA status\n\nMost importantly:\n\nTHE CITIZEN SHOULD FEEL:\n\342\200\234Reporting is easy and I can see what is happening.\342\200\235\n\nTHE MUNICIPAL OFFICER SHOULD FEEL:\n\342\200\234I can see everything, prioritize work, assign teams and track whether problems are actually being resolved.\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nKEY VISUAL STORY TO COMMUNICATE\n==================================================\n\nThe frontend should visibly demonstrate the platform\'s core innovation:\n\nMANY CITIZEN REPORTS\n        \342\206\223\nAI + LOCATION + TRUST\n        \342\206\223\nONE CANONICAL CIVIC ISSUE\n        \342\206\223\nPRIORITY\n        \342\206\223\nCORRECT DEPARTMENT\n        \342\206\223\nFIELD TEAM\n        \342\206\223\nRESOLUTION EVIDENCE\n        \342\206\223\nCITIZEN VERIFICATION\n        \342\206\223\nCITY ANALYTICS\n\nInclude this concept subtly in the government dashboard.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL QUALITY REQUIREMENTS\n==================================================\n\nThe entire frontend prototype must feel like one coherent product.\n\nDo not create disconnected pages with inconsistent layouts.\n\nUse:\n- Consistent spacing\n- Consistent card radius\n- Consistent table styles\n- Consistent badge styles\n- Consistent iconography\n- Consistent typography\n- Consistent navigation\n\nAll screens should use realistic content rather than placeholder lorem ipsum.\n\nThe prototype should be visually impressive enough for a hackathon demo while remaining credible as a real municipal product.\n\nMOST IMPORTANT:\nThe citizen experience must be SIMPLE.\nThe government experience must be DETAILED.\nThe connection between them must be obvious.\n\nThe prototype should make the judges immediately understand:\n\342\200\234Citizen reports \342\206\222 platform intelligence \342\206\222 municipal action \342\206\222 verified resolution.\342\200\235\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/assets/.aistudio/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
  }
}
