  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented the complete end-to-end simulated workflow in the frontend code. The prototype is now a connected system that relies purely on local state (`AppContext`), allowing you to demonstrate the exact journey step-by-step. \n\n### **How to Demonstrate the Flow:**\n\n1. **Start as Citizen (Report Creation):**\n   * Go to the Citizen App and click the central **\"Report\"** (+) button in the bottom navigation.\n   * **Step 1:** Tap \"Take Photo\" (simulates capturing the pothole).\n   * **Step 2:** Tap \"Confirm Location\" (simulates GPS detection at Ward 37).\n   * **Step 3:** Enter a description or leave it blank to rely on the AI. Notice the **AI Assist** panel classifying the image as \"Pothole\" with 96% confidence.\n   * **Step 4:** Click **\"Submit Report\"**. The system processes it and generates a unique `CIV-XXXXX` ID.\n   * *Behind the scenes:* The mocked system instantly updates the issue context: it merges it as 43 canonical reports (42 existing + 1), sets the Priority to **HIGH**, assigns it to the **Roads Department**, and tags it to **Ward 37**.\n\n2. **Switch to Government View (Assignment & Resolution):**\n   * Switch the role to Government and open the **\"Citizen Queue\"**. The newly generated issue will be sitting at the top of the queue with its unique ID.\n   * Click **\"View Details\"** on the issue.\n   * Observe the \"Duplicate Cluster\" block showing that 43 reports were merged automatically by the system.\n   * **Action 1:** Click **\"Assign to Field Team B\"**. (Notice the Current Owner dynamically updates).\n   * **Action 2:** Click **\"Mark as In Progress\"**.\n   * **Action 3:** Click **\"Upload After-Photo & Submit\"**. This mocks the field team taking the final photo, attaches it to the issue context, and changes the status to **\"Awaiting Verification\"**. \n\n3. **Switch Back to Citizen View (Verification):**\n   * In the Citizen app, notice a **Red Notification Dot** appears on the top right bell icon and the bottom navigation \"Alerts\" tab.\n   * Go to **Alerts/Notifications** and click the new \"Action Required\" notification.\n   * This immediately opens the simulated **Issue Detail** page.\n   * A verification dialog asks the citizen to compare the **Before** and **After** photos (with the after-photo dynamically populated by the Gov action).\n   * Click **\"Confirm Resolution\"**. The issue status becomes **Closed**.\n\n4. **Switch to Government View (Analytics Impact):**\n   * Open the **\"Analytics\"** dashboard.\n   * **Department Workload:** The \"Roads\" department resolved count has dynamically incremented by 1.\n   * **Volume Trends:** The June report count has incremented by 1 (the new issue submitted).\n   * **Hotspots (Scroll down):** The Ward 37 (Anna Nagar) high-priority zone counter has actively dynamically incremented to account for the new issue, confirming that the single submission immediately updates city-wide metrics. \n\nEvery button you need for this presentation flow is wired strictly to the front-end context without dead ends. Good luck with the functional demonstration! Let me know if you need any adjustments to the simulation timing or data."
    thinking: "**Confirming Success and Details**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the success of the initial prompt. I\'m now meticulously reviewing it to ensure that nothing was overlooked in the initial execution. So far, the AI is correctly identifying the submitted report as a pothole. Further investigation is needed for more robust use cases.\n\n\n**Refining Civic Issue Flow**\n\nI\'ve refined the civic issue flow. An ID is generated, and the system now correctly detects and merges similar reports into a single canonical issue. The priority is set to HIGH, with Ward 37 and correct routing to the Roads Department confirmed. The process also includes appropriate assignment to \"Unassigned\" initially, with the Government officer later assigning to \"Field Team B.\" The government officer can now see the issue, open it, assign a team, start work, upload an after-photo, and mark the issue as \"Awaiting Citizen Verification.\"\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have implemented the complete end-to-end simulated workflow in the frontend code. The prototype is now a connected system that relies purely on local state (`AppContext`), allowing you to demonstrate the exact journey step-by-step. \n\n### **How to Demonstrate the Flow:**\n\n1. **Start as Citizen (Report Creation):**\n   * Go to the Citizen App and click the central **\"Report\"** (+) button in the bottom navigation.\n   * **Step 1:** Tap \"Take Photo\" (simulates capturing the pothole).\n   * **Step 2:** Tap \"Confirm Location\" (simulates GPS detection at Ward 37).\n   * **Step 3:** Enter a description or leave it blank to rely on the AI. Notice the **AI Assist** panel classifying the image as \"Pothole\" with 96% confidence.\n   * **Step 4:** Click **\"Submit Report\"**. The system processes it and generates a unique `CIV-XXXXX` ID.\n   * *Behind the scenes:* The mocked system instantly updates the issue context: it merges it as 43 canonical reports (42 existing + 1), sets the Priority to **HIGH**, assigns it to the **Roads Department**, and tags it to **Ward 37**.\n\n2. **Switch to Government View (Assignment & Resolution):**\n   * Switch the role to Government and open the **\"Citizen Queue\"**. The newly generated issue will be sitting at the top of the queue with its unique ID.\n   * Click **\"View Details\"** on the issue.\n   * Observe the \"Duplicate Cluster\" block showing that 43 reports were merged automatically by the system.\n   * **Action 1:** Click **\"Assign to Field Team B\"**. (Notice the Current Owner dynamically updates).\n   * **Action 2:** Click **\"Mark as In Progress\"**.\n   * **Action 3:** Click **\"Upload After-Photo & Submit\"**. This mocks the field team taking the final photo, attaches it to the issue context, and changes the status to **\"Awaiting Verification\"**. \n\n3. **Switch Back to Citizen View (Verification):**\n   * In the Citizen app, notice a **Red Notification Dot** appears on the top right bell icon and the bottom navigation \"Alerts\" tab.\n   * Go to **Alerts/Notifications** and click the new \"Action Required\" notification.\n   * This immediately opens the simulated **Issue Detail** page.\n   * A verification dialog asks the citizen to compare the **Before** and **After** photos (with the after-photo dynamically populated by the Gov action).\n   * Click **\"Confirm Resolution\"**. The issue status becomes **Closed**.\n\n4. **Switch to Government View (Analytics Impact):**\n   * Open the **\"Analytics\"** dashboard.\n   * **Department Workload:** The \"Roads\" department resolved count has dynamically incremented by 1.\n   * **Volume Trends:** The June report count has incremented by 1 (the new issue submitted).\n   * **Hotspots (Scroll down):** The Ward 37 (Anna Nagar) high-priority zone counter has actively dynamically incremented to account for the new issue, confirming that the single submission immediately updates city-wide metrics. \n\nEvery button you need for this presentation flow is wired strictly to the front-end context without dead ends. Good luck with the functional demonstration! Let me know if you need any adjustments to the simulation timing or data."
