  planner_response {
    response: "I have strengthened the prototype\'s unique product differentiators by injecting highly visible, compact \"Intelligence\" panels into the existing UI. \n\nHere is exactly how the 7 core concepts are now visualized for the judges within a 3\342\200\2235 second scan:\n\n1. **REPORT \342\211\240 ISSUE (Canonical Merging)**\n   * **Gov Detail View:** Replaced the simple duplicate list with a **\"Canonical Issue Generation\"** panel. It explicitly states: *\"Report \342\211\240 Issue: The AI has analyzed photos and coordinates, consolidating 43 separate citizen reports into this single canonical task to prevent duplicate municipal dispatch.\"*\n   * **Citizen Detail View:** Added an \"AI Canonical Merge\" indicator badge at the top of the details card if the issue has multiple reports.\n\n2. **AI TRIAGE & 3. JURISDICTION INTELLIGENCE**\n   * **Gov Detail View:** Expanded \"Platform Intelligence\" to a full engine block.\n   * **Spam & Confidence:** Shows 96% AI Classification confidence and a 98% High Trust Verification Score.\n   * **Jurisdiction Flow:** Added a visual routing diagram: `[GPS] \342\206\222 [Ward 37] \342\206\222 [Roads Dept] \342\206\222 [Team B]`.\n   * **Citizen Flow:** Added a \"System Triage Preview\" during submission that tells the citizen: *\"Checking for duplicates... Will route to Roads Dept (Ward 37)\"*.\n\n4. **CAPACITY-AWARE PRIORITIZATION**\n   * **Gov Detail View:** Added a **\"Capacity-Aware Prioritization\"** factors block beneath the jurisdiction flow. It visually lists why the issue is high priority using compact tags: `\342\232\240\357\270\217 School Zone (120m)`, `\360\237\223\213 High Report Volume`, and `\342\217\261\357\270\217 Dept Load: 84%`.\n\n5. **EVIDENCE-BACKED RESOLUTION**\n   * **Gov Detail View:** Updated the \"Location Evidence\" column. Once the field team uploads the after-photo, it now immediately renders side-by-side with the Before photo for the government officer to review the physical evidence.\n\n6. **CITIZEN-VERIFIED CLOSURE**\n   * **Citizen Detail View:** When the notification is tapped, a highly visible \"Verify Resolution\" card anchors the screen. It forces the citizen to compare the Before/After photos and either click **\"Confirm Resolution\"** (closing it) or **\"Not Resolved \342\200\224 Reopen\"**.\n\n7. **RECURRING INFRASTRUCTURE INTELLIGENCE**\n   * **Analytics View:** Overhauled the Hotspots section into **\"Recurring Infrastructure Intelligence\"**.\n   * Instead of just showing numbers, Ward 37 now displays a critical **AI Recommendation: Preventive Road Resurfacing**. It explains in one sentence: *\"Pothole recurrence rate is 430% above city baseline. Structural intervention required.\"* (Ward 12 similarly recommends a Sewer Line Audit).\n\nThese additions are completely functional within the local simulated state and explicitly translate complex backend AI concepts into front-end visual proof for your demonstration."
