  planner_response {
    response: "I have overhauled the Government Dashboard specifically to support high-velocity municipal decision-making. The layout is now designed to be dense, actionable, and immediately informative.\n\nHere is an overview of the operational improvements:\n\n- **Command Center KPIs:** Replaced the generic metrics with actionable operational alerts. The dashboard now instantly flags **Critical/Unassigned** issues, **Reopened by Citizen** (escalations), and **SLA Breaching (<2h)** tickets.\n- **Department Workload Widget:** Added a live capacity tracker on the Overview page showing exactly what percentage of a department\'s capacity is utilized (e.g., Roads: 84%, Sanitation: 62%) alongside their active SLA alerts to guide bulk routing and escalation.\n- **Priority Issue Queue:** \n  - **SLA Countdowns:** The SLA Limit column now actively parses countdowns and flashes a red `Overdue` badge if a breach occurs.\n  - **Escalation Indicators:** Issues with a `Reopened` status now display a red **\"Citizen Escalated\"** warning icon directly in the status column.\n  - **Action Prompts:** Added a distinct blue `Action` button per row to immediately route the officer to the resolution workflow.\n- **Live Intelligence Map:** Implemented interactive map clustering. The map now plots raw priority densities (e.g., a pulsing red cluster of 42 critical issues) rather than individual pins, allowing officers to identify systemic hotspots like Ward 37 instantly.\n- **Evidence-Backed Workflow:** The Issue Detail page retains the side-by-side Before/After photo evidence block and explicit quick actions (`Assign to Field Team B`, `Mark as In Progress`, `Escalate Issue`) based directly on the issue\'s current local state.\n\nEvery operational component is fully hooked up to the simulated state for your demonstration. Let me know if you need any adjustments to the SLA formulas or assignment logic before presenting!"
    modified_response: "I have overhauled the Government Dashboard specifically to support high-velocity municipal decision-making. The layout is now designed to be dense, actionable, and immediately informative.\n\nHere is an overview of the operational improvements:\n\n- **Command Center KPIs:** Replaced the generic metrics with actionable operational alerts. The dashboard now instantly flags **Critical/Unassigned** issues, **Reopened by Citizen** (escalations), and **SLA Breaching (<2h)** tickets.\n- **Department Workload Widget:** Added a live capacity tracker on the Overview page showing exactly what percentage of a department\'s capacity is utilized (e.g., Roads: 84%, Sanitation: 62%) alongside their active SLA alerts to guide bulk routing and escalation.\n- **Priority Issue Queue:** \n  - **SLA Countdowns:** The SLA Limit column now actively parses countdowns and flashes a red `Overdue` badge if a breach occurs.\n  - **Escalation Indicators:** Issues with a `Reopened` status now display a red **\"Citizen Escalated\"** warning icon directly in the status column.\n  - **Action Prompts:** Added a distinct blue `Action` button per row to immediately route the officer to the resolution workflow.\n- **Live Intelligence Map:** Implemented interactive map clustering. The map now plots raw priority densities (e.g., a pulsing red cluster of 42 critical issues) rather than individual pins, allowing officers to identify systemic hotspots like Ward 37 instantly.\n- **Evidence-Backed Workflow:** The Issue Detail page retains the side-by-side Before/After photo evidence block and explicit quick actions (`Assign to Field Team B`, `Mark as In Progress`, `Escalate Issue`) based directly on the issue\'s current local state.\n\nEvery operational component is fully hooked up to the simulated state for your demonstration. Let me know if you need any adjustments to the SLA formulas or assignment logic before presenting!"
