  planner_response {
    response: "I have completely redesigned the Citizen Reporting Flow to ensure anyone, regardless of digital familiarity, can submit an issue in under a minute with minimal cognitive load. \n\nThe citizen-facing application now strictly prioritizes accessibility, large touch targets, and dead-simple language, while maintaining the sophisticated AI backend.\n\nHere is an overview of the optimized experience:\n\n- **Frictionless Entry**: The primary \"Report an Issue\" button on the citizen home screen has been significantly enlarged with generous padding to act as an unmissable call-to-action.\n- **Step 1: Visual First**: The flow starts immediately with \"What needs fixing?\", removing technical jargon. The \"Take Photo\" and \"Choose from Gallery\" buttons are now massive touch targets.\n- **Step 2: Effortless Location**: Instead of a complex map interface, the system simply states \"We found you using GPS\" and shows the auto-detected location. The citizen just taps a massive \"Yes, this is correct\" button to proceed. \n- **Step 3: Multi-Modal Input**: \n  - **Language Support**: Added highly visible language toggle buttons for English, \340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215 (Tamil), and \340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200 (Hindi).\n  - **Voice Input**: A prominent red microphone button floats directly on the text area for citizens who prefer speaking to typing. \n  - **Plain-English AI**: The complex AI Triage panel was removed. It is replaced by a simple, friendly confirmation: *\"\342\234\250 AI sees a Pothole. We will route this directly to the Roads team.\"*\n- **Offline Resilience**: If the user submits while offline, the success screen plainly states \"Saved Offline: We will send this automatically when you have internet,\" removing technical anxiety about data loss. \n\nThe entire flow is strictly linear (Photo \342\206\222 Location \342\206\222 Details \342\206\222 Submit) and avoids overwhelming the citizen with the administrative details that exist on the Government side."
    modified_response: "I have completely redesigned the Citizen Reporting Flow to ensure anyone, regardless of digital familiarity, can submit an issue in under a minute with minimal cognitive load. \n\nThe citizen-facing application now strictly prioritizes accessibility, large touch targets, and dead-simple language, while maintaining the sophisticated AI backend.\n\nHere is an overview of the optimized experience:\n\n- **Frictionless Entry**: The primary \"Report an Issue\" button on the citizen home screen has been significantly enlarged with generous padding to act as an unmissable call-to-action.\n- **Step 1: Visual First**: The flow starts immediately with \"What needs fixing?\", removing technical jargon. The \"Take Photo\" and \"Choose from Gallery\" buttons are now massive touch targets.\n- **Step 2: Effortless Location**: Instead of a complex map interface, the system simply states \"We found you using GPS\" and shows the auto-detected location. The citizen just taps a massive \"Yes, this is correct\" button to proceed. \n- **Step 3: Multi-Modal Input**: \n  - **Language Support**: Added highly visible language toggle buttons for English, \340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215 (Tamil), and \340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200 (Hindi).\n  - **Voice Input**: A prominent red microphone button floats directly on the text area for citizens who prefer speaking to typing. \n  - **Plain-English AI**: The complex AI Triage panel was removed. It is replaced by a simple, friendly confirmation: *\"\342\234\250 AI sees a Pothole. We will route this directly to the Roads team.\"*\n- **Offline Resilience**: If the user submits while offline, the success screen plainly states \"Saved Offline: We will send this automatically when you have internet,\" removing technical anxiety about data loss. \n\nThe entire flow is strictly linear (Photo \342\206\222 Location \342\206\222 Details \342\206\222 Submit) and avoids overwhelming the citizen with the administrative details that exist on the Government side."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
