  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the final audit and tightened up the demonstration story. \n\nThe application is now entirely focused on three highly specific flagship issues that clearly illustrate the product\'s value proposition without distracting boilerplate data.\n\nHere is how the data perfectly supports your hackathon presentation story:\n\n**1. The Canonical AI Merge (CIV-10482: Large Pothole)**\n- **Story:** \"Multiple people reported this, but our AI merged 42 duplicate reports into a single, high-priority canonical task for the Roads department.\"\n- **Data Support:** This issue sits at `Critical` priority with `43 reports` and `98%` AI confidence. If you open it in the government dashboard, you will see the full \"Canonical Issue Generation\" intelligence block explaining exactly how it deduplicated the reports.\n\n**2. The Citizen Verification Loop (CIV-10501: Open Manhole)**\n- **Story:** \"A contractor might say the work is done, but the citizen has the final say. If the citizen marks it as unresolved, it gets escalated and reopened immediately, breaking the SLA.\"\n- **Data Support:** This issue is positioned near a school (boosting its priority) and sits in a `Reopened` status. On the citizen side, you can show the Verification UI where the citizen rejected the \"fix\". On the government side, it is flagged as `Citizen Escalated` with an actively breached SLA of `-2h 10m`.\n\n**3. The Automated Triage (CIV-10512: Overflowing Sewage)**\n- **Story:** \"As soon as a new report comes in, AI classifies it, evaluates the photo, and queues it up for the exact right department to take action.\"\n- **Data Support:** This is a brand new, `Unassigned` issue sitting in the queue waiting for someone to hit the blue \"Action\" button and assign it to a field team.\n\nI also fixed the image layout in the Citizen Issue Detail view so that if an issue has an \"After\" photo, both photos are displayed side-by-side with clear \"Before\" and \"After\" labels, allowing you to easily demonstrate the evidence loop.\n\nThe application looks like a real, polished civic tech product. Good luck with your hackathon presentation!"
    modified_response: "I have completed the final audit and tightened up the demonstration story. \n\nThe application is now entirely focused on three highly specific flagship issues that clearly illustrate the product\'s value proposition without distracting boilerplate data.\n\nHere is how the data perfectly supports your hackathon presentation story:\n\n**1. The Canonical AI Merge (CIV-10482: Large Pothole)**\n- **Story:** \"Multiple people reported this, but our AI merged 42 duplicate reports into a single, high-priority canonical task for the Roads department.\"\n- **Data Support:** This issue sits at `Critical` priority with `43 reports` and `98%` AI confidence. If you open it in the government dashboard, you will see the full \"Canonical Issue Generation\" intelligence block explaining exactly how it deduplicated the reports.\n\n**2. The Citizen Verification Loop (CIV-10501: Open Manhole)**\n- **Story:** \"A contractor might say the work is done, but the citizen has the final say. If the citizen marks it as unresolved, it gets escalated and reopened immediately, breaking the SLA.\"\n- **Data Support:** This issue is positioned near a school (boosting its priority) and sits in a `Reopened` status. On the citizen side, you can show the Verification UI where the citizen rejected the \"fix\". On the government side, it is flagged as `Citizen Escalated` with an actively breached SLA of `-2h 10m`.\n\n**3. The Automated Triage (CIV-10512: Overflowing Sewage)**\n- **Story:** \"As soon as a new report comes in, AI classifies it, evaluates the photo, and queues it up for the exact right department to take action.\"\n- **Data Support:** This is a brand new, `Unassigned` issue sitting in the queue waiting for someone to hit the blue \"Action\" button and assign it to a field team.\n\nI also fixed the image layout in the Citizen Issue Detail view so that if an issue has an \"After\" photo, both photos are displayed side-by-side with clear \"Before\" and \"After\" labels, allowing you to easily demonstrate the evidence loop.\n\nThe application looks like a real, polished civic tech product. Good luck with your hackathon presentation!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
