steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787826983
      nanos: 352993054
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Now add a complete AUTHENTICATION AND USER ACCOUNT LAYER to the existing CivicPulse prototype.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not redesign or remove the existing citizen and government dashboards.\n- Preserve the current visual identity, layouts, spacing and navigation.\n- Add authentication as a new foundational layer around the existing application.\n- This is a FRONTEND-ONLY HACKATHON PROTOTYPE, so simulate Aadhaar verification using mock data and local state.\n- Do NOT implement real Aadhaar authentication or collect/store real Aadhaar numbers.\n- Make it visually clear that the prototype represents \342\200\234Aadhaar-verified identity\342\200\235.\n- The architecture should be designed so a real authorized Aadhaar verification provider could be integrated later.\n\n==================================================\n1. AUTHENTICATION MODEL\n==================================================\n\nEvery citizen must have ONE permanent account.\n\nThe intended experience is:\n\nFIRST TIME:\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Create Account\n\342\206\222 Aadhaar Verification\n\342\206\222 Account Created\n\342\206\222 Stay signed in\n\nRETURNING USER:\nOpen application\n\342\206\222 Automatically recognized\n\342\206\222 No repeated login\n\342\206\222 Directly enters the application\n\nThe user should NOT see a login screen every time they open the app.\n\nUse persistent frontend session state to simulate this behavior.\n\nShow:\n\342\200\234Welcome back, [Name]\342\200\235\n\nand a persistent profile/avatar in the top corner.\n\n==================================================\n2. CITIZEN SIGN-UP / ONBOARDING\n==================================================\n\nCreate a new first-time-user onboarding flow.\n\nSCREEN:\n\342\200\234Create your CivicPulse Account\342\200\235\n\nExplain:\n\n\342\200\234Your account helps us prevent duplicate and fraudulent reports and lets you track issues from report to resolution.\342\200\235\n\nStep 1:\nMobile Number\n\nField:\n+91 __________\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Continue\342\200\235\n\nStep 2:\nOTP Verification\n\nShow:\n\342\200\234OTP sent to your registered mobile number\342\200\235\n\nInput:\n6-digit OTP\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Verify Mobile\342\200\235\n\nFor the prototype, accept a mock OTP.\n\nStep 3:\nAadhaar Verification\n\nHeading:\n\342\200\234Verify your identity\342\200\235\n\nDescription:\n\342\200\234Use Aadhaar-based identity verification to create your CivicPulse account.\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT ask the user to upload or store a real Aadhaar card in the prototype.\n\nInstead provide a clearly labelled DEMO verification interface:\n\n\342\200\234Aadhaar Verification \342\200\224 Demo\342\200\235\n\nFields:\nMasked Aadhaar:\nXXXX XXXX 1234\n\nOTP:\n6-digit OTP\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Verify Identity\342\200\235\n\nAfter verification show:\n\n\342\234\223 Identity Verified\n\n\342\200\234Your CivicPulse account is now verified.\342\200\235\n\nInclude a small privacy message:\n\n\342\200\234Your Aadhaar number is not displayed publicly. The prototype stores only a verified-account state and non-sensitive profile information.\342\200\235\n\nDo not expose full Aadhaar numbers anywhere.\n\n==================================================\n3. ACCOUNT CREATION\n==================================================\n\nAfter successful verification:\n\nCreate a mock citizen profile:\n\nName:\nArun Kumar\n\nPhone:\n+91 XXXXX XXXXX\n\nIdentity:\n\342\200\234Aadhaar Verified\342\200\235\n\nVerification badge:\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nPreferred language:\nEnglish\n\nLocation:\nUser\'s selected area\n\nShow:\n\n\342\200\234Account created successfully.\342\200\235\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Continue to CivicPulse\342\200\235\n\nThen open the Citizen Home Dashboard.\n\n==================================================\n4. PERSISTENT SIGN-IN\n==================================================\n\nThis is CRITICAL.\n\nOnce the citizen has completed account creation and verification:\n\n- Store mock authenticated state in localStorage/session persistence.\n- On reopening or refreshing the prototype, automatically recognize the user.\n- Do NOT show login again.\n- Go directly to the Citizen Home Dashboard.\n\nSimulate:\n\nlocalStorage:\ncivicpulse_authenticated = true\ncivicpulse_user = { ...mock profile... }\n\nThe user should experience this as:\n\n\342\200\234One-time account creation \342\206\222 permanent signed-in experience.\342\200\235\n\nAlso show a small profile/avatar in the top-right corner of the application.\n\nExample:\n\n[AR]\nArun Kumar\n\342\234\223 Verified\n\n==================================================\n5. CITIZEN PROFILE MENU\n==================================================\n\nClicking the profile avatar should open a compact profile menu.\n\nShow:\n\nArun Kumar\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified Citizen\n\nMobile:\n+91 XXXXX XXXXX\n\nReports:\n27\n\nResolved:\n18\n\nReopened:\n2\n\nContribution:\n92%\n\nMenu options:\n\nProfile\nMy Reports\nNotifications\nLanguage\nPrivacy & Security\nSign Out\n\nDo NOT display the full Aadhaar number.\n\nShow only:\n\n\342\200\234Aadhaar Verified\342\200\235\n\nor:\n\n\342\200\234Aadhaar \342\200\242\342\200\242\342\200\242\342\200\242 1234\342\200\235\n\nif a masked identifier is needed.\n\n==================================================\n6. PROFILE PAGE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a detailed but simple profile page.\n\nHeader:\n\n\342\200\234Your Profile\342\200\235\n\nProfile avatar\n\nName:\nArun Kumar\n\nVerification:\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified\n\nMobile:\n+91 XXXXX XXXXX\n\nPreferred Language:\nTamil\n\nArea:\nWard 37\n\nAccount Created:\n27 August 2026\n\nThen:\n\n\342\200\234Your Civic Contribution\342\200\235\n\nReports submitted:\n27\n\nVerified reports:\n24\n\nResolved:\n18\n\nReopened:\n2\n\nKeep this clean and citizen-friendly.\n\n==================================================\n7. SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nAdd a proper sign-out interaction.\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\nShow confirmation:\n\n\342\200\234Sign out of CivicPulse?\342\200\235\n\nButtons:\n\nCancel\nSign Out\n\nAfter signing out:\n- Clear mock authenticated state.\n- Return to the Welcome/Login screen.\n\n==================================================\n8. RETURNING USER EXPERIENCE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a polished welcome screen for users who have not yet authenticated.\n\nIf not authenticated:\n\nShow:\n\nCivicPulse\n\n\342\200\234Report. Resolve. Verify.\342\200\235\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Create / Verify Account\342\200\235\n\nSecondary:\n\342\200\234About CivicPulse\342\200\235\n\nAfter the user has authenticated once:\n\nSkip this screen automatically on future sessions.\n\nInstead:\n\nOpen directly to:\n\nCitizen Home Dashboard\n\nTop-right:\nAvatar\nName\n\342\234\223 Verified\n\n==================================================\n9. GOVERNMENT AUTHENTICATION\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo NOT use Aadhaar authentication for municipal staff.\n\nThe government side should have a separate STAFF LOGIN / ROLE-BASED AUTHENTICATION model.\n\nCreate:\n\nGovernment Login\n\nFields:\nOfficial Email / Employee ID\nPassword\n\nOptional:\n2FA / OTP\n\nRoles:\n\nMunicipal Administrator\nDepartment Supervisor\nDepartment Officer\nField Staff\nAnalyst\n\nAfter login:\nOpen the Government Dashboard.\n\nDisplay in top-right:\n\nOfficer Name\nRole\nDepartment\n\nExample:\n\nPriya Raman\nRoads Department\nSupervisor\n\n==================================================\n10. ROLE-BASED ACCESS\n==================================================\n\nSimulate permissions in the frontend.\n\nMUNICIPAL ADMIN:\nCan view:\n- Everything\n- All departments\n- Settings\n- User management\n- Analytics\n- Routing rules\n- SLA rules\n\nSUPERVISOR:\nCan view:\n- Department dashboard\n- Assigned issues\n- Team workload\n- SLA\n- Escalations\n\nFIELD STAFF:\nCan view:\n- Assigned issues\n- Issue details\n- Location\n- Route\n- Upload resolution evidence\n- Mark work completed\n\nANALYST:\nCan view:\n- Analytics\n- Trends\n- Hotspots\n- Performance data\n\nHide or disable controls that a role should not access.\n\n==================================================\n11. VERIFICATION BADGES\n==================================================\n\nUse subtle but highly visible verification indicators.\n\nCitizen:\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified\n\nGovernment:\n\342\234\223 Official Account\n\nDo not overuse these badges.\n\nThey should increase trust without dominating the interface.\n\n==================================================\n12. CONNECT AUTHENTICATION TO THE CIVIC WORKFLOW\n==================================================\n\nThe authenticated citizen should be linked to every report.\n\nWhen a citizen creates a report, conceptually store:\n\nCitizen ID\nIssue ID\nTimestamp\nLocation\nEvidence\nDescription\n\nThe UI should display:\n\n\342\200\234Reported by You\342\200\235\n\nrather than repeatedly showing personal information.\n\nExample:\n\nIssue #CIV-10482\nReported by You\n27 Aug 2026\n\n==================================================\n13. USE AUTHENTICATION TO SUPPORT TRUST\n==================================================\n\nIntegrate the verified-account concept into the existing trust/spam system.\n\nFor the prototype, show:\n\nReporter:\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nTrust Score:\n92/100\n\nThis should NOT mean that an Aadhaar-verified user is automatically considered truthful.\n\nAadhaar verification establishes account identity, while the trust score represents reporting behaviour.\n\nKeep these concepts visually separate:\n\nIDENTITY:\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified\n\nREPORT TRUST:\n92/100\n\n==================================================\n14. DUPLICATE REPORTING\n==================================================\n\nWhen a verified citizen submits a report that matches an existing civic issue, show:\n\n\342\200\234We found a nearby existing issue.\342\200\235\n\nExample:\n\nExisting Issue:\nCIV-10482\n\n43 citizens have already reported this problem.\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Add My Report\342\200\235\n\nSecondary:\n\342\200\234Report as Different Issue\342\200\235\n\nThis reinforces:\n\nONE PHYSICAL ISSUE\n\342\206\220\nMANY VERIFIED CITIZEN REPORTS\n\n==================================================\n15. NOTIFICATION INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nAuthenticated users should receive personalized notifications.\n\nExamples:\n\n\342\200\234Your report CIV-10482 has been assigned to the Roads Department.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Work has started on the issue you reported.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234CIV-10482 has been marked resolved.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Please verify whether the issue has actually been fixed.\342\200\235\n\nThe profile menu should include a notification indicator.\n\n==================================================\n16. PRIVACY & SECURITY UI\n==================================================\n\nAdd a simple Privacy & Security section.\n\nShow:\n\nIdentity:\n\342\234\223 Verified\n\nAadhaar:\n\342\200\234Protected / Not publicly displayed\342\200\235\n\nPhone:\n\342\200\234Private\342\200\235\n\nReports:\n\342\200\234Only necessary information is publicly visible\342\200\235\n\nAlso show:\n\n\342\200\234CivicPulse never displays your full Aadhaar number in the application.\342\200\235\n\nDo not create unnecessary legal text.\n\nKeep it understandable.\n\n==================================================\n17. AUTHENTICATION STATES\n==================================================\n\nThe frontend must visibly support these states:\n\n1. NOT_AUTHENTICATED\n2. MOBILE_VERIFIED\n3. IDENTITY_VERIFICATION_PENDING\n4. IDENTITY_VERIFIED\n5. AUTHENTICATED\n6. SIGNED_OUT\n\nUse mock local state.\n\nMake transitions actually work.\n\n==================================================\n18. DEMO FLOW FOR JUDGES\n==================================================\n\nCreate a polished demonstration path:\n\nFIRST VISIT:\nWelcome\n\342\206\223\nCreate Account\n\342\206\223\nMobile OTP\n\342\206\223\nAadhaar Verification (Demo)\n\342\206\223\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\342\206\223\nAccount Created\n\342\206\223\nCitizen Dashboard\n\nThen demonstrate:\n\nRefresh page\n\342\206\223\nStill authenticated\n\342\206\223\nNo login required\n\342\206\223\nDashboard opens directly\n\nThen:\n\nProfile icon\n\342\206\223\n\342\200\234Arun Kumar\342\200\235\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified\n\nThen:\n\nReport Issue\n\342\206\223\nIssue linked to authenticated citizen\n\342\206\223\nTrack report\n\342\206\223\nReceive notification\n\342\206\223\nVerify resolution\n\nThis should feel like a complete user identity journey.\n\n==================================================\n19. UI REQUIREMENTS\n==================================================\n\nDo not turn authentication into a complicated multi-page enterprise interface.\n\nCitizen authentication must feel:\n\n- Simple\n- Trustworthy\n- Fast\n- Familiar\n- Mobile-friendly\n\nGovernment authentication should feel:\n\n- Secure\n- Official\n- Professional\n\nUse:\n- Clear verification badges\n- Masked identifiers\n- Minimal forms\n- Strong success states\n- Clear error states\n- Accessible text\n\n==================================================\n20. IMPORTANT PRIVACY DESIGN RULE\n==================================================\n\nFor this prototype:\n\nNEVER:\n- Display a full Aadhaar number\n- Store real Aadhaar information\n- Ask the user to upload a real Aadhaar card\n- Pretend that the prototype is actually connected to UIDAI\n\nInstead use:\n\n\342\200\234Demo Aadhaar Verification\342\200\235\n\nand clearly label the simulated flow.\n\nThe architecture should leave a clean integration point for a future authorized Aadhaar authentication/e-KYC service.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL RESULT\n==================================================\n\nThe final prototype should now behave like:\n\nFIRST TIME USER\n\342\206\222 One-time identity verification\n\342\206\222 Account created\n\342\206\222 Persistent signed-in experience\n\nRETURNING USER\n\342\206\222 Automatically recognized\n\342\206\222 No repeated login\n\342\206\222 Profile always visible in corner\n\nCITIZEN:\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified Citizen\n\342\206\222 Report issues\n\342\206\222 Track reports\n\342\206\222 Receive notifications\n\342\206\222 Verify resolutions\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\342\234\223 Official Account\n\342\206\222 Role-based dashboard\n\342\206\222 Manage issues\n\342\206\222 Assign teams\n\342\206\222 Track SLAs\n\342\206\222 Resolve issues\n\342\206\222 Analyze civic data\n\nDo not break any of the existing features.\n\nThe authentication layer should feel like it was part of CivicPulse from the beginning."
    items {
      text: "Now add a complete AUTHENTICATION AND USER ACCOUNT LAYER to the existing CivicPulse prototype.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not redesign or remove the existing citizen and government dashboards.\n- Preserve the current visual identity, layouts, spacing and navigation.\n- Add authentication as a new foundational layer around the existing application.\n- This is a FRONTEND-ONLY HACKATHON PROTOTYPE, so simulate Aadhaar verification using mock data and local state.\n- Do NOT implement real Aadhaar authentication or collect/store real Aadhaar numbers.\n- Make it visually clear that the prototype represents \342\200\234Aadhaar-verified identity\342\200\235.\n- The architecture should be designed so a real authorized Aadhaar verification provider could be integrated later.\n\n==================================================\n1. AUTHENTICATION MODEL\n==================================================\n\nEvery citizen must have ONE permanent account.\n\nThe intended experience is:\n\nFIRST TIME:\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Create Account\n\342\206\222 Aadhaar Verification\n\342\206\222 Account Created\n\342\206\222 Stay signed in\n\nRETURNING USER:\nOpen application\n\342\206\222 Automatically recognized\n\342\206\222 No repeated login\n\342\206\222 Directly enters the application\n\nThe user should NOT see a login screen every time they open the app.\n\nUse persistent frontend session state to simulate this behavior.\n\nShow:\n\342\200\234Welcome back, [Name]\342\200\235\n\nand a persistent profile/avatar in the top corner.\n\n==================================================\n2. CITIZEN SIGN-UP / ONBOARDING\n==================================================\n\nCreate a new first-time-user onboarding flow.\n\nSCREEN:\n\342\200\234Create your CivicPulse Account\342\200\235\n\nExplain:\n\n\342\200\234Your account helps us prevent duplicate and fraudulent reports and lets you track issues from report to resolution.\342\200\235\n\nStep 1:\nMobile Number\n\nField:\n+91 __________\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Continue\342\200\235\n\nStep 2:\nOTP Verification\n\nShow:\n\342\200\234OTP sent to your registered mobile number\342\200\235\n\nInput:\n6-digit OTP\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Verify Mobile\342\200\235\n\nFor the prototype, accept a mock OTP.\n\nStep 3:\nAadhaar Verification\n\nHeading:\n\342\200\234Verify your identity\342\200\235\n\nDescription:\n\342\200\234Use Aadhaar-based identity verification to create your CivicPulse account.\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT ask the user to upload or store a real Aadhaar card in the prototype.\n\nInstead provide a clearly labelled DEMO verification interface:\n\n\342\200\234Aadhaar Verification \342\200\224 Demo\342\200\235\n\nFields:\nMasked Aadhaar:\nXXXX XXXX 1234\n\nOTP:\n6-digit OTP\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Verify Identity\342\200\235\n\nAfter verification show:\n\n\342\234\223 Identity Verified\n\n\342\200\234Your CivicPulse account is now verified.\342\200\235\n\nInclude a small privacy message:\n\n\342\200\234Your Aadhaar number is not displayed publicly. The prototype stores only a verified-account state and non-sensitive profile information.\342\200\235\n\nDo not expose full Aadhaar numbers anywhere.\n\n==================================================\n3. ACCOUNT CREATION\n==================================================\n\nAfter successful verification:\n\nCreate a mock citizen profile:\n\nName:\nArun Kumar\n\nPhone:\n+91 XXXXX XXXXX\n\nIdentity:\n\342\200\234Aadhaar Verified\342\200\235\n\nVerification badge:\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nPreferred language:\nEnglish\n\nLocation:\nUser\'s selected area\n\nShow:\n\n\342\200\234Account created successfully.\342\200\235\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Continue to CivicPulse\342\200\235\n\nThen open the Citizen Home Dashboard.\n\n==================================================\n4. PERSISTENT SIGN-IN\n==================================================\n\nThis is CRITICAL.\n\nOnce the citizen has completed account creation and verification:\n\n- Store mock authenticated state in localStorage/session persistence.\n- On reopening or refreshing the prototype, automatically recognize the user.\n- Do NOT show login again.\n- Go directly to the Citizen Home Dashboard.\n\nSimulate:\n\nlocalStorage:\ncivicpulse_authenticated = true\ncivicpulse_user = { ...mock profile... }\n\nThe user should experience this as:\n\n\342\200\234One-time account creation \342\206\222 permanent signed-in experience.\342\200\235\n\nAlso show a small profile/avatar in the top-right corner of the application.\n\nExample:\n\n[AR]\nArun Kumar\n\342\234\223 Verified\n\n==================================================\n5. CITIZEN PROFILE MENU\n==================================================\n\nClicking the profile avatar should open a compact profile menu.\n\nShow:\n\nArun Kumar\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified Citizen\n\nMobile:\n+91 XXXXX XXXXX\n\nReports:\n27\n\nResolved:\n18\n\nReopened:\n2\n\nContribution:\n92%\n\nMenu options:\n\nProfile\nMy Reports\nNotifications\nLanguage\nPrivacy & Security\nSign Out\n\nDo NOT display the full Aadhaar number.\n\nShow only:\n\n\342\200\234Aadhaar Verified\342\200\235\n\nor:\n\n\342\200\234Aadhaar \342\200\242\342\200\242\342\200\242\342\200\242 1234\342\200\235\n\nif a masked identifier is needed.\n\n==================================================\n6. PROFILE PAGE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a detailed but simple profile page.\n\nHeader:\n\n\342\200\234Your Profile\342\200\235\n\nProfile avatar\n\nName:\nArun Kumar\n\nVerification:\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified\n\nMobile:\n+91 XXXXX XXXXX\n\nPreferred Language:\nTamil\n\nArea:\nWard 37\n\nAccount Created:\n27 August 2026\n\nThen:\n\n\342\200\234Your Civic Contribution\342\200\235\n\nReports submitted:\n27\n\nVerified reports:\n24\n\nResolved:\n18\n\nReopened:\n2\n\nKeep this clean and citizen-friendly.\n\n==================================================\n7. SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nAdd a proper sign-out interaction.\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\nShow confirmation:\n\n\342\200\234Sign out of CivicPulse?\342\200\235\n\nButtons:\n\nCancel\nSign Out\n\nAfter signing out:\n- Clear mock authenticated state.\n- Return to the Welcome/Login screen.\n\n==================================================\n8. RETURNING USER EXPERIENCE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a polished welcome screen for users who have not yet authenticated.\n\nIf not authenticated:\n\nShow:\n\nCivicPulse\n\n\342\200\234Report. Resolve. Verify.\342\200\235\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Create / Verify Account\342\200\235\n\nSecondary:\n\342\200\234About CivicPulse\342\200\235\n\nAfter the user has authenticated once:\n\nSkip this screen automatically on future sessions.\n\nInstead:\n\nOpen directly to:\n\nCitizen Home Dashboard\n\nTop-right:\nAvatar\nName\n\342\234\223 Verified\n\n==================================================\n9. GOVERNMENT AUTHENTICATION\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo NOT use Aadhaar authentication for municipal staff.\n\nThe government side should have a separate STAFF LOGIN / ROLE-BASED AUTHENTICATION model.\n\nCreate:\n\nGovernment Login\n\nFields:\nOfficial Email / Employee ID\nPassword\n\nOptional:\n2FA / OTP\n\nRoles:\n\nMunicipal Administrator\nDepartment Supervisor\nDepartment Officer\nField Staff\nAnalyst\n\nAfter login:\nOpen the Government Dashboard.\n\nDisplay in top-right:\n\nOfficer Name\nRole\nDepartment\n\nExample:\n\nPriya Raman\nRoads Department\nSupervisor\n\n==================================================\n10. ROLE-BASED ACCESS\n==================================================\n\nSimulate permissions in the frontend.\n\nMUNICIPAL ADMIN:\nCan view:\n- Everything\n- All departments\n- Settings\n- User management\n- Analytics\n- Routing rules\n- SLA rules\n\nSUPERVISOR:\nCan view:\n- Department dashboard\n- Assigned issues\n- Team workload\n- SLA\n- Escalations\n\nFIELD STAFF:\nCan view:\n- Assigned issues\n- Issue details\n- Location\n- Route\n- Upload resolution evidence\n- Mark work completed\n\nANALYST:\nCan view:\n- Analytics\n- Trends\n- Hotspots\n- Performance data\n\nHide or disable controls that a role should not access.\n\n==================================================\n11. VERIFICATION BADGES\n==================================================\n\nUse subtle but highly visible verification indicators.\n\nCitizen:\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified\n\nGovernment:\n\342\234\223 Official Account\n\nDo not overuse these badges.\n\nThey should increase trust without dominating the interface.\n\n==================================================\n12. CONNECT AUTHENTICATION TO THE CIVIC WORKFLOW\n==================================================\n\nThe authenticated citizen should be linked to every report.\n\nWhen a citizen creates a report, conceptually store:\n\nCitizen ID\nIssue ID\nTimestamp\nLocation\nEvidence\nDescription\n\nThe UI should display:\n\n\342\200\234Reported by You\342\200\235\n\nrather than repeatedly showing personal information.\n\nExample:\n\nIssue #CIV-10482\nReported by You\n27 Aug 2026\n\n==================================================\n13. USE AUTHENTICATION TO SUPPORT TRUST\n==================================================\n\nIntegrate the verified-account concept into the existing trust/spam system.\n\nFor the prototype, show:\n\nReporter:\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nTrust Score:\n92/100\n\nThis should NOT mean that an Aadhaar-verified user is automatically considered truthful.\n\nAadhaar verification establishes account identity, while the trust score represents reporting behaviour.\n\nKeep these concepts visually separate:\n\nIDENTITY:\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified\n\nREPORT TRUST:\n92/100\n\n==================================================\n14. DUPLICATE REPORTING\n==================================================\n\nWhen a verified citizen submits a report that matches an existing civic issue, show:\n\n\342\200\234We found a nearby existing issue.\342\200\235\n\nExample:\n\nExisting Issue:\nCIV-10482\n\n43 citizens have already reported this problem.\n\nButton:\n\342\200\234Add My Report\342\200\235\n\nSecondary:\n\342\200\234Report as Different Issue\342\200\235\n\nThis reinforces:\n\nONE PHYSICAL ISSUE\n\342\206\220\nMANY VERIFIED CITIZEN REPORTS\n\n==================================================\n15. NOTIFICATION INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nAuthenticated users should receive personalized notifications.\n\nExamples:\n\n\342\200\234Your report CIV-10482 has been assigned to the Roads Department.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Work has started on the issue you reported.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234CIV-10482 has been marked resolved.\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Please verify whether the issue has actually been fixed.\342\200\235\n\nThe profile menu should include a notification indicator.\n\n==================================================\n16. PRIVACY & SECURITY UI\n==================================================\n\nAdd a simple Privacy & Security section.\n\nShow:\n\nIdentity:\n\342\234\223 Verified\n\nAadhaar:\n\342\200\234Protected / Not publicly displayed\342\200\235\n\nPhone:\n\342\200\234Private\342\200\235\n\nReports:\n\342\200\234Only necessary information is publicly visible\342\200\235\n\nAlso show:\n\n\342\200\234CivicPulse never displays your full Aadhaar number in the application.\342\200\235\n\nDo not create unnecessary legal text.\n\nKeep it understandable.\n\n==================================================\n17. AUTHENTICATION STATES\n==================================================\n\nThe frontend must visibly support these states:\n\n1. NOT_AUTHENTICATED\n2. MOBILE_VERIFIED\n3. IDENTITY_VERIFICATION_PENDING\n4. IDENTITY_VERIFIED\n5. AUTHENTICATED\n6. SIGNED_OUT\n\nUse mock local state.\n\nMake transitions actually work.\n\n==================================================\n18. DEMO FLOW FOR JUDGES\n==================================================\n\nCreate a polished demonstration path:\n\nFIRST VISIT:\nWelcome\n\342\206\223\nCreate Account\n\342\206\223\nMobile OTP\n\342\206\223\nAadhaar Verification (Demo)\n\342\206\223\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\342\206\223\nAccount Created\n\342\206\223\nCitizen Dashboard\n\nThen demonstrate:\n\nRefresh page\n\342\206\223\nStill authenticated\n\342\206\223\nNo login required\n\342\206\223\nDashboard opens directly\n\nThen:\n\nProfile icon\n\342\206\223\n\342\200\234Arun Kumar\342\200\235\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified\n\nThen:\n\nReport Issue\n\342\206\223\nIssue linked to authenticated citizen\n\342\206\223\nTrack report\n\342\206\223\nReceive notification\n\342\206\223\nVerify resolution\n\nThis should feel like a complete user identity journey.\n\n==================================================\n19. UI REQUIREMENTS\n==================================================\n\nDo not turn authentication into a complicated multi-page enterprise interface.\n\nCitizen authentication must feel:\n\n- Simple\n- Trustworthy\n- Fast\n- Familiar\n- Mobile-friendly\n\nGovernment authentication should feel:\n\n- Secure\n- Official\n- Professional\n\nUse:\n- Clear verification badges\n- Masked identifiers\n- Minimal forms\n- Strong success states\n- Clear error states\n- Accessible text\n\n==================================================\n20. IMPORTANT PRIVACY DESIGN RULE\n==================================================\n\nFor this prototype:\n\nNEVER:\n- Display a full Aadhaar number\n- Store real Aadhaar information\n- Ask the user to upload a real Aadhaar card\n- Pretend that the prototype is actually connected to UIDAI\n\nInstead use:\n\n\342\200\234Demo Aadhaar Verification\342\200\235\n\nand clearly label the simulated flow.\n\nThe architecture should leave a clean integration point for a future authorized Aadhaar authentication/e-KYC service.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL RESULT\n==================================================\n\nThe final prototype should now behave like:\n\nFIRST TIME USER\n\342\206\222 One-time identity verification\n\342\206\222 Account created\n\342\206\222 Persistent signed-in experience\n\nRETURNING USER\n\342\206\222 Automatically recognized\n\342\206\222 No repeated login\n\342\206\222 Profile always visible in corner\n\nCITIZEN:\n\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified Citizen\n\342\206\222 Report issues\n\342\206\222 Track reports\n\342\206\222 Receive notifications\n\342\206\222 Verify resolutions\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\342\234\223 Official Account\n\342\206\222 Role-based dashboard\n\342\206\222 Manage issues\n\342\206\222 Assign teams\n\342\206\222 Track SLAs\n\342\206\222 Resolve issues\n\342\206\222 Analyze civic data\n\nDo not break any of the existing features.\n\nThe authentication layer should feel like it was part of CivicPulse from the beginning."
    }
  }
}
