  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the precise scope of this authentication and user account layer for the CivicPulse prototype. I\'m carefully considering the goal of adding this functionality without altering existing dashboards or the visual identity. Preserving the existing layouts, spacing, and navigation is paramount to this process.\n\n\n**Outlining Functionality**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the specific features. The \"Demo\" flow for Aadhaar is crucial, masking numbers. I\'m prioritizing citizen onboarding, persistent login, and profile menus. I\'ll need to create profile pages. I also want government authentication, role-based access, and verification badges. Connecting auth to the civic workflow and duplicate reporting are also essential. I will focus on trust scores versus identity integration.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the existing code architecture. I see I need to expand the `AppContext` to manage authentication state and user details. Specifically, `src/context/AppContext.tsx` and `src/App.tsx` require updates to integrate auth status and routing. I will focus on integrating a new `Welcome/Login` screen and updating `CitizenApp.tsx` and `GovApp.tsx` to reflect new authentication states, adding profile features and role-based conditional rendering.\n\n\n**Implementing Authentication Steps**\n\nI\'ve been working on authentication functions and persisting the authentication state to local storage. I\'m now crafting the necessary screens, including a welcome screen to route users to the Citizen or Government login flows. For the citizen side, I\'m developing an onboarding flow, including Aadhaar demo integration. For government users, I\'m creating an email-password login with mock role selection. Integrating these changes, I\'m updating `App.tsx` to conditionally render citizen or government applications based on authentication. I plan to enhance both app interfaces with profile features and role-based elements.\n\n\n**Refactoring AppContext**\n\nI\'m now refactoring `AppContext.tsx` to ensure it loads authentication from `localStorage` on component mount. The goal is to manage the user\'s state, including `CitizenUser` or `GovUser` and handle `loginCitizen()`, `loginGov()`, and `logout()`.  I\'m also preparing to create the authentication screens: `Welcome.tsx`, `CitizenLogin.tsx`, and `GovLogin.tsx` with specific flows for each role.\n\n\n"
