  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the Authentication and User Account layer for the CivicPulse prototype, focusing on a seamless identity flow for both citizens and government staff without compromising the existing design language.\n\nHere is an overview of the implementation:\n\n- **Welcome & Auth Routing (`AuthFlow`)**: Replaced the direct global app-switcher with a polished landing screen. New users enter through a simplified onboarding journey, while returning users with a saved session (using `localStorage` mock state) are securely routed directly into their respective dashboards.\n- **Citizen \"Aadhaar-Verified\" Flow**: Implemented a realistic but safely simulated mobile OTP and mock Aadhaar verification pipeline. Upon completion, the citizen receives a permanent **\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified** identity badge that follows them through the application.\n- **Persistent Profile & Trust Integration**: The citizen application now features a dynamic profile menu displaying their verification status and an expansive `Profile` screen detailing their civic contributions. All new reports are conceptually linked to the citizen\'s authenticated identity, showing a **\"\342\234\223 Reported by You\"** badge in the issue detail view.\n- **Smart Duplicate Issue Warning**: When a verified citizen files a report, they are now shown a \"Similar Issue Found\" step (e.g. for canonical issue `CIV-10482`), allowing you to smoothly demonstrate how Aadhaar-verified identity helps merge duplicate reports and prevent spam.\n- **Government Role-Based Security**: Built a secure staff login portal with a dropdown for roles (e.g., Administrator, Supervisor, Field Staff). The government dashboard now displays a robust header with their role, an **\342\234\223 Official Account** badge, and dynamically filters the sidebar navigation depending on the authenticated staff member\'s permissions.\n\nThe prototype is now fully stateful and ready for your hackathon demonstration."
    thinking: "**Concluding the Build Process**\n\nThe build completed successfully! My focus now shifts to articulating a concise summary. I\'ve concentrated on encapsulating the overarching authentication state within `AuthFlow.tsx`, effectively managing the login process without disrupting the current router\'s functionality. With this crucial piece now complete, I\'m ready to wrap up.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the Authentication and User Account layer for the CivicPulse prototype, focusing on a seamless identity flow for both citizens and government staff without compromising the existing design language.\n\nHere is an overview of the implementation:\n\n- **Welcome & Auth Routing (`AuthFlow`)**: Replaced the direct global app-switcher with a polished landing screen. New users enter through a simplified onboarding journey, while returning users with a saved session (using `localStorage` mock state) are securely routed directly into their respective dashboards.\n- **Citizen \"Aadhaar-Verified\" Flow**: Implemented a realistic but safely simulated mobile OTP and mock Aadhaar verification pipeline. Upon completion, the citizen receives a permanent **\342\234\223 Aadhaar Verified** identity badge that follows them through the application.\n- **Persistent Profile & Trust Integration**: The citizen application now features a dynamic profile menu displaying their verification status and an expansive `Profile` screen detailing their civic contributions. All new reports are conceptually linked to the citizen\'s authenticated identity, showing a **\"\342\234\223 Reported by You\"** badge in the issue detail view.\n- **Smart Duplicate Issue Warning**: When a verified citizen files a report, they are now shown a \"Similar Issue Found\" step (e.g. for canonical issue `CIV-10482`), allowing you to smoothly demonstrate how Aadhaar-verified identity helps merge duplicate reports and prevent spam.\n- **Government Role-Based Security**: Built a secure staff login portal with a dropdown for roles (e.g., Administrator, Supervisor, Field Staff). The government dashboard now displays a robust header with their role, an **\342\234\223 Official Account** badge, and dynamically filters the sidebar navigation depending on the authenticated staff member\'s permissions.\n\nThe prototype is now fully stateful and ready for your hackathon demonstration."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 200034729
    }
