    thinking: "**Initiating Privacy Focus**\n\nI\'m starting by meticulously analyzing the project request. The core goal is adding a \"Privacy Protection\" feature, focusing specifically on automatic face blurring in user-uploaded photos. I\'ve broken down the key requirements to better understand the project scope, and am now diving into specific implementation details. I anticipate this will be a challenging, yet engaging process.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation Strategy**\n\nI\'ve established a concrete implementation strategy, keeping existing features intact. I\'m focusing on additions to the citizen and government interfaces. Specifically, I\'m integrating processing states and privacy indicators into the Citizen Report Screen, and adding a \"Privacy Protected\" badge and a \"PHOTO PRIVACY\" section to the Government Dashboard. I\'m making sure my work aligns with the required file modifications. The simulated upload flow is now ready to begin.\n\n\n**Refining Mock Data Strategy**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on mock data, starting with crucial file updates. I\'ve updated the `Issue` type to include `privacyProcessed` and `facesBlurredCount`. I\'ve also incorporated these values into the `MOCK_ISSUES` data, focusing especially on the demo issues. For the image, I\'m considering several options, including a placeholder with CSS blur, and a visually appealing mock URL.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Demo**\n\nI\'ve decided on the demo strategy for face blurring: using a small, blurred `div` overlaying part of the image. For the citizen flow, when the user clicks \"Capture\", it will go into a \"Protecting Privacy...\" loading state for 1-1.5 seconds. Then, I\'ll show the captured image with the blurred overlay, plus a \"\342\234\223 Privacy Protected\" badge with explanatory text. This should be a good proof-of-concept.\n\n\n**Finalizing User Experience**\n\nI\'ve determined the final visual representation for the face blurring feature. I\'ll overlay a blurred `div` element on the image to simulate the effect, ensuring visual consistency. In the citizen flow, when the user clicks \"Capture,\" it transitions into a \"Protecting Privacy...\" loading state for 1-1.5 seconds before displaying the captured image with the blurred overlay and a \"\342\234\223 Privacy Protected\" badge alongside a message explaining the number of faces blurred. This offers a clear demonstration to the judges.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 54830754
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
