  user_input {
    user_response: "IMPORTANT: Simplify the CITIZEN-FACING interface of the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nThis change is specifically for citizens with LIMITED DIGITAL LITERACY.\n\nDO NOT redesign or simplify the Government / Municipal Dashboard.\nThe government interface should remain detailed and information-rich.\n\nDo NOT remove any backend concepts or existing prototype functionality.\nOnly hide unnecessary technical complexity from the citizen-facing UI.\n\n==================================================\n1. CAMERA-FIRST HOME EXPERIENCE\n==================================================\n\nWhen an authenticated citizen opens the application, do NOT open a complex dashboard first.\n\nThe default landing experience should immediately be:\n\nCAMERA / REPORT ISSUE SCREEN\n\nThe primary purpose of the app should be visually obvious:\n\n\342\200\234See a problem? Take a photo.\342\200\235\n\nOpen directly into the camera experience.\n\nShow:\n\n[ CAMERA VIEWFINDER ]\n\nLarge button:\n\n\342\200\234Take Photo\342\200\235\n\nKeep the interface extremely minimal.\n\nDo NOT show:\n- Analytics\n- Issue categories\n- Department information\n- AI information\n- Workflow information\n- Technical terminology\n- Complex forms\n- Multiple dashboard cards\n\nThe citizen should immediately understand:\n\n\342\200\234Take a picture of the problem.\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\n2. AFTER TAKING THE PHOTO\n==================================================\n\nImmediately move to:\n\n\342\200\234Describe the problem\342\200\235\n\nShow the captured image at the top.\n\nProvide ONE large text field:\n\n\342\200\234What is the problem?\342\200\235\n\nExample placeholder:\n\n\342\200\234Example: There is a big pothole here.\342\200\235\n\nAllow a microphone button:\n\n\360\237\216\244 \342\200\234Speak\342\200\235\n\nThis lets users describe the issue instead of typing.\n\nDo not force the citizen to select:\n- Category\n- Severity\n- Department\n- Ward\n- Priority\n- Issue type\n\nThe system should handle those in the background.\n\n==================================================\n3. LOCATION\n==================================================\n\nAutomatically capture the user\'s location.\n\nDo NOT make citizens manually enter:\n- Latitude\n- Longitude\n- Ward\n- Department\n- Municipality\n\nShow only a simple confirmation:\n\n\360\237\223\215 Location detected\n\nOptionally show:\n\342\200\234Anna Nagar Main Road\342\200\235\n\nProvide a small:\n\n\342\200\234Change location\342\200\235\n\noption for users who need to correct it.\n\n==================================================\n4. SUBMISSION\n==================================================\n\nAfter:\n\nPHOTO\n+\nDESCRIPTION\n+\nLOCATION\n\nShow one large primary button:\n\n\342\200\234Submit Report\342\200\235\n\nNothing else should compete visually with this action.\n\nAfter submission:\n\n\342\234\223 \342\200\234Report submitted\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Thank you for reporting this civic issue.\342\200\235\n\nShow the Issue ID in a secondary location.\n\nThen provide:\n\n\342\200\234Track Report\342\200\235\n\nDo not expose technical processing details.\n\n==================================================\n5. HIDE AI COMPLETELY FROM CITIZENS\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe word \342\200\234AI\342\200\235 must NOT appear anywhere in the citizen-facing interface.\n\nDo NOT show:\n\n- AI\n- AI detected\n- AI classification\n- AI confidence\n- AI score\n- AI processing\n- Machine learning\n- Model confidence\n- Duplicate probability\n- Spam probability\n\nAI may continue to operate in the background, but it should be completely invisible to the citizen.\n\nInstead of:\n\n\342\200\234AI detected a pothole\342\200\235\n\ndo not show any classification message at all.\n\nThe citizen simply reports the problem.\n\n==================================================\n6. HIDE THE MUNICIPAL WORKFLOW FROM CITIZENS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT expose the internal government workflow.\n\nDo NOT show:\n\nSubmitted\n\342\206\222 Verified\n\342\206\222 Routed\n\342\206\222 Assigned\n\342\206\222 SLA\n\342\206\222 Escalated\n\342\206\222 Work Started\n\342\206\222 Resolved\n\nas an internal workflow diagram.\n\nThe citizen only needs a simple status.\n\nUse plain-language states such as:\n\n\342\200\234Report received\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Being handled\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Work completed\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Please confirm the fix\342\200\235\n\nKeep the internal workflow completely hidden.\n\n==================================================\n7. KEEP CITIZEN STATUS SIMPLE\n==================================================\n\nWhen citizens open \342\200\234My Reports\342\200\235, use extremely simple cards.\n\nExample:\n\n--------------------------------\n\360\237\223\267 Pothole near bus stop\n\n\360\237\223\215 Anna Nagar\n\n\360\237\237\240 Being handled\n--------------------------------\n\nAnother:\n\n--------------------------------\n\360\237\223\267 Broken streetlight\n\n\360\237\223\215 Ward 37\n\n\360\237\237\242 Fixed \342\200\224 Please confirm\n--------------------------------\n\nAvoid technical details.\n\nDo not show:\n- Department\n- SLA\n- Priority score\n- AI confidence\n- Internal routing\n- Assignment information\n- Escalation level\n\n==================================================\n8. CITIZEN ISSUE DETAIL\n==================================================\n\nKeep the issue detail screen simple.\n\nShow:\n\nLarge issue photo\n\nIssue description\n\nLocation\n\nCurrent simple status\n\nExample:\n\n\342\200\234Your report has been received.\342\200\235\n\nThen:\n\n\342\200\234Work completed\342\200\235\n\nThen:\n\n\342\200\234Is the problem fixed?\342\200\235\n\nTwo large buttons:\n\n\342\234\205 Yes, fixed\n\n\342\235\214 No, still a problem\n\nIf the user selects \342\200\234No\342\200\235:\n\n\342\200\234Thank you. We\342\200\231ll ask the responsible team to look at it again.\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT expose internal workflow mechanics.\n\n==================================================\n9. SIMPLE LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nUse plain everyday language.\n\nAvoid words such as:\n\n- Jurisdiction\n- Municipality routing\n- Priority engine\n- SLA\n- Escalation\n- Classification\n- Confidence score\n- Department assignment\n- Workflow\n- Verification pipeline\n\nInstead use:\n\n\342\200\234Your report\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Being handled\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Work completed\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Problem still exists\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Report again\342\200\235\n\nThe interface should feel understandable to someone who has very little experience using smartphones.\n\n==================================================\n10. MINIMAL NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nThe citizen bottom navigation should contain only:\n\n\360\237\217\240 Home\n\360\237\223\267 Report\n\360\237\223\213 My Reports\n\360\237\221\244 Profile\n\nDo not add many menu items.\n\nNotifications can appear as a small icon in the header rather than another major navigation item.\n\n==================================================\n11. LARGE TOUCH TARGETS\n==================================================\n\nDesign specifically for users who may struggle with small controls.\n\nUse:\n\n- Large buttons\n- Large icons\n- Large text\n- High contrast\n- Generous spacing\n- Simple labels\n- Minimal scrolling\n\nAvoid:\n- Tiny icons\n- Dense cards\n- Hidden gestures\n- Small dropdowns\n- Complex forms\n- Multi-column layouts\n\n==================================================\n12. LANGUAGE SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nKeep language selection extremely simple.\n\nAllow:\n\nEnglish\n\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\n+ Other supported Indian languages\n\nPlace a simple language selector in Profile / Settings.\n\nThe citizen should not need to configure anything before reporting.\n\n==================================================\n13. VOICE INPUT\n==================================================\n\nMake voice reporting obvious.\n\nOn the description screen:\n\n\360\237\216\244\n\n\342\200\234Speak instead\342\200\235\n\nWhen pressed:\n\n\342\200\234Tell us what the problem is.\342\200\235\n\nConvert the spoken description into text.\n\nDo not expose speech-processing terminology.\n\n==================================================\n14. OFFLINE MODE\n==================================================\n\nKeep offline functionality simple.\n\nIf the user has no internet:\n\nShow a small banner:\n\n\342\200\234No internet connection\342\200\235\n\nThe citizen can STILL:\n\nTake photo\n\342\206\222 Write/speak description\n\342\206\222 Submit\n\nThen show:\n\n\342\200\234Saved. It will be sent when internet returns.\342\200\235\n\nDo not expose technical sync queues or background-processing terminology.\n\n==================================================\n15. PRIVACY FEATURE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the existing automatic face-blurring feature.\n\nAfter photo capture, if faces are detected:\n\nAutomatically blur them.\n\nShow only a small message:\n\n\342\234\223 \342\200\234People\'s faces are protected\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT explain the technical implementation.\n\n==================================================\n16. PROFILE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the profile accessible from the top-right corner.\n\nShow:\n\n[Avatar]\n\nArun Kumar\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nKeep the rest simple.\n\nProfile options:\n\nMy Profile\nMy Reports\nLanguage\nPrivacy\nSign Out\n\nDo not expose complicated account information.\n\n==================================================\n17. VERY IMPORTANT PRODUCT PRINCIPLE\n==================================================\n\nThe citizen should NOT have to understand how CivicPulse works internally.\n\nThe citizen should only need to understand:\n\nSEE A PROBLEM\n\342\206\223\nTAKE PHOTO\n\342\206\223\nDESCRIBE IT\n\342\206\223\nSUBMIT\n\342\206\223\nTRACK IT\n\342\206\223\nCONFIRM THE FIX\n\nEverything else should happen behind the scenes.\n\n==================================================\n18. DO NOT REMOVE GOVERNMENT-SIDE COMPLEXITY\n==================================================\n\nThis simplification applies ONLY to the citizen-facing experience.\n\nKeep the Government / Municipal Dashboard detailed.\n\nGovernment users can still see:\n\n- AI-generated classifications\n- Confidence scores\n- Duplicate clusters\n- Trust scores\n- Priority scores\n- Jurisdiction\n- Department\n- SLA\n- Assignment\n- Escalation\n- Workflow\n- Analytics\n- Hotspots\n- Resolution evidence\n\nThe system should therefore have:\n\nCITIZEN VIEW\n\342\206\222 Simple\n\342\206\222 Minimal\n\342\206\222 Action-oriented\n\nGOVERNMENT VIEW\n\342\206\222 Detailed\n\342\206\222 Information-rich\n\342\206\222 Operational\n\n==================================================\n19. FINAL CITIZEN EXPERIENCE\n==================================================\n\nThe ideal first-time experience should feel like this:\n\nOpen app\n\342\206\223\nCamera opens\n\342\206\223\nTake photo\n\342\206\223\n\342\200\234What\'s the problem?\342\200\235\n\342\206\223\nType or speak\n\342\206\223\nLocation automatically detected\n\342\206\223\nSubmit Report\n\342\206\223\nDone\n\nThe citizen should not need to understand:\n- AI\n- Municipal departments\n- Routing\n- Priority\n- Workflows\n- SLAs\n- Administrative boundaries\n\nThe platform handles the complexity.\n\nThe citizen only reports the problem.\n\nDO NOT CHANGE THE OFFICIAL PRODUCT NAME:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235\n\nPreserve the existing authentication, Aadhaar demo verification, privacy/face-blurring feature, government dashboard, analytics, and other functionality.\n\nOnly simplify the citizen-facing experience as specified above."
    items {
      text: "IMPORTANT: Simplify the CITIZEN-FACING interface of the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nThis change is specifically for citizens with LIMITED DIGITAL LITERACY.\n\nDO NOT redesign or simplify the Government / Municipal Dashboard.\nThe government interface should remain detailed and information-rich.\n\nDo NOT remove any backend concepts or existing prototype functionality.\nOnly hide unnecessary technical complexity from the citizen-facing UI.\n\n==================================================\n1. CAMERA-FIRST HOME EXPERIENCE\n==================================================\n\nWhen an authenticated citizen opens the application, do NOT open a complex dashboard first.\n\nThe default landing experience should immediately be:\n\nCAMERA / REPORT ISSUE SCREEN\n\nThe primary purpose of the app should be visually obvious:\n\n\342\200\234See a problem? Take a photo.\342\200\235\n\nOpen directly into the camera experience.\n\nShow:\n\n[ CAMERA VIEWFINDER ]\n\nLarge button:\n\n\342\200\234Take Photo\342\200\235\n\nKeep the interface extremely minimal.\n\nDo NOT show:\n- Analytics\n- Issue categories\n- Department information\n- AI information\n- Workflow information\n- Technical terminology\n- Complex forms\n- Multiple dashboard cards\n\nThe citizen should immediately understand:\n\n\342\200\234Take a picture of the problem.\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\n2. AFTER TAKING THE PHOTO\n==================================================\n\nImmediately move to:\n\n\342\200\234Describe the problem\342\200\235\n\nShow the captured image at the top.\n\nProvide ONE large text field:\n\n\342\200\234What is the problem?\342\200\235\n\nExample placeholder:\n\n\342\200\234Example: There is a big pothole here.\342\200\235\n\nAllow a microphone button:\n\n\360\237\216\244 \342\200\234Speak\342\200\235\n\nThis lets users describe the issue instead of typing.\n\nDo not force the citizen to select:\n- Category\n- Severity\n- Department\n- Ward\n- Priority\n- Issue type\n\nThe system should handle those in the background.\n\n==================================================\n3. LOCATION\n==================================================\n\nAutomatically capture the user\'s location.\n\nDo NOT make citizens manually enter:\n- Latitude\n- Longitude\n- Ward\n- Department\n- Municipality\n\nShow only a simple confirmation:\n\n\360\237\223\215 Location detected\n\nOptionally show:\n\342\200\234Anna Nagar Main Road\342\200\235\n\nProvide a small:\n\n\342\200\234Change location\342\200\235\n\noption for users who need to correct it.\n\n==================================================\n4. SUBMISSION\n==================================================\n\nAfter:\n\nPHOTO\n+\nDESCRIPTION\n+\nLOCATION\n\nShow one large primary button:\n\n\342\200\234Submit Report\342\200\235\n\nNothing else should compete visually with this action.\n\nAfter submission:\n\n\342\234\223 \342\200\234Report submitted\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Thank you for reporting this civic issue.\342\200\235\n\nShow the Issue ID in a secondary location.\n\nThen provide:\n\n\342\200\234Track Report\342\200\235\n\nDo not expose technical processing details.\n\n==================================================\n5. HIDE AI COMPLETELY FROM CITIZENS\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe word \342\200\234AI\342\200\235 must NOT appear anywhere in the citizen-facing interface.\n\nDo NOT show:\n\n- AI\n- AI detected\n- AI classification\n- AI confidence\n- AI score\n- AI processing\n- Machine learning\n- Model confidence\n- Duplicate probability\n- Spam probability\n\nAI may continue to operate in the background, but it should be completely invisible to the citizen.\n\nInstead of:\n\n\342\200\234AI detected a pothole\342\200\235\n\ndo not show any classification message at all.\n\nThe citizen simply reports the problem.\n\n==================================================\n6. HIDE THE MUNICIPAL WORKFLOW FROM CITIZENS\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT expose the internal government workflow.\n\nDo NOT show:\n\nSubmitted\n\342\206\222 Verified\n\342\206\222 Routed\n\342\206\222 Assigned\n\342\206\222 SLA\n\342\206\222 Escalated\n\342\206\222 Work Started\n\342\206\222 Resolved\n\nas an internal workflow diagram.\n\nThe citizen only needs a simple status.\n\nUse plain-language states such as:\n\n\342\200\234Report received\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Being handled\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Work completed\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Please confirm the fix\342\200\235\n\nKeep the internal workflow completely hidden.\n\n==================================================\n7. KEEP CITIZEN STATUS SIMPLE\n==================================================\n\nWhen citizens open \342\200\234My Reports\342\200\235, use extremely simple cards.\n\nExample:\n\n--------------------------------\n\360\237\223\267 Pothole near bus stop\n\n\360\237\223\215 Anna Nagar\n\n\360\237\237\240 Being handled\n--------------------------------\n\nAnother:\n\n--------------------------------\n\360\237\223\267 Broken streetlight\n\n\360\237\223\215 Ward 37\n\n\360\237\237\242 Fixed \342\200\224 Please confirm\n--------------------------------\n\nAvoid technical details.\n\nDo not show:\n- Department\n- SLA\n- Priority score\n- AI confidence\n- Internal routing\n- Assignment information\n- Escalation level\n\n==================================================\n8. CITIZEN ISSUE DETAIL\n==================================================\n\nKeep the issue detail screen simple.\n\nShow:\n\nLarge issue photo\n\nIssue description\n\nLocation\n\nCurrent simple status\n\nExample:\n\n\342\200\234Your report has been received.\342\200\235\n\nThen:\n\n\342\200\234Work completed\342\200\235\n\nThen:\n\n\342\200\234Is the problem fixed?\342\200\235\n\nTwo large buttons:\n\n\342\234\205 Yes, fixed\n\n\342\235\214 No, still a problem\n\nIf the user selects \342\200\234No\342\200\235:\n\n\342\200\234Thank you. We\342\200\231ll ask the responsible team to look at it again.\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT expose internal workflow mechanics.\n\n==================================================\n9. SIMPLE LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nUse plain everyday language.\n\nAvoid words such as:\n\n- Jurisdiction\n- Municipality routing\n- Priority engine\n- SLA\n- Escalation\n- Classification\n- Confidence score\n- Department assignment\n- Workflow\n- Verification pipeline\n\nInstead use:\n\n\342\200\234Your report\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Being handled\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Work completed\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Problem still exists\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Report again\342\200\235\n\nThe interface should feel understandable to someone who has very little experience using smartphones.\n\n==================================================\n10. MINIMAL NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nThe citizen bottom navigation should contain only:\n\n\360\237\217\240 Home\n\360\237\223\267 Report\n\360\237\223\213 My Reports\n\360\237\221\244 Profile\n\nDo not add many menu items.\n\nNotifications can appear as a small icon in the header rather than another major navigation item.\n\n==================================================\n11. LARGE TOUCH TARGETS\n==================================================\n\nDesign specifically for users who may struggle with small controls.\n\nUse:\n\n- Large buttons\n- Large icons\n- Large text\n- High contrast\n- Generous spacing\n- Simple labels\n- Minimal scrolling\n\nAvoid:\n- Tiny icons\n- Dense cards\n- Hidden gestures\n- Small dropdowns\n- Complex forms\n- Multi-column layouts\n\n==================================================\n12. LANGUAGE SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nKeep language selection extremely simple.\n\nAllow:\n\nEnglish\n\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\n+ Other supported Indian languages\n\nPlace a simple language selector in Profile / Settings.\n\nThe citizen should not need to configure anything before reporting.\n\n==================================================\n13. VOICE INPUT\n==================================================\n\nMake voice reporting obvious.\n\nOn the description screen:\n\n\360\237\216\244\n\n\342\200\234Speak instead\342\200\235\n\nWhen pressed:\n\n\342\200\234Tell us what the problem is.\342\200\235\n\nConvert the spoken description into text.\n\nDo not expose speech-processing terminology.\n\n==================================================\n14. OFFLINE MODE\n==================================================\n\nKeep offline functionality simple.\n\nIf the user has no internet:\n\nShow a small banner:\n\n\342\200\234No internet connection\342\200\235\n\nThe citizen can STILL:\n\nTake photo\n\342\206\222 Write/speak description\n\342\206\222 Submit\n\nThen show:\n\n\342\200\234Saved. It will be sent when internet returns.\342\200\235\n\nDo not expose technical sync queues or background-processing terminology.\n\n==================================================\n15. PRIVACY FEATURE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the existing automatic face-blurring feature.\n\nAfter photo capture, if faces are detected:\n\nAutomatically blur them.\n\nShow only a small message:\n\n\342\234\223 \342\200\234People\'s faces are protected\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT explain the technical implementation.\n\n==================================================\n16. PROFILE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the profile accessible from the top-right corner.\n\nShow:\n\n[Avatar]\n\nArun Kumar\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nKeep the rest simple.\n\nProfile options:\n\nMy Profile\nMy Reports\nLanguage\nPrivacy\nSign Out\n\nDo not expose complicated account information.\n\n==================================================\n17. VERY IMPORTANT PRODUCT PRINCIPLE\n==================================================\n\nThe citizen should NOT have to understand how CivicPulse works internally.\n\nThe citizen should only need to understand:\n\nSEE A PROBLEM\n\342\206\223\nTAKE PHOTO\n\342\206\223\nDESCRIBE IT\n\342\206\223\nSUBMIT\n\342\206\223\nTRACK IT\n\342\206\223\nCONFIRM THE FIX\n\nEverything else should happen behind the scenes.\n\n==================================================\n18. DO NOT REMOVE GOVERNMENT-SIDE COMPLEXITY\n==================================================\n\nThis simplification applies ONLY to the citizen-facing experience.\n\nKeep the Government / Municipal Dashboard detailed.\n\nGovernment users can still see:\n\n- AI-generated classifications\n- Confidence scores\n- Duplicate clusters\n- Trust scores\n- Priority scores\n- Jurisdiction\n- Department\n- SLA\n- Assignment\n- Escalation\n- Workflow\n- Analytics\n- Hotspots\n- Resolution evidence\n\nThe system should therefore have:\n\nCITIZEN VIEW\n\342\206\222 Simple\n\342\206\222 Minimal\n\342\206\222 Action-oriented\n\nGOVERNMENT VIEW\n\342\206\222 Detailed\n\342\206\222 Information-rich\n\342\206\222 Operational\n\n==================================================\n19. FINAL CITIZEN EXPERIENCE\n==================================================\n\nThe ideal first-time experience should feel like this:\n\nOpen app\n\342\206\223\nCamera opens\n\342\206\223\nTake photo\n\342\206\223\n\342\200\234What\'s the problem?\342\200\235\n\342\206\223\nType or speak\n\342\206\223\nLocation automatically detected\n\342\206\223\nSubmit Report\n\342\206\223\nDone\n\nThe citizen should not need to understand:\n- AI\n- Municipal departments\n- Routing\n- Priority\n- Workflows\n- SLAs\n- Administrative boundaries\n\nThe platform handles the complexity.\n\nThe citizen only reports the problem.\n\nDO NOT CHANGE THE OFFICIAL PRODUCT NAME:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235\n\nPreserve the existing authentication, Aadhaar demo verification, privacy/face-blurring feature, government dashboard, analytics, and other functionality.\n\nOnly simplify the citizen-facing experience as specified above."
