  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Focus**\n\nI\'m zeroing in on simplifying the citizen-facing interface, specifically targeting those with limited digital literacy. My scope is strictly the `src/citizen/` directory, excluding any changes to the government dashboard, authentication, or data logic.\n\n\n**Refining the Approach**\n\nI\'ve got a much clearer picture now. The citizen experience will start with the camera; the user sees a problem, and they take a photo. After taking a photo, the next page has only a simple description with an auto-captured location. It\'s streamlined to submission with no mention of AI or complex municipal workflows. Simplicity is key!\n\n\n**Prioritizing Citizen Clarity**\n\nMy focus is sharpening, I\'m now honing in on the \"My Reports\" section and issue detail views. I\'m imagining large photos, straightforward descriptions, and an ultra-clear status. \"Work completed\" will trigger a simple \"Is the problem fixed?\" with Yes/No buttons. I\'m deliberately excluding any complex jargon, so it should be plain, everyday language throughout. Navigation is getting minimal, with Home (Report), My Reports, and Profile. I\'m making sure all the touch targets are big and easy, with language selection available, voice input, and an offline mode.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Interface**\n\nI\'m deep in the code now, particularly `CitizenApp.tsx`, and planning to overhaul the initial screen. The current `Home.tsx` is clunky, so I\'m thinking of either making it a simple camera launch button or just redirecting to `ReportFlow` immediately. I\'m axing the category selection in the flow, so the camera view becomes Step 1, with the description step as Step 2. I\'m focusing on simplicity, removing any unnecessary steps, and streamlining to the core functionality. I will replace \"\342\234\223 People\'s faces are protected\" message instead of technical explanations. The profile will be easily accessible.\n\n\n**Simplifying Citizen Reports**\n\nI\'m now implementing the redesigned report submission flow. The old text input area gets a large \"Speak instead\" button. Priority, type, and category fields are gone. Location is simplified to \"\360\237\223\215 Location detected\" with a change option. Step 4 (Duplicate Warning) is being removed entirely, or at least heavily simplified. The \"Submit Report\" button is now prominent. The privacy message gets a friendlier tweak. I\'m streamlining \"My Reports\" with clear status updates.\n\n\n**Executing the Implementation**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the code. I\'m focusing on the implementation of the core components. I\'m starting by streamlining the profile screen. I\'m adding a language selector placeholder. I\'m focusing on Step 1, updating routes in `CitizenApp.tsx` and bottom navigation, and then moving to `ReportFlow.tsx`, rewriting the flow into a simple photo/description/submit. I\'m ensuring everything is super easy for all citizens.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 43063633
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
