  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully simplified the Citizen-facing interface of the **Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution** prototype, optimizing it specifically for users with limited digital literacy, while keeping the complex workflows safely behind the scenes in the Government dashboard.\n\nHere is an overview of the simplified experience:\n\n- **Camera-First Landing**: When citizens open the application, they immediately land on the camera experience with a simple prompt to take a photo of the problem. No complex dashboards, categories, or analytics compete for their attention.\n- **Unified Reporting Step**: After capturing the image, the user sees a single, focused screen featuring their photo, a large \"Describe the problem\" input with a prominent **\360\237\216\244 Speak instead** voice-input button, and their auto-detected location. Technical fields like Priority, Category, and Ward have been completely removed.\n- **Abstracted Technical & AI Logic**: All references to Artificial Intelligence, confidence scores, duplicate merging, and municipal routing have been completely removed from the citizen view. \n- **Plain Language Statuses**: The complex internal statuses (e.g., *Under Review*, *Assigned*) are now translated into plain, everyday language for citizens:\n  - *Report received*\n  - *Being handled*\n  - *Work completed*\n  - *Fixed \342\200\224 Please confirm*\n- **Simplified Resolution Flow**: When a municipality marks a report as resolved, the citizen simply sees the before-and-after photos and is asked \"Is the problem fixed?\" with two massive touch targets: **\342\234\205 Yes, fixed** and **\342\235\214 No, still a problem**.\n- **Large Touch Targets & Contrast**: Every button, navigation item, and text field in the citizen view has been significantly increased in scale to accommodate individuals who struggle with fine motor control on digital devices.\n- **Language Selector**: The Profile screen has been heavily simplified, removing trust scores and analytics, replacing them with a straightforward tap-to-select language option (English, \340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215, \340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200).\n\nThe detailed Government/Municipal Dashboard has been left entirely untouched, ensuring municipal workers can still rely on the sophisticated AI workflows, deduplication logic, and SLAs."
    thinking: "**Verifying Progress**\n\nIt appears the core functionality, generating the base CitizenApp with the desired camera-first behavior, is complete. I\'m now cross-referencing this against the initial user prompt. Specifically, I\'m checking that the workflow after image capture fulfills all requirements, including description and location input. The CitizenApp seems to naturally support the described 2nd step.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully simplified the Citizen-facing interface of the **Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution** prototype, optimizing it specifically for users with limited digital literacy, while keeping the complex workflows safely behind the scenes in the Government dashboard.\n\nHere is an overview of the simplified experience:\n\n- **Camera-First Landing**: When citizens open the application, they immediately land on the camera experience with a simple prompt to take a photo of the problem. No complex dashboards, categories, or analytics compete for their attention.\n- **Unified Reporting Step**: After capturing the image, the user sees a single, focused screen featuring their photo, a large \"Describe the problem\" input with a prominent **\360\237\216\244 Speak instead** voice-input button, and their auto-detected location. Technical fields like Priority, Category, and Ward have been completely removed.\n- **Abstracted Technical & AI Logic**: All references to Artificial Intelligence, confidence scores, duplicate merging, and municipal routing have been completely removed from the citizen view. \n- **Plain Language Statuses**: The complex internal statuses (e.g., *Under Review*, *Assigned*) are now translated into plain, everyday language for citizens:\n  - *Report received*\n  - *Being handled*\n  - *Work completed*\n  - *Fixed \342\200\224 Please confirm*\n- **Simplified Resolution Flow**: When a municipality marks a report as resolved, the citizen simply sees the before-and-after photos and is asked \"Is the problem fixed?\" with two massive touch targets: **\342\234\205 Yes, fixed** and **\342\235\214 No, still a problem**.\n- **Large Touch Targets & Contrast**: Every button, navigation item, and text field in the citizen view has been significantly increased in scale to accommodate individuals who struggle with fine motor control on digital devices.\n- **Language Selector**: The Profile screen has been heavily simplified, removing trust scores and analytics, replacing them with a straightforward tap-to-select language option (English, \340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215, \340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200).\n\nThe detailed Government/Municipal Dashboard has been left entirely untouched, ensuring municipal workers can still rely on the sophisticated AI workflows, deduplication logic, and SLAs."
