t change\n- Headings must change\n- Citizen instructions must change\n- Status labels must change\n- Notifications must change\n- Report flow text must change\n- Profile page must change\n- Privacy messages must change\n- Error/success messages must change\n\nThe ENTIRE citizen-facing interface should update dynamically.\n\nDo NOT translate only a few labels.\n\nCreate a centralized translation/localization object such as:\n\ntranslations = {\n  en: {...},\n  ta: {...},\n  hi: {...}\n}\n\nUse translation keys consistently throughout the citizen UI.\n\nDo NOT hardcode English text directly inside individual components when a translation key should be used.\n\nPersist the user\'s manually selected language in localStorage.\n\nIf the user manually changes the language, that language should remain selected on future visits and override GPS-based default detection.\n\nPriority:\n\n1. Previously saved user language\n2. Otherwise GPS-based default\n3. Otherwise English fallback\n\n==================================================\n3. MULTILINGUAL DUMMY DATA\n==================================================\n\nExpand the mock data significantly.\n\nThe application currently does not contain enough different situations.\n\nCreate a rich and realistic multilingual dataset.\n\nMANDATORY LANGUAGES:\n\nEnglish\nTamil\nHindi\n\nReports should contain descriptions in their original language.\n\nExamples:\n\nTamil:\n\342\200\234\340\256\252\340\256\263\340\257\215\340\256\263\340\256\277\340\256\225\340\257\215\340\256\225\340\257\201 \340\256\205\340\256\260\340\257\201\340\256\225\340\256\277\340\256\262\340\257\215 \340\256\232\340\256\276\340\256\262\340\257\210\340\256\257\340\256\277\340\256\262\340\257\215 \340\256\252\340\257\206\340\256\260\340\256\277\340\256\257 \340\256\225\340\257\201\340\256\264\340\256\277 \340\256\211\340\256\263\340\257\215\340\256\263\340\256\244\340\257\201.\342\200\235\n\nHindi:\n\342\200\234\340\244\270\340\245\215\340\244\225\340\245\202\340\244\262 \340\244\225\340\245\207 \340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\270 \340\244\270\340\244\241\340\244\274\340\244\225 \340\244\252\340\244\260 \340\244\217\340\244\225 \340\244\254\340\244\241\340\244\274\340\244\276 \340\244\227\340\244\241\340\245\215\340\244\242\340\244\276 \340\244\271\340\245\210\340\245\244\342\200\235\n\nEnglish:\n\342\200\234There is a large pothole near the bus stop.\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT translate every report into English only.\n\nThe government dashboard should demonstrate that the platform can receive reports in multiple languages.\n\nFor each report store:\n\noriginalLanguage\noriginalDescription\ntranslated/normalizedDescription if needed\nissueType\nlocation\nauthority\ndepartment\npriority\nstatus\n\nThe citizen should normally see the original language associated with their report.\n\nGovernment staff may see:\nOriginal report\n+ normalized/translated version where appropriate.\n\n==================================================\n4. EXPAND THE SCENARIO DATASET\n==================================================\n\nCreate substantially more realistic situations.\n\nDo not use only potholes.\n\nInclude at least these issue categories:\n\n- Pothole\n- Garbage accumulation\n- Overflowing drain\n- Broken streetlight\n- Open manhole\n- Damaged footpath\n- Water leakage\n- Illegal dumping\n- Fallen tree\n- Road flooding\n- Damaged traffic signal\n- Stray animal hazard\n- Public toilet maintenance\n- Waterlogging\n- Road debris\n\nCreate at least 25\342\200\22340 realistic report records.\n\nUse a mixture of:\n\n- Chennai\n- Coimbatore\n- Madurai\n- Bengaluru\n- Hyderabad\n- Delhi\n- Mumbai\n\nUse realistic Indian locations, wards, streets, municipalities, and authorities.\n\nDo not make all reports come from the same city.\n\n==================================================\n5. USE REALISTIC INDIAN AUTHORITIES\n==================================================\n\nThe existing prototype should demonstrate proper authority assignment.\n\nUse realistic authorities such as:\n\nGreater Chennai Corporation (GCC)\nChennai Metropolitan Water Supply and Sewerage Board (CMWSSB)\nTamil Nadu Highways / PWD\nRelevant Municipal Corporations\nRelevant city civic authorities\nAppropriate electricity / utility authorities\n\nExamples:\n\nPothole in Chennai\n\342\206\222 Greater Chennai Corporation\n\342\206\222 Roads / related civic department\n\nWater supply issue in Chennai\n\342\206\222 CMWSSB\n\nState highway-related issue\n\342\206\222 Relevant state highways/PWD authority\n\nDo not use a generic label such as:\n\342\200\234Government Authority\342\200\235\n\nShow the actual responsible authority.\n\n==================================================\n6. FIX EXISTING REPORT IMAGE UPLOAD ISSUES\n==================================================\n\nSome existing reports have broken or missing images.\n\nAudit ALL existing mock reports and ensure every report has a valid image reference.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Every issue card with an image must successfully display an image.\n- Every issue detail page must successfully display its associated image.\n- Government issue tables/cards should not show broken image icons.\n- Before/after images must also work.\n- If an image is missing, use a valid fallback image rather than showing a broken image.\n\nImplement a reusable image fallback component.\n\nExample logic:\n\nimage loads successfully\n\342\206\222 show image\n\nimage fails\n\342\206\222 show fallback civic image\n\342\206\222 show appropriate placeholder\n\nDo NOT allow broken image icons anywhere in the final prototype.\n\nFor mock reports, use reliable local/static assets where possible rather than unstable external URLs.\n\n==================================================\n7. FIX LANGUAGE BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nThe existing \342\200\234Language\342\200\235 button under Profile does not work.\n\nFix it.\n\nWhen clicked:\n\nOpen a language selection modal/sheet.\n\nShow:\n\n\340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\340\244\271\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\245\200\nEnglish\n\nSelecting a language should immediately update the interface.\n\nClose the modal after selection.\n\nShow a visual indicator beside the selected language.\n\nExample:\n\n\342\234\223 \340\256\244\340\256\256\340\256\277\340\256\264\340\257\215\n\nPersist the selection.\n\n==================================================\n8. FIX PRIVACY & SECURITY BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nThe existing \342\200\234Privacy & Security\342\200\235 button does not work.\n\nMake it open a real page/modal.\n\nShow:\n\n\342\200\234Privacy & Security\342\200\235\n\nInclude simple sections:\n\nIdentity\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nAadhaar\n\342\200\234Identity verification completed\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Full Aadhaar number is never displayed.\342\200\235\n\nPhoto Privacy\n\342\234\223 Faces automatically blurred in uploaded evidence\n\nPersonal Data\n\342\200\234Only necessary information is used for civic reporting.\342\200\235\n\nReport Visibility\n\342\200\234Your personal identity is not publicly displayed with civic reports.\342\200\235\n\nUse the existing privacy/face-blurring feature.\n\nKeep the page understandable and concise.\n\n==================================================\n9. FIX SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nThe existing Sign Out button does not work.\n\nImplement the complete interaction.\n\nClick:\n\nSign Out\n\nShow confirmation:\n\n\342\200\234Are you sure you want to sign out?\342\200\235\n\nButtons:\n\nCancel\nSign Out\n\nIf the user confirms:\n\n- Clear authenticated state\n- Clear mock session state\n- Return to the authentication/welcome screen\n- Do not delete the user\'s stored mock account data unless necessary\n\nAfter signing out, the next visit should require the demo authentication flow again.\n\nMake sure this works even after page refresh.\n\n==================================================\n10. GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD \342\200\224 FULL DATA DEMONSTRATION MODE\n==================================================\n\nAt the moment, there is no easy way to demonstrate the government dashboard with all system data.\n\nFix this by creating a COMPLETE DEMO DATA ENVIRONMENT for the municipal side.\n\nWhen the user opens the government dashboard, it should already contain a realistic amount of data.\n\nDo NOT show an empty dashboard.\n\nPopulate it with enough records to demonstrate:\n\n- Multiple wards\n- Multiple departments\n- Multiple authorities\n- Multiple issue categories\n- Multiple priorities\n- Multiple statuses\n- Multiple languages\n- Duplicate clusters\n- Citizen report counts\n- SLA states\n- Reopened issues\n- Resolved issues\n- Pending issues\n- In-progress issues\n- Critical issues\n- Different dates\n\nUse at least 40\342\200\22360 mock citizen reports and 20\342\200\22330 canonical civic issues.\n\n==================================================\n11. GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD OVERVIEW\n==================================================\n\nMake the overview dashboard dynamically calculate KPIs from the mock dataset.\n\nDo NOT hardcode unrelated numbers.\n\nCalculate:\n\nTotal Reports\nUnique Civic Issues\nOpen Issues\nCritical Issues\nHigh Priority Issues\nIn Progress\nResolved Today\nReopened\nSLA Breaches\nAverage Response Time\nAverage Resolution Time\nCitizen Verification Rate\n\nAll values displayed in KPI cards should correspond to the dataset.\n\n==================================================\n12. GOVERNMENT ISSUE QUEUE\n==================================================\n\nPopulate the issue table with the complete mock dataset.\n\nInclude:\n\nIssue ID\nIssue Type\nOriginal Language\nLocation\nWard\nAuthority\nDepartment\nReports\nPriority\nStatus\nAssigned Team\nSLA\nActions\n\nMake sure filtering actually changes the displayed data.\n\nFilters:\n\n- City\n- Authority\n- Department\n- Ward\n- Issue type\n- Priority\n- Status\n- Language\n- Date\n\nSearch must work.\n\nSorting must work.\n\n==================================================\n13. GOVERNMENT LIVE MAP\n==================================================\n\nPopulate the map with issue markers from the mock dataset.\n\nMarkers should reflect:\n\n- Issue location\n- Priority\n- Status\n- Issue category\n\nClicking a marker should open the corresponding issue.\n\nThe map and issue table must reference the same underlying mock data.\n\n==================================================\n14. GOVERNMENT ISSUE DETAIL\n==================================================\n\nEvery issue opened in the government dashboard must contain:\n\nIssue ID\nIssue category\nOriginal citizen language\nOriginal description\nNormalized description\nCitizen report count\nLocation\nWard\nAuthority\nDepartment\nPriority\nTrust / verification state\nCurrent status\nAssigned team\nSLA\nEvidence images\nResolution evidence\nHistory/timeline\n\nMake sure all fields correspond to the selected issue.\n\n==================================================\n15. DEMONSTRATE MULTILINGUAL REPORTS\n==================================================\n\nThe Government Dashboard should contain a mixture of:\n\nTamil reports\nHindi reports\nEnglish reports\n\nAdd a dashboard metric:\n\n\342\200\234Reports by Language\342\200\235\n\nExample:\n\nTamil \342\200\224 38%\nHindi \342\200\224 27%\nEnglish \342\200\224 35%\n\nUse the actual mock dataset to generate the chart.\n\n==================================================\n16. DEMONSTRATE DUPLICATE CLUSTERS\n==================================================\n\nCreate realistic duplicate groups.\n\nExample:\n\nCanonical Issue:\nCIV-10482\n\nReports:\n17\n\nLanguages:\nTamil\nEnglish\nTamil\nHindi\n\nShow:\n\n\342\200\23417 citizen reports consolidated into 1 civic issue\342\200\235\n\nThe government dashboard should make this easy to understand.\n\n==================================================\n17. DEMONSTRATE REOPENED ISSUES\n==================================================\n\nInclude some issues that were:\n\nResolved\n\342\206\222 Citizen rejected resolution\n\342\206\222 Reopened\n\342\206\222 Back in municipal workflow\n\nMake these visible in:\n\nIssue Queue\nIssue Detail\nAnalytics\nReopened filter\n\n==================================================\n18. DEMONSTRATE DIFFERENT MUNICIPAL SCENARIOS\n==================================================\n\nCreate examples such as:\n\nSCENARIO A:\nChennai pothole\nTamil report\n\342\206\222 Greater Chennai Corporation\n\342\206\222 Roads Department\n\nSCENARIO B:\nChennai water leakage\nTamil report\n\342\206\222 CMWSSB\n\nSCENARIO C:\nDelhi garbage accumulation\nHindi report\n\342\206\222 Relevant municipal sanitation authority\n\nSCENARIO D:\nBengaluru streetlight issue\nEnglish report\n\342\206\222 Relevant civic/electrical authority\n\nSCENARIO E:\nChennai open manhole\nTamil report\n\342\206\222 Greater Chennai Corporation\n\342\206\222 relevant department\n\nUse realistic variation.\n\n==================================================\n19. DATA CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nAll screens must use the SAME underlying mock dataset.\n\nDo not create independent hardcoded data for:\n\nDashboard\nIssue Queue\nMap\nIssue Detail\nAnalytics\n\nThey must all reference the same data model.\n\nIf an issue exists in the Issue Queue, it should exist on the map.\n\nIf its status changes, the dashboard count should update.\n\nIf its priority changes, KPI and charts should reflect it.\n\nIf a report is merged into an issue, the report count should change.\n\n==================================================\n20. DEMO DATA RESET\n==================================================\n\nAdd a small government-side development/demo control:\n\n\342\200\234Reset Demo Data\342\200\235\n\nThis should restore the initial mock dataset.\n\nDo not show this prominently to normal users.\n\nIt can be placed under:\nAdmin / Settings / Demo Controls.\n\n==================================================\n21. DATA MODEL\n==================================================\n\nUse a coherent mock data model.\n\nExample:\n\nCitizen {\n  id,\n  name,\n  language,\n  verified,\n  city\n}\n\nReport {\n  id,\n  citizenId,\n  issueId,\n  originalLanguage,\n  originalDescription,\n  image,\n  location,\n  timestamp,\n  trustScore\n}\n\nIssue {\n  id,\n  category,\n  location,\n  city,\n  ward,\n  authority,\n  department,\n  priority,\n  priorityScore,\n  status,\n  reportIds,\n  assignedTeam,\n  sla,\n  beforeImage,\n  afterImage,\n  reopened,\n  history\n}\n\nDepartment {\n  id,\n  name,\n  authority,\n  city\n}\n\nMake sure relationships are consistent.\n\n==================================================\n22. PRESERVE EXISTING CITIZEN SIMPLICITY\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT undo the previous simplification.\n\nCitizen interface should still:\n\nOpen \342\206\222 Camera\n\342\206\222 Take Photo\n\342\206\222 Describe Problem\n\342\206\222 Location\n\342\206\222 Submit\n\nDo not display:\n- AI\n- Internal workflow\n- SLA\n- Priority engine\n- Department routing logic\n- Technical confidence scores\n\nGovernment dashboard may show those details.\n\n==================================================\n23. PRESERVE PRIVACY PROTECTION\n==================================================\n\nKeep automatic face blurring.\n\nCitizen-facing:\n\342\234\223 People\342\200\231s faces are protected\n\nGovernment-facing:\nPrivacy Protected\n\nDo not expose full personal identity or full Aadhaar data.\n\n==================================================\n24. FINAL FUNCTIONALITY AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nAfter implementing all fixes, test the following:\n\n- GPS-based default language works\n- Manual language switch works\n- Tamil UI works\n- Hindi UI works\n- English UI works\n- Language persists\n- Language button works\n- Privacy & Security button works\n- Sign Out works\n- Demo authentication still works\n- Face-blurring feature still works\n- Existing report images all load\n- Broken-image fallback works\n- Government dashboard contains substantial data\n- Dashboard KPIs match the dataset\n- Filters work\n- Search works\n- Map data matches issue data\n- Issue detail matches selected issue\n- Duplicate clusters display correctly\n- Reopened issues display correctly\n- Multilingual reports appear correctly\n- Authorities are specific and realistic\n- All navigation continues to work\n\n==================================================\nFINAL PRODUCT EXPERIENCE\n==================================================\n\nThe finished prototype should demonstrate:\n\nCITIZEN SIDE:\nSimple\nCamera-first\nMultilingual\nAccessible\nPrivacy-protected\nLow cognitive load\n\nGOVERNMENT SIDE:\nData-rich\nOperational\nMulti-city\nMulti-language\nAuthority-aware\nActionable\n\nMost importantly, the entire prototype should now feel like a populated, functioning civic platform rather than a collection of static screens.\n\nDo NOT change the official product name:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    }
  }
}
