steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787830144
      nanos: 734414515
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "IMPORTANT:\nPerform a targeted FUNCTIONAL FIX on the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nDo NOT redesign the application.\nDo NOT remove existing features.\nDo NOT change the official product name.\nDo NOT change the current language implementation since it is now working.\n\nFocus ONLY on these three unresolved problems:\n\n1. Every mock issue/report needs a UNIQUE and relevant image.\n2. The Government Dashboard must be accessible and fully demonstrable.\n3. Sign Out must work completely.\n\n==================================================\n1. UNIQUE IMAGE FOR EVERY MOCK REPORT / ISSUE\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nMany or all mock reports are displaying the same image.\n\nFix the mock dataset so that EVERY report/issue has its own appropriate image.\n\nDo NOT simply reuse one generic civic image.\n\nCreate a unique image assignment for every mock issue.\n\nThe image must visually correspond to the issue category.\n\nExamples:\n\nPothole\n\342\206\222 photo of a road with a pothole\n\nGarbage accumulation\n\342\206\222 photo of garbage piled on roadside\n\nBroken streetlight\n\342\206\222 photo of damaged/non-functional streetlight\n\nOverflowing drain\n\342\206\222 photo showing overflowing drain\n\nOpen manhole\n\342\206\222 photo showing uncovered manhole\n\nDamaged footpath\n\342\206\222 photo showing broken pavement\n\nWater leakage\n\342\206\222 photo showing leaking water pipe / water accumulation\n\nFallen tree\n\342\206\222 photo showing fallen tree obstructing road\n\nRoad flooding\n\342\206\222 photo showing flooded street\n\nDamaged traffic signal\n\342\206\222 photo showing damaged traffic signal\n\nPublic toilet issue\n\342\206\222 photo showing public toilet maintenance problem\n\nRoad debris\n\342\206\222 photo showing construction/road debris\n\n==================================================\nIMAGE DATA MODEL\n==================================================\n\nEvery REPORT must have its own image reference.\n\nExample:\n\nreport_001 \342\206\222 pothole_01.jpg\nreport_002 \342\206\222 garbage_01.jpg\nreport_003 \342\206\222 streetlight_01.jpg\nreport_004 \342\206\222 drain_01.jpg\n\nDo NOT assign:\n\nreport_001 \342\206\222 same-image.jpg\nreport_002 \342\206\222 same-image.jpg\nreport_003 \342\206\222 same-image.jpg\n\nIf several citizen reports belong to the SAME CANONICAL CIVIC ISSUE, they may share the same underlying physical issue context, BUT the individual reports should preferably have different supporting photographs where appropriate.\n\nFor example:\n\nCIV-10482\n\342\200\234Large pothole near bus stop\342\200\235\n\ncould have:\n\nReport R001 \342\206\222 photo of pothole from one angle\nReport R002 \342\206\222 photo of same pothole from another angle\nReport R003 \342\206\222 closer photo of same pothole\n\nDo not duplicate identical images across unrelated issues.\n\n==================================================\nIMAGE RELIABILITY\n==================================================\n\nUse reliable LOCAL / STATIC image assets wherever possible.\n\nAvoid unstable external image URLs that can randomly fail.\n\nEvery image must:\n- Load successfully\n- Have a relevant fallback\n- Be used consistently across the application\n\nAudit ALL existing mock records.\n\nThere must be ZERO broken images.\n\nIf an image cannot be loaded:\n\n\342\206\222 automatically use a category-specific fallback image\n\nDo NOT display a broken image icon.\n\n==================================================\n2. GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD ACCESS\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Government Dashboard exists in the design but I cannot actually access it.\n\nFix this as a PRIORITY.\n\nCreate a clearly accessible Government / Municipal entry point.\n\nThere must be a complete working path:\n\nLanding / Authentication\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nThe dashboard must NOT be hidden behind an inaccessible route.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT LOGIN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a simple DEMO government login.\n\nDo NOT require a real backend authentication system.\n\nUse mock authentication/local state.\n\nShow:\n\n\342\200\234Municipal Administration Login\342\200\235\n\nFields:\n\nEmployee ID / Official Email\nPassword\n\nButton:\n\n\342\200\234Sign In\342\200\235\n\nFor the prototype, allow a clearly documented demo credential such as:\n\nEmployee ID:\nadmin@gov.demo\n\nPassword:\ndemo123\n\nOR provide a visible:\n\n\342\200\234Enter Demo Dashboard\342\200\235\n\nbutton.\n\nThe purpose is to make the government dashboard immediately demonstrable to judges.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT ACCESS FROM THE MAIN APP\n==================================================\n\nProvide a subtle but visible way to access the government side.\n\nFor example on the landing/authentication screen:\n\n\342\200\234Municipal Staff Login\342\200\235\n\nThis should open the Government Login.\n\nDo NOT put a prominent government-login button inside the normal citizen reporting flow.\n\nCitizen experience must remain simple.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT DASHBOARD ROUTING\n==================================================\n\nAfter successful government demo login:\n\n\342\206\222 Open Government Overview Dashboard.\n\nMake sure routing works even after refresh.\n\nUse a separate government session state.\n\nExample:\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated = true\n\nStore using localStorage.\n\nIf governmentAuthenticated is true:\n\n\342\206\222 open Government Dashboard\n\nIf false:\n\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT DASHBOARD MUST CONTAIN DATA\n==================================================\n\nWhen opened, the Government Dashboard must NOT be empty.\n\nPopulate it using the existing mock dataset.\n\nShow:\n\nTotal Reports\nUnique Civic Issues\nOpen Issues\nCritical Issues\nHigh Priority\nIn Progress\nResolved\nReopened\nSLA Breaches\nAverage Resolution Time\n\nThe numbers must be generated from the mock dataset rather than manually typed unrelated numbers.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nMake sure the following government pages are actually accessible:\n\nOverview\nLive Issue Map\nIssue Queue\nIssue Details\nDepartments\nField Operations\nSLA & Escalations\nCitizen Reports\nAnalytics\nRecurring Hotspots\nSettings\n\nEach navigation item must lead somewhere meaningful.\n\nNo dead buttons.\n\nNo placeholder pages.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT DASHBOARD DEMO DATA\n==================================================\n\nEnsure the dashboard visibly demonstrates:\n\n- Multiple cities\n- Multiple Indian authorities\n- Multiple departments\n- Tamil reports\n- Hindi reports\n- English reports\n- Multiple civic issue types\n- Different priorities\n- Different statuses\n- Duplicate report clusters\n- Reopened issues\n- SLA breaches\n- Resolved issues\n- Reports with unique images\n\nUse the same central mock dataset throughout.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT ISSUE DETAIL\n==================================================\n\nOpening any issue from the Government Dashboard should show:\n\nIssue ID\nIssue type\nOriginal citizen language\nOriginal description\nImage\nLocation\nWard\nAuthority\nDepartment\nPriority\nCitizen report count\nAssigned team\nSLA\nStatus\nBefore image\nAfter image\nIssue history\n\nMake sure the displayed image corresponds to that specific issue.\n\n==================================================\n3. FIX SIGN OUT COMPLETELY\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Sign Out button still does not work.\n\nAudit the current authentication implementation and fix it rather than adding another disconnected sign-out button.\n\nCitizen sign-out flow:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation dialog\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\nThen:\n\n- authenticated = false\n- Clear persistent citizen session state\n- Redirect to citizen authentication/welcome screen\n- Ensure dashboard cannot be accessed as an authenticated user\n\nThe profile avatar must disappear after sign-out.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nAlso implement government sign-out.\n\nGovernment Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 governmentAuthenticated = false\n\342\206\222 Return to Government Login\n\nDo not leave government dashboard accessible after sign-out.\n\n==================================================\nIMPORTANT AUTHENTICATION RULE\n==================================================\n\nKeep citizen and government authentication states SEPARATE.\n\nCitizen:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated\n\nGovernment:\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated\n\nSigning out of one must NOT accidentally sign out the other.\n\n==================================================\n4. DEMO ACCOUNT SELECTOR\n==================================================\n\nTo make the prototype easy to demonstrate, add optional demo account shortcuts.\n\nCitizen Demo:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Demo Citizen\342\200\235\n\nGovernment Demo:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Municipal Officer\342\200\235\n\nThese should bypass real authentication requirements and directly load the appropriate environment.\n\nLabel clearly:\n\n\342\200\234Demo Mode\342\200\235\n\nThis is for hackathon presentation only.\n\n==================================================\n5. DO NOT BREAK EXISTING FEATURES\n==================================================\n\nThe following are already working and must remain working:\n\n- GPS-based default language\n- Manual language switching\n- Tamil UI\n- Hindi UI\n- English UI\n- Persistent citizen account\n- Aadhaar demo verification\n- Camera-first citizen flow\n- Offline reporting simulation\n- Privacy / face blurring\n- Citizen report tracking\n- Citizen verification / reopening\n- AI functionality in the backend/mock logic\n- Government-side detailed intelligence\n- Existing navigation\n- Existing visual styling\n\nDo not expose AI or internal workflow information on the citizen side.\n\n==================================================\n6. FINAL FUNCTIONAL TEST\n==================================================\n\nAfter making the changes, test these exact flows:\n\nFLOW A \342\200\224 CITIZEN\n\nOpen app\n\342\206\222 Citizen authentication\n\342\206\222 Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Welcome/authentication screen\n\nFLOW B \342\200\224 GOVERNMENT\n\nOpen app\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Issue Queue\n\342\206\222 Open Issue\n\342\206\222 Return Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Government Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nFLOW C \342\200\224 IMAGE\n\nOpen Government Issue Queue\n\342\206\222 Open 10 different issues\n\342\206\222 Verify each displays a DIFFERENT relevant image\n\nFLOW D \342\200\224 DATA\n\nOpen Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Verify KPI values exist\n\342\206\222 Open Live Map\n\342\206\222 Verify issues appear\n\342\206\222 Open Issue Queue\n\342\206\222 Verify same issues exist\n\342\206\222 Open Issue Detail\n\342\206\222 Verify matching image/data\n\342\206\222 Open Analytics\n\342\206\222 Verify charts use the same dataset\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe finished prototype must have:\n\n\342\234\223 Unique relevant images across the mock dataset\n\342\234\223 No broken images\n\342\234\223 A clearly accessible Government Login\n\342\234\223 A fully accessible Government Dashboard\n\342\234\223 Rich government-side demo data\n\342\234\223 Working citizen Sign Out\n\342\234\223 Working government Sign Out\n\342\234\223 Separate citizen/government sessions\n\342\234\223 Consistent shared mock data\n\342\234\223 No dead navigation paths\n\nDo NOT redesign the UI.\nDo NOT change the product name.\n\nOfficial product name:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    items {
      text: "IMPORTANT:\nPerform a targeted FUNCTIONAL FIX on the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nDo NOT redesign the application.\nDo NOT remove existing features.\nDo NOT change the official product name.\nDo NOT change the current language implementation since it is now working.\n\nFocus ONLY on these three unresolved problems:\n\n1. Every mock issue/report needs a UNIQUE and relevant image.\n2. The Government Dashboard must be accessible and fully demonstrable.\n3. Sign Out must work completely.\n\n==================================================\n1. UNIQUE IMAGE FOR EVERY MOCK REPORT / ISSUE\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nMany or all mock reports are displaying the same image.\n\nFix the mock dataset so that EVERY report/issue has its own appropriate image.\n\nDo NOT simply reuse one generic civic image.\n\nCreate a unique image assignment for every mock issue.\n\nThe image must visually correspond to the issue category.\n\nExamples:\n\nPothole\n\342\206\222 photo of a road with a pothole\n\nGarbage accumulation\n\342\206\222 photo of garbage piled on roadside\n\nBroken streetlight\n\342\206\222 photo of damaged/non-functional streetlight\n\nOverflowing drain\n\342\206\222 photo showing overflowing drain\n\nOpen manhole\n\342\206\222 photo showing uncovered manhole\n\nDamaged footpath\n\342\206\222 photo showing broken pavement\n\nWater leakage\n\342\206\222 photo showing leaking water pipe / water accumulation\n\nFallen tree\n\342\206\222 photo showing fallen tree obstructing road\n\nRoad flooding\n\342\206\222 photo showing flooded street\n\nDamaged traffic signal\n\342\206\222 photo showing damaged traffic signal\n\nPublic toilet issue\n\342\206\222 photo showing public toilet maintenance problem\n\nRoad debris\n\342\206\222 photo showing construction/road debris\n\n==================================================\nIMAGE DATA MODEL\n==================================================\n\nEvery REPORT must have its own image reference.\n\nExample:\n\nreport_001 \342\206\222 pothole_01.jpg\nreport_002 \342\206\222 garbage_01.jpg\nreport_003 \342\206\222 streetlight_01.jpg\nreport_004 \342\206\222 drain_01.jpg\n\nDo NOT assign:\n\nreport_001 \342\206\222 same-image.jpg\nreport_002 \342\206\222 same-image.jpg\nreport_003 \342\206\222 same-image.jpg\n\nIf several citizen reports belong to the SAME CANONICAL CIVIC ISSUE, they may share the same underlying physical issue context, BUT the individual reports should preferably have different supporting photographs where appropriate.\n\nFor example:\n\nCIV-10482\n\342\200\234Large pothole near bus stop\342\200\235\n\ncould have:\n\nReport R001 \342\206\222 photo of pothole from one angle\nReport R002 \342\206\222 photo of same pothole from another angle\nReport R003 \342\206\222 closer photo of same pothole\n\nDo not duplicate identical images across unrelated issues.\n\n==================================================\nIMAGE RELIABILITY\n==================================================\n\nUse reliable LOCAL / STATIC image assets wherever possible.\n\nAvoid unstable external image URLs that can randomly fail.\n\nEvery image must:\n- Load successfully\n- Have a relevant fallback\n- Be used consistently across the application\n\nAudit ALL existing mock records.\n\nThere must be ZERO broken images.\n\nIf an image cannot be loaded:\n\n\342\206\222 automatically use a category-specific fallback image\n\nDo NOT display a broken image icon.\n\n==================================================\n2. GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD ACCESS\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Government Dashboard exists in the design but I cannot actually access it.\n\nFix this as a PRIORITY.\n\nCreate a clearly accessible Government / Municipal entry point.\n\nThere must be a complete working path:\n\nLanding / Authentication\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nThe dashboard must NOT be hidden behind an inaccessible route.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT LOGIN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a simple DEMO government login.\n\nDo NOT require a real backend authentication system.\n\nUse mock authentication/local state.\n\nShow:\n\n\342\200\234Municipal Administration Login\342\200\235\n\nFields:\n\nEmployee ID / Official Email\nPassword\n\nButton:\n\n\342\200\234Sign In\342\200\235\n\nFor the prototype, allow a clearly documented demo credential such as:\n\nEmployee ID:\nadmin@gov.demo\n\nPassword:\ndemo123\n\nOR provide a visible:\n\n\342\200\234Enter Demo Dashboard\342\200\235\n\nbutton.\n\nThe purpose is to make the government dashboard immediately demonstrable to judges.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT ACCESS FROM THE MAIN APP\n==================================================\n\nProvide a subtle but visible way to access the government side.\n\nFor example on the landing/authentication screen:\n\n\342\200\234Municipal Staff Login\342\200\235\n\nThis should open the Government Login.\n\nDo NOT put a prominent government-login button inside the normal citizen reporting flow.\n\nCitizen experience must remain simple.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT DASHBOARD ROUTING\n==================================================\n\nAfter successful government demo login:\n\n\342\206\222 Open Government Overview Dashboard.\n\nMake sure routing works even after refresh.\n\nUse a separate government session state.\n\nExample:\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated = true\n\nStore using localStorage.\n\nIf governmentAuthenticated is true:\n\n\342\206\222 open Government Dashboard\n\nIf false:\n\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT DASHBOARD MUST CONTAIN DATA\n==================================================\n\nWhen opened, the Government Dashboard must NOT be empty.\n\nPopulate it using the existing mock dataset.\n\nShow:\n\nTotal Reports\nUnique Civic Issues\nOpen Issues\nCritical Issues\nHigh Priority\nIn Progress\nResolved\nReopened\nSLA Breaches\nAverage Resolution Time\n\nThe numbers must be generated from the mock dataset rather than manually typed unrelated numbers.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nMake sure the following government pages are actually accessible:\n\nOverview\nLive Issue Map\nIssue Queue\nIssue Details\nDepartments\nField Operations\nSLA & Escalations\nCitizen Reports\nAnalytics\nRecurring Hotspots\nSettings\n\nEach navigation item must lead somewhere meaningful.\n\nNo dead buttons.\n\nNo placeholder pages.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT DASHBOARD DEMO DATA\n==================================================\n\nEnsure the dashboard visibly demonstrates:\n\n- Multiple cities\n- Multiple Indian authorities\n- Multiple departments\n- Tamil reports\n- Hindi reports\n- English reports\n- Multiple civic issue types\n- Different priorities\n- Different statuses\n- Duplicate report clusters\n- Reopened issues\n- SLA breaches\n- Resolved issues\n- Reports with unique images\n\nUse the same central mock dataset throughout.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT ISSUE DETAIL\n==================================================\n\nOpening any issue from the Government Dashboard should show:\n\nIssue ID\nIssue type\nOriginal citizen language\nOriginal description\nImage\nLocation\nWard\nAuthority\nDepartment\nPriority\nCitizen report count\nAssigned team\nSLA\nStatus\nBefore image\nAfter image\nIssue history\n\nMake sure the displayed image corresponds to that specific issue.\n\n==================================================\n3. FIX SIGN OUT COMPLETELY\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Sign Out button still does not work.\n\nAudit the current authentication implementation and fix it rather than adding another disconnected sign-out button.\n\nCitizen sign-out flow:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation dialog\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\nThen:\n\n- authenticated = false\n- Clear persistent citizen session state\n- Redirect to citizen authentication/welcome screen\n- Ensure dashboard cannot be accessed as an authenticated user\n\nThe profile avatar must disappear after sign-out.\n\n==================================================\nGOVERNMENT SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nAlso implement government sign-out.\n\nGovernment Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 governmentAuthenticated = false\n\342\206\222 Return to Government Login\n\nDo not leave government dashboard accessible after sign-out.\n\n==================================================\nIMPORTANT AUTHENTICATION RULE\n==================================================\n\nKeep citizen and government authentication states SEPARATE.\n\nCitizen:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated\n\nGovernment:\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated\n\nSigning out of one must NOT accidentally sign out the other.\n\n==================================================\n4. DEMO ACCOUNT SELECTOR\n==================================================\n\nTo make the prototype easy to demonstrate, add optional demo account shortcuts.\n\nCitizen Demo:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Demo Citizen\342\200\235\n\nGovernment Demo:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Municipal Officer\342\200\235\n\nThese should bypass real authentication requirements and directly load the appropriate environment.\n\nLabel clearly:\n\n\342\200\234Demo Mode\342\200\235\n\nThis is for hackathon presentation only.\n\n==================================================\n5. DO NOT BREAK EXISTING FEATURES\n==================================================\n\nThe following are already working and must remain working:\n\n- GPS-based default language\n- Manual language switching\n- Tamil UI\n- Hindi UI\n- English UI\n- Persistent citizen account\n- Aadhaar demo verification\n- Camera-first citizen flow\n- Offline reporting simulation\n- Privacy / face blurring\n- Citizen report tracking\n- Citizen verification / reopening\n- AI functionality in the backend/mock logic\n- Government-side detailed intelligence\n- Existing navigation\n- Existing visual styling\n\nDo not expose AI or internal workflow information on the citizen side.\n\n==================================================\n6. FINAL FUNCTIONAL TEST\n==================================================\n\nAfter making the changes, test these exact flows:\n\nFLOW A \342\200\224 CITIZEN\n\nOpen app\n\342\206\222 Citizen authentication\n\342\206\222 Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Welcome/authentication screen\n\nFLOW B \342\200\224 GOVERNMENT\n\nOpen app\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Issue Queue\n\342\206\222 Open Issue\n\342\206\222 Return Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Government Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nFLOW C \342\200\224 IMAGE\n\nOpen Government Issue Queue\n\342\206\222 Open 10 different issues\n\342\206\222 Verify each displays a DIFFERENT relevant image\n\nFLOW D \342\200\224 DATA\n\nOpen Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Verify KPI values exist\n\342\206\222 Open Live Map\n\342\206\222 Verify issues appear\n\342\206\222 Open Issue Queue\n\342\206\222 Verify same issues exist\n\342\206\222 Open Issue Detail\n\342\206\222 Verify matching image/data\n\342\206\222 Open Analytics\n\342\206\222 Verify charts use the same dataset\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe finished prototype must have:\n\n\342\234\223 Unique relevant images across the mock dataset\n\342\234\223 No broken images\n\342\234\223 A clearly accessible Government Login\n\342\234\223 A fully accessible Government Dashboard\n\342\234\223 Rich government-side demo data\n\342\234\223 Working citizen Sign Out\n\342\234\223 Working government Sign Out\n\342\234\223 Separate citizen/government sessions\n\342\234\223 Consistent shared mock data\n\342\234\223 No dead navigation paths\n\nDo NOT redesign the UI.\nDo NOT change the product name.\n\nOfficial product name:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    }
  }
}
