    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "FIX THE AUTHENTICATION / LOGOUT / ROLE SWITCHING ISSUE in the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Citizen Dashboard and Government Dashboard both now display data correctly.\n\nHowever:\n\n- If I enter the Citizen Dashboard, I cannot successfully log out and access the Government Dashboard.\n- If I enter the Government Dashboard, I cannot successfully log out and access the Citizen Dashboard.\n- The application appears to maintain one global authenticated state instead of properly separating citizen and government sessions.\n\nDO NOT redesign the UI.\nDO NOT remove existing data.\nDO NOT change the existing language implementation.\nDO NOT change the existing dashboard designs.\n\nONLY fix authentication, logout, routing and role/session separation.\n\n==================================================\n1. SEPARATE CITIZEN AND GOVERNMENT AUTHENTICATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate completely independent authentication states.\n\nUse:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated\n\nand\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated\n\nDo NOT use a single global variable such as:\n\nauthenticated = true\n\nDo NOT allow one role\'s authentication state to automatically authenticate the other role.\n\nThe two environments must be independent.\n\n==================================================\n2. CITIZEN LOGIN\n==================================================\n\nWhen a citizen authenticates:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated = true\n\nStore the citizen session persistently using localStorage.\n\nExample:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated = true\ncivic_citizen_user = {...}\n\nThe citizen should then be taken to:\n\nCITIZEN DASHBOARD\n\n==================================================\n3. GOVERNMENT LOGIN\n==================================================\n\nWhen government staff authenticate:\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated = true\n\nStore separately:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated = true\ncivic_government_user = {...}\n\nThe government user should then be taken to:\n\nGOVERNMENT DASHBOARD\n\n==================================================\n4. CITIZEN SIGN OUT MUST WORK\n==================================================\n\nCitizen profile:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\nWhen confirmed:\n\nSet:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated = false\n\nRemove the citizen session only.\n\nThen redirect to:\n\nCITIZEN AUTHENTICATION / WELCOME SCREEN\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated\n\nIf a government session exists, it must remain intact.\n\n==================================================\n5. GOVERNMENT SIGN OUT MUST WORK\n==================================================\n\nGovernment profile:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\nWhen confirmed:\n\nSet:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated = false\n\nRemove the government session only.\n\nThen redirect to:\n\nGOVERNMENT LOGIN\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated\n\n==================================================\n6. ROLE-AWARE ROUTING\n==================================================\n\nThe router must know which environment the user is entering.\n\nCitizen routes:\n\n/citizen\n/citizen/home\n/citizen/reports\n/citizen/report\n/citizen/profile\n\nGovernment routes:\n\n/government\n/government/dashboard\n/government/issues\n/government/map\n/government/analytics\n/government/settings\n\nDo not allow:\n\nCitizen \342\206\222 Government dashboard without government authentication.\n\nDo not allow:\n\nGovernment \342\206\222 Citizen private dashboard without citizen authentication.\n\n==================================================\n7. SWITCHING BETWEEN THE TWO FOR THE HACKATHON DEMO\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe prototype needs to allow me to easily demonstrate BOTH sides.\n\nCreate a clear entry point for:\n\n\342\200\234Citizen\342\200\235\n\nand\n\n\342\200\234Municipal Staff\342\200\235\n\non the appropriate welcome/authentication screen.\n\nExample:\n\n------------------------------\nCrowd Sourced Civic Issue\nReporting and Resolution\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n------------------------------\n\nSelecting:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen authentication\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nSelecting:\n\nMunicipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government authentication\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nDo NOT place this selector prominently inside the normal citizen experience.\n\n==================================================\n8. LOGOUT \342\206\222 SWITCH ROLE FLOW\n==================================================\n\nThe following exact flows MUST work:\n\nFLOW A:\n\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen Welcome/Login\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nFLOW B:\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Authentication\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nBoth flows must work without refreshing the browser or clearing all application data.\n\n==================================================\n9. DEMO MODE\n==================================================\n\nAdd two clearly labelled demo shortcuts:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Demo Citizen\342\200\235\n\nand\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Municipal Officer\342\200\235\n\nThese should immediately establish the appropriate session.\n\nDemo Citizen:\n\342\206\222 citizenAuthenticated = true\n\nDemo Government:\n\342\206\222 governmentAuthenticated = true\n\nDo NOT make these shortcuts interfere with each other\'s authentication state.\n\n==================================================\n10. PERSISTENT SESSIONS\n==================================================\n\nIf the citizen refreshes the page:\n\nIf:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated = true\n\n\342\206\222 restore Citizen Dashboard.\n\nIf the government session exists:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated = true\n\n\342\206\222 restore Government Dashboard.\n\nHowever, NEVER automatically switch roles.\n\nThe application must know which route/environment the user is currently in.\n\n==================================================\n11. CURRENT ROLE\n==================================================\n\nCreate an explicit current-role value such as:\n\ncurrentRole = \"citizen\"\n\nor\n\ncurrentRole = \"government\"\n\nUse this only for routing/UI context.\n\nPossible localStorage:\n\ncivic_current_role = \"citizen\"\n\nor\n\ncivic_current_role = \"government\"\n\nWhen signing out, clear the current role.\n\nDo NOT use currentRole as the only authentication mechanism.\n\nA role must still have its corresponding authenticated state.\n\n==================================================\n12. PREVENT AUTHENTICATION LEAKAGE\n==================================================\n\nAudit the entire application for code such as:\n\nauthenticated\nisLoggedIn\nuser\nsession\ncurrentUser\n\nthat is shared between citizen and government environments.\n\nSeparate them where necessary.\n\nThe following must be independently stored:\n\nCitizen user\nCitizen authentication\nGovernment user\nGovernment authentication\nCurrent role\n\n==================================================\n13. PROFILE UI\n==================================================\n\nCitizen profile should display:\n\nArun Kumar\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nGovernment profile should display:\n\nPriya Raman\n\342\234\223 Municipal Officer\nRoads Department\n\nDo not mix user data between the two roles.\n\nWhen switching roles, the correct profile must appear automatically.\n\n==================================================\n14. PROTECT DASHBOARD ROUTES\n==================================================\n\nIf a user attempts to open the Government Dashboard without:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated = true\n\nredirect them to:\n\nGovernment Login\n\nIf a user attempts to open the Citizen Dashboard without:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated = true\n\nredirect them to:\n\nCitizen Authentication\n\nDo not show the dashboard and then ask for login afterward.\n\n==================================================\n15. DO NOT CLEAR APPLICATION DATA DURING LOGOUT\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nSigning out should remove ONLY the authentication/session state.\n\nDo NOT delete:\n\n- Mock civic reports\n- Government dashboard data\n- Citizen profile data\n- Language preference\n- Demo dataset\n- Images\n- Issue history\n\nThe user should be able to sign out and immediately enter the other environment with all data still available.\n\n==================================================\n16. FINAL TEST\n==================================================\n\nTest all of the following before finishing:\n\nTEST 1:\nCitizen Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\nTEST 2:\nGovernment Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nTEST 3:\nCitizen Login\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nTEST 4:\nGovernment Login\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nTEST 5:\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Refresh\n\342\206\222 Still authenticated\n\nTEST 6:\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Refresh\n\342\206\222 Still authenticated\n\nTEST 7:\nCitizen Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government session/data should NOT be destroyed\n\nTEST 8:\nGovernment Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen session/data should NOT be destroyed\n\nTEST 9:\nOpening /government/dashboard while not authenticated\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nTEST 10:\nOpening /citizen/home while not authenticated\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe application must behave as TWO connected but independent environments:\n\n              CROWD SOURCED CIVIC ISSUE\n              REPORTING AND RESOLUTION\n                         \342\224\202\n              \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n              \342\224\202                     \342\224\202\n           CITIZEN              GOVERNMENT\n           SESSION                SESSION\n              \342\224\202                     \342\224\202\n        Citizen Dashboard     Government Dashboard\n              \342\224\202                     \342\224\202\n          Sign Out              Sign Out\n              \342\224\202                     \342\224\202\n         Citizen Login       Government Login\n\nSigning out of one role must never break access to the other.\n\nThe final result must let me demonstrate:\n\nCitizen Side\n\342\206\222 Sign out\n\342\206\222 Government Side\n\342\206\222 Sign out\n\342\206\222 Citizen Side\n\nsmoothly, without manually clearing browser storage, refreshing repeatedly, or restarting the application."
    items {
      text: "FIX THE AUTHENTICATION / LOGOUT / ROLE SWITCHING ISSUE in the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Citizen Dashboard and Government Dashboard both now display data correctly.\n\nHowever:\n\n- If I enter the Citizen Dashboard, I cannot successfully log out and access the Government Dashboard.\n- If I enter the Government Dashboard, I cannot successfully log out and access the Citizen Dashboard.\n- The application appears to maintain one global authenticated state instead of properly separating citizen and government sessions.\n\nDO NOT redesign the UI.\nDO NOT remove existing data.\nDO NOT change the existing language implementation.\nDO NOT change the existing dashboard designs.\n\nONLY fix authentication, logout, routing and role/session separation.\n\n==================================================\n1. SEPARATE CITIZEN AND GOVERNMENT AUTHENTICATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate completely independent authentication states.\n\nUse:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated\n\nand\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated\n\nDo NOT use a single global variable such as:\n\nauthenticated = true\n\nDo NOT allow one role\'s authentication state to automatically authenticate the other role.\n\nThe two environments must be independent.\n\n==================================================\n2. CITIZEN LOGIN\n==================================================\n\nWhen a citizen authenticates:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated = true\n\nStore the citizen session persistently using localStorage.\n\nExample:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated = true\ncivic_citizen_user = {...}\n\nThe citizen should then be taken to:\n\nCITIZEN DASHBOARD\n\n==================================================\n3. GOVERNMENT LOGIN\n==================================================\n\nWhen government staff authenticate:\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated = true\n\nStore separately:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated = true\ncivic_government_user = {...}\n\nThe government user should then be taken to:\n\nGOVERNMENT DASHBOARD\n\n==================================================\n4. CITIZEN SIGN OUT MUST WORK\n==================================================\n\nCitizen profile:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\nWhen confirmed:\n\nSet:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated = false\n\nRemove the citizen session only.\n\nThen redirect to:\n\nCITIZEN AUTHENTICATION / WELCOME SCREEN\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated\n\nIf a government session exists, it must remain intact.\n\n==================================================\n5. GOVERNMENT SIGN OUT MUST WORK\n==================================================\n\nGovernment profile:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\nWhen confirmed:\n\nSet:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated = false\n\nRemove the government session only.\n\nThen redirect to:\n\nGOVERNMENT LOGIN\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT modify:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated\n\n==================================================\n6. ROLE-AWARE ROUTING\n==================================================\n\nThe router must know which environment the user is entering.\n\nCitizen routes:\n\n/citizen\n/citizen/home\n/citizen/reports\n/citizen/report\n/citizen/profile\n\nGovernment routes:\n\n/government\n/government/dashboard\n/government/issues\n/government/map\n/government/analytics\n/government/settings\n\nDo not allow:\n\nCitizen \342\206\222 Government dashboard without government authentication.\n\nDo not allow:\n\nGovernment \342\206\222 Citizen private dashboard without citizen authentication.\n\n==================================================\n7. SWITCHING BETWEEN THE TWO FOR THE HACKATHON DEMO\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe prototype needs to allow me to easily demonstrate BOTH sides.\n\nCreate a clear entry point for:\n\n\342\200\234Citizen\342\200\235\n\nand\n\n\342\200\234Municipal Staff\342\200\235\n\non the appropriate welcome/authentication screen.\n\nExample:\n\n------------------------------\nCrowd Sourced Civic Issue\nReporting and Resolution\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n------------------------------\n\nSelecting:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen authentication\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nSelecting:\n\nMunicipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government authentication\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nDo NOT place this selector prominently inside the normal citizen experience.\n\n==================================================\n8. LOGOUT \342\206\222 SWITCH ROLE FLOW\n==================================================\n\nThe following exact flows MUST work:\n\nFLOW A:\n\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen Welcome/Login\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nFLOW B:\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Authentication\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nBoth flows must work without refreshing the browser or clearing all application data.\n\n==================================================\n9. DEMO MODE\n==================================================\n\nAdd two clearly labelled demo shortcuts:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Demo Citizen\342\200\235\n\nand\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Municipal Officer\342\200\235\n\nThese should immediately establish the appropriate session.\n\nDemo Citizen:\n\342\206\222 citizenAuthenticated = true\n\nDemo Government:\n\342\206\222 governmentAuthenticated = true\n\nDo NOT make these shortcuts interfere with each other\'s authentication state.\n\n==================================================\n10. PERSISTENT SESSIONS\n==================================================\n\nIf the citizen refreshes the page:\n\nIf:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated = true\n\n\342\206\222 restore Citizen Dashboard.\n\nIf the government session exists:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated = true\n\n\342\206\222 restore Government Dashboard.\n\nHowever, NEVER automatically switch roles.\n\nThe application must know which route/environment the user is currently in.\n\n==================================================\n11. CURRENT ROLE\n==================================================\n\nCreate an explicit current-role value such as:\n\ncurrentRole = \"citizen\"\n\nor\n\ncurrentRole = \"government\"\n\nUse this only for routing/UI context.\n\nPossible localStorage:\n\ncivic_current_role = \"citizen\"\n\nor\n\ncivic_current_role = \"government\"\n\nWhen signing out, clear the current role.\n\nDo NOT use currentRole as the only authentication mechanism.\n\nA role must still have its corresponding authenticated state.\n\n==================================================\n12. PREVENT AUTHENTICATION LEAKAGE\n==================================================\n\nAudit the entire application for code such as:\n\nauthenticated\nisLoggedIn\nuser\nsession\ncurrentUser\n\nthat is shared between citizen and government environments.\n\nSeparate them where necessary.\n\nThe following must be independently stored:\n\nCitizen user\nCitizen authentication\nGovernment user\nGovernment authentication\nCurrent role\n\n==================================================\n13. PROFILE UI\n==================================================\n\nCitizen profile should display:\n\nArun Kumar\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nGovernment profile should display:\n\nPriya Raman\n\342\234\223 Municipal Officer\nRoads Department\n\nDo not mix user data between the two roles.\n\nWhen switching roles, the correct profile must appear automatically.\n\n==================================================\n14. PROTECT DASHBOARD ROUTES\n==================================================\n\nIf a user attempts to open the Government Dashboard without:\n\ncivic_government_authenticated = true\n\nredirect them to:\n\nGovernment Login\n\nIf a user attempts to open the Citizen Dashboard without:\n\ncivic_citizen_authenticated = true\n\nredirect them to:\n\nCitizen Authentication\n\nDo not show the dashboard and then ask for login afterward.\n\n==================================================\n15. DO NOT CLEAR APPLICATION DATA DURING LOGOUT\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nSigning out should remove ONLY the authentication/session state.\n\nDo NOT delete:\n\n- Mock civic reports\n- Government dashboard data\n- Citizen profile data\n- Language preference\n- Demo dataset\n- Images\n- Issue history\n\nThe user should be able to sign out and immediately enter the other environment with all data still available.\n\n==================================================\n16. FINAL TEST\n==================================================\n\nTest all of the following before finishing:\n\nTEST 1:\nCitizen Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\nTEST 2:\nGovernment Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nTEST 3:\nCitizen Login\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nTEST 4:\nGovernment Login\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nTEST 5:\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Refresh\n\342\206\222 Still authenticated\n\nTEST 6:\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Refresh\n\342\206\222 Still authenticated\n\nTEST 7:\nCitizen Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government session/data should NOT be destroyed\n\nTEST 8:\nGovernment Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen session/data should NOT be destroyed\n\nTEST 9:\nOpening /government/dashboard while not authenticated\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nTEST 10:\nOpening /citizen/home while not authenticated\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe application must behave as TWO connected but independent environments:\n\n              CROWD SOURCED CIVIC ISSUE\n              REPORTING AND RESOLUTION\n                         \342\224\202\n              \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n              \342\224\202                     \342\224\202\n           CITIZEN              GOVERNMENT\n           SESSION                SESSION\n              \342\224\202                     \342\224\202\n        Citizen Dashboard     Government Dashboard\n              \342\224\202                     \342\224\202\n          Sign Out              Sign Out\n              \342\224\202                     \342\224\202\n         Citizen Login       Government Login\n\nSigning out of one role must never break access to the other.\n\nThe final result must let me demonstrate:\n\nCitizen Side\n\342\206\222 Sign out\n\342\206\222 Government Side\n\342\206\222 Sign out\n\342\206\222 Citizen Side\n\nsmoothly, without manually clearing browser storage, refreshing repeatedly, or restarting the application."
    }
  }
}
