steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787838129
      nanos: 564153417
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "IMPORTANT:\nPerform a targeted FUNCTIONAL FIX and enhancement on the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nDo NOT redesign the existing application.\nDo NOT remove existing features.\nPreserve the current visual identity, citizen interface, government dashboard, authentication, multilingual support, privacy protection, mock data, and existing workflows.\n\nThere are TWO critical problems to fix:\n\n1. I still cannot exit one authenticated environment and access the other login option.\n2. The Government Dashboard map is not functioning.\n\nAddress both completely.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 FIX ROLE EXIT / LOGIN SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nAfter entering either the Citizen Dashboard or Government Dashboard, I cannot properly back out to choose the other environment.\n\nThe application appears to trap the user inside the currently authenticated role.\n\nI need a reliable way to:\n\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out / Exit\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nAND:\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out / Exit\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\n==================================================\n1. CREATE A ROLE SELECTION SCREEN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a clean entry screen:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235\n\nChoose how you want to continue:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nThis must be accessible after signing out from either environment.\n\nKeep this screen simple.\n\nDo not expose it inside the normal citizen workflow.\n\n==================================================\n2. CITIZEN SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nCitizen:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\nThen:\n\n- Clear citizen authentication state\n- Clear current role\n- Redirect to ROLE SELECTION screen\n\nDo NOT delete:\n- Citizen account\n- Reports\n- Mock data\n- Language preference\n- Existing issue data\n\n==================================================\n3. GOVERNMENT SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nGovernment:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\nThen:\n\n- Clear government authentication state\n- Clear current role\n- Redirect to ROLE SELECTION screen\n\nDo NOT delete:\n- Government demo data\n- Civic issues\n- Reports\n- Analytics data\n\n==================================================\n4. ROLE SELECTION MUST ALWAYS BE ACCESSIBLE\n==================================================\n\nFrom the role-selection screen:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Demo Authentication\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nMunicipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Demo Authentication\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nThe user must be able to repeatedly switch:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government\n\nwithout clearing browser storage manually.\n\n==================================================\n5. ADD A SECONDARY \342\200\234SWITCH ROLE\342\200\235 ACTION\n==================================================\n\nFor hackathon demonstration convenience, add a small secondary action in each profile menu:\n\nCitizen:\n\342\200\234Switch to Municipal Staff\342\200\235\n\nGovernment:\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nWhen clicked:\n\nShow confirmation:\n\n\342\200\234Switch account type?\342\200\235\n\nThen:\n\n- Sign out current role\n- Clear current role\n- Redirect to role-selection screen\n\nThis is only for the prototype/demo.\n\nDo not make this button more prominent than Sign Out.\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 REPLACE THE BROKEN GOVERNMENT MAP\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Government Dashboard map is not working.\n\nDo NOT attempt to preserve a non-functional mock map.\n\nReplace the existing government map implementation with a REAL INTERACTIVE MAP.\n\nUse a proper map API/provider.\n\nPREFERRED OPTION:\n\nGoogle Maps JavaScript API.\n\nGoogle\'s current documentation requires a Maps JavaScript API key and recommends restricting that key to the intended application/domain. Use the current Maps JavaScript API implementation rather than deprecated versions.\n\nIf a working Google Maps API key is already configured in the project, use it.\n\nIf an API key is not available, implement the map behind a clean configuration/environment variable such as:\n\nVITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY\n\nand provide a graceful development fallback.\n\nDO NOT hardcode a secret API key into source code.\n\n==================================================\n3. INDIA-WIDE MAP\n==================================================\n\nThe Government Dashboard map must open as an interactive map centered on INDIA.\n\nInitial viewport:\nIndia\n\nThe user must be able to:\n\n- Zoom\n- Pan\n- Click markers\n- Cluster markers\n- Open issue information\n- Return to India view\n\nShow realistic mock civic issues across multiple Indian cities.\n\nAt minimum include:\n\nChennai\nCoimbatore\nMadurai\nBengaluru\nHyderabad\nMumbai\nDelhi\nKolkata\nPune\nAhmedabad\n\nDo not limit the map to Chennai.\n\n==================================================\n4. REAL MAP + MOCK CIVIC DATA\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe MAP must be real.\n\nThe CIVIC ISSUE DATA can remain mock/demo data.\n\nUse real geographic coordinates for the mocked issues.\n\nExample:\n\nChennai:\n13.0827, 80.2707\n\nBengaluru:\n12.9716, 77.5946\n\nHyderabad:\n17.3850, 78.4867\n\nDelhi:\n28.6139, 77.2090\n\nMumbai:\n19.0760, 72.8777\n\nAdd many issue markers across India.\n\nDo not create random coordinates that appear to be in oceans or unrelated places.\n\n==================================================\n5. ISSUE MARKERS\n==================================================\n\nEvery issue in the existing mock dataset that has valid coordinates should appear on the map.\n\nMarker appearance should reflect priority:\n\nCRITICAL\n\342\206\222 Red\n\nHIGH\n\342\206\222 Orange\n\nMEDIUM\n\342\206\222 Yellow\n\nLOW\n\342\206\222 Green\n\nResolved issues may use a muted/neutral marker.\n\nDo not use excessive visual effects.\n\n==================================================\n6. MARKER POPUP\n==================================================\n\nClicking a marker must open a compact issue card/popover.\n\nShow:\n\nIssue ID\nIssue Type\nCity\nLocation\nAuthority\nDepartment\nPriority\nStatus\nCitizen Reports\n\nExample:\n\nCIV-10482\n\nOpen Manhole\n\nChennai\n\nGreater Chennai Corporation\nRoads / related department\n\nPriority:\nCRITICAL\n\nCitizen Reports:\n43\n\nStatus:\nBeing handled\n\nButton:\n\n\342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235\n\nClicking \342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235 must open the existing Government Issue Detail page for that exact issue.\n\n==================================================\n7. USE THE EXISTING MOCK DATA\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nDo NOT create a second independent map dataset.\n\nThe map must consume the SAME issue dataset already used by:\n\nGovernment Overview\nIssue Queue\nIssue Detail\nAnalytics\nRecurring Hotspots\n\nIf the issue data contains:\n\nid\nlatitude\nlongitude\ncategory\npriority\nstatus\ncity\nauthority\ndepartment\n\nuse those fields directly.\n\nThere must be ONE source of truth.\n\n==================================================\n8. MAP FILTERING\n==================================================\n\nThe existing Government Dashboard filters should control the map.\n\nFilters:\n\nCity\nState\nAuthority\nDepartment\nIssue Type\nPriority\nStatus\nLanguage\n\nExample:\n\nSelect:\nChennai\n\n\342\206\222 Only Chennai issue markers remain.\n\nSelect:\nCritical\n\n\342\206\222 Only critical markers remain.\n\nSelect:\nRoads Department\n\n\342\206\222 Only Roads Department markers remain.\n\nThe issue queue/table and map should remain synchronized where appropriate.\n\n==================================================\n9. MARKER CLUSTERING\n==================================================\n\nThere may be many mock reports in the same geographic area.\n\nUse marker clustering so that the map remains readable.\n\nFor example:\n\n\342\200\23427 issues\342\200\235\n\ncan appear as a cluster.\n\nWhen zooming in:\n\n\342\206\222 cluster expands into individual issues.\n\nThis is especially important for dense cities such as:\n\nChennai\nMumbai\nDelhi\nBengaluru\n\n==================================================\n10. MAP LEGEND\n==================================================\n\nAdd a simple map legend:\n\n\342\227\217 Critical\n\342\227\217 High\n\342\227\217 Medium\n\342\227\217 Low\n\342\227\217 Resolved\n\nKeep it compact.\n\n==================================================\n11. INDIA OVERVIEW\n==================================================\n\nWhen the Government Dashboard opens, show an India-wide view with visible clusters.\n\nThe map should immediately communicate:\n\n\342\200\234This system is capable of monitoring civic issues across multiple Indian cities.\342\200\235\n\nInclude realistic mock issue distribution across regions.\n\nDo not make all issues concentrated in one city.\n\n==================================================\n12. MAP CONTROLS\n==================================================\n\nAdd:\n\n- Zoom in/out\n- Re-center India\n- Optional \342\200\234Fit all issues\342\200\235\n- Marker clustering\n- Map/satellite toggle only if already supported reliably\n\nDo not add unnecessary controls.\n\n==================================================\n13. LIVE-DATA LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nBecause this is a prototype, do NOT falsely claim that the displayed civic issues are real live government reports.\n\nAdd a small label:\n\n\342\200\234Demo Data\342\200\235\n\nor:\n\n\342\200\234Prototype Data\342\200\235\n\nThe geographic base map is real and interactive.\nThe civic issue markers are simulated demonstration data.\n\nThis distinction must be clear.\n\n==================================================\n14. MAP LOADING / FAILURE STATE\n==================================================\n\nDo not show a blank panel when the map fails.\n\nShow a clear loading state:\n\n\342\200\234Loading India map\342\200\246\342\200\235\n\nIf the API fails:\n\n\342\200\234Map unavailable\342\200\235\n\nwith:\n\n\342\200\234Retry\342\200\235\n\nbutton.\n\nDo NOT display a broken blank container.\n\n==================================================\n15. FALLBACK MAP OPTION\n==================================================\n\nIf Google Maps cannot be initialized because no API key is configured, use a reliable alternative such as:\n\nLeaflet + OpenStreetMap-derived tiles\n\nfor development/demo purposes.\n\nIf using OpenStreetMap tiles, follow the current OSM tile policy:\n- Correct HTTPS tile URL\n- Visible \302\251 OpenStreetMap contributors attribution\n- Normal interactive tile usage only\n- No bulk downloading or prefetching\n\nDo not silently present a fake map.\n\n==================================================\nPART 3 \342\200\224 GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD MAP INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nUpdate the Government Overview page so the map is a functional operational component.\n\nLayout:\n\nLEFT:\nKPIs / priority information\n\nRIGHT / CENTER:\nLarge India map\n\nBelow:\nPriority Queue\n\nThe map should occupy a substantial part of the dashboard.\n\nDo not make it a tiny decorative widget.\n\n==================================================\n16. MAP + ISSUE QUEUE SYNCHRONIZATION\n==================================================\n\nWhen the user clicks an issue in the Issue Queue:\n\n\342\206\222 Map should automatically center on that issue\n\342\206\222 Highlight the marker\n\342\206\222 Open issue popup if appropriate\n\nWhen the user clicks a map marker:\n\n\342\206\222 Corresponding issue should open in the Issue Detail view.\n\nThis establishes a real relationship between spatial and operational data.\n\n==================================================\n17. HOTSPOT VISUALIZATION\n==================================================\n\nUse the existing recurring hotspot data to visually emphasize areas with repeated problems.\n\nFor example:\n\nMultiple pothole reports around one location\n\n\342\206\222 clustered marker / hotspot indicator\n\nDo not add an overcomplicated heatmap if it harms readability.\n\nThe goal is to demonstrate:\n\n\342\200\234Where are civic problems concentrated?\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\n18. GOVERNMENT AUTHORITY DATA\n==================================================\n\nUse the correct authority from the existing issue record.\n\nExamples:\n\nChennai road issue:\nGreater Chennai Corporation\n\nChennai water issue:\nChennai Metropolitan Water Supply and Sewerage Board (CMWSSB)\n\nState highway issue:\nRelevant Tamil Nadu Highways / PWD authority\n\nBengaluru issue:\nBruhat Bengaluru Mahanagara Palike (BBMP)\n\nMumbai issue:\nBrihanmumbai Municipal Corporation (BMC)\n\nDelhi issue:\nRelevant Delhi civic authority based on mock jurisdiction\n\nDo not use generic \342\200\234Government Authority\342\200\235 labels where a specific authority can be shown.\n\n==================================================\nPART 4 \342\200\224 DO NOT BREAK THE CURRENT SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nPreserve all currently working functionality:\n\n- Tamil language\n- Hindi language\n- English language\n- GPS-based language default\n- Manual language switching\n- Persistent citizen account\n- Demo Aadhaar verification\n- Camera-first citizen reporting\n- Offline reporting simulation\n- Photo privacy / face blurring\n- Citizen tracking\n- Citizen resolution verification\n- Citizen reopening\n- Government dashboard\n- Analytics\n- Issue queue\n- Department data\n- Mock dataset\n\nDo NOT expose:\n- AI terminology\n- Internal workflow details\n\nto citizens.\n\nGovernment users may continue to see the detailed operational information already implemented.\n\n==================================================\nPART 5 \342\200\224 FINAL TESTS\n==================================================\n\nTEST ROLE SWITCHING:\n\n1. Open application\n2. Choose Citizen\n3. Enter Citizen Dashboard\n4. Profile \342\206\222 Sign Out\n5. Role Selection appears\n6. Choose Municipal Staff\n7. Enter Government Dashboard\n8. Government Profile \342\206\222 Sign Out\n9. Role Selection appears\n10. Choose Citizen\n11. Citizen Dashboard opens\n\nRepeat this multiple times.\n\nTEST MAP:\n\n1. Open Government Dashboard\n2. India map loads successfully\n3. Multiple cities are visible\n4. Issue markers appear\n5. Zoom works\n6. Pan works\n7. Marker clustering works\n8. Clicking marker opens issue\n9. \342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235 opens correct issue detail\n10. Filters update the map\n11. Issue Queue selection centers the map\n12. Map and dashboard use the same issue data\n13. Map loading failure has a visible fallback/error state\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe application must now provide TWO completely demonstrable environments:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 Sign In\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nGOVERNMENT\n\342\206\222 Sign In\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 India-wide interactive map\n\342\206\222 Civic issue markers\n\342\206\222 Filters\n\342\206\222 Issue details\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nThe Government Dashboard map should feel like a real municipal GIS operations map, while the underlying civic issues remain clearly marked as DEMO DATA.\n\nMost importantly:\n\nI must be able to demonstrate the entire product by switching:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\nwithout manually clearing browser storage or restarting the application."
    items {
      text: "IMPORTANT:\nPerform a targeted FUNCTIONAL FIX and enhancement on the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nDo NOT redesign the existing application.\nDo NOT remove existing features.\nPreserve the current visual identity, citizen interface, government dashboard, authentication, multilingual support, privacy protection, mock data, and existing workflows.\n\nThere are TWO critical problems to fix:\n\n1. I still cannot exit one authenticated environment and access the other login option.\n2. The Government Dashboard map is not functioning.\n\nAddress both completely.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 FIX ROLE EXIT / LOGIN SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nAfter entering either the Citizen Dashboard or Government Dashboard, I cannot properly back out to choose the other environment.\n\nThe application appears to trap the user inside the currently authenticated role.\n\nI need a reliable way to:\n\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out / Exit\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nAND:\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out / Exit\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\n==================================================\n1. CREATE A ROLE SELECTION SCREEN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a clean entry screen:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235\n\nChoose how you want to continue:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nThis must be accessible after signing out from either environment.\n\nKeep this screen simple.\n\nDo not expose it inside the normal citizen workflow.\n\n==================================================\n2. CITIZEN SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nCitizen:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\nThen:\n\n- Clear citizen authentication state\n- Clear current role\n- Redirect to ROLE SELECTION screen\n\nDo NOT delete:\n- Citizen account\n- Reports\n- Mock data\n- Language preference\n- Existing issue data\n\n==================================================\n3. GOVERNMENT SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nGovernment:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\nThen:\n\n- Clear government authentication state\n- Clear current role\n- Redirect to ROLE SELECTION screen\n\nDo NOT delete:\n- Government demo data\n- Civic issues\n- Reports\n- Analytics data\n\n==================================================\n4. ROLE SELECTION MUST ALWAYS BE ACCESSIBLE\n==================================================\n\nFrom the role-selection screen:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Demo Authentication\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nMunicipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Demo Authentication\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nThe user must be able to repeatedly switch:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Government\n\nwithout clearing browser storage manually.\n\n==================================================\n5. ADD A SECONDARY \342\200\234SWITCH ROLE\342\200\235 ACTION\n==================================================\n\nFor hackathon demonstration convenience, add a small secondary action in each profile menu:\n\nCitizen:\n\342\200\234Switch to Municipal Staff\342\200\235\n\nGovernment:\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nWhen clicked:\n\nShow confirmation:\n\n\342\200\234Switch account type?\342\200\235\n\nThen:\n\n- Sign out current role\n- Clear current role\n- Redirect to role-selection screen\n\nThis is only for the prototype/demo.\n\nDo not make this button more prominent than Sign Out.\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 REPLACE THE BROKEN GOVERNMENT MAP\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Government Dashboard map is not working.\n\nDo NOT attempt to preserve a non-functional mock map.\n\nReplace the existing government map implementation with a REAL INTERACTIVE MAP.\n\nUse a proper map API/provider.\n\nPREFERRED OPTION:\n\nGoogle Maps JavaScript API.\n\nGoogle\'s current documentation requires a Maps JavaScript API key and recommends restricting that key to the intended application/domain. Use the current Maps JavaScript API implementation rather than deprecated versions.\n\nIf a working Google Maps API key is already configured in the project, use it.\n\nIf an API key is not available, implement the map behind a clean configuration/environment variable such as:\n\nVITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY\n\nand provide a graceful development fallback.\n\nDO NOT hardcode a secret API key into source code.\n\n==================================================\n3. INDIA-WIDE MAP\n==================================================\n\nThe Government Dashboard map must open as an interactive map centered on INDIA.\n\nInitial viewport:\nIndia\n\nThe user must be able to:\n\n- Zoom\n- Pan\n- Click markers\n- Cluster markers\n- Open issue information\n- Return to India view\n\nShow realistic mock civic issues across multiple Indian cities.\n\nAt minimum include:\n\nChennai\nCoimbatore\nMadurai\nBengaluru\nHyderabad\nMumbai\nDelhi\nKolkata\nPune\nAhmedabad\n\nDo not limit the map to Chennai.\n\n==================================================\n4. REAL MAP + MOCK CIVIC DATA\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe MAP must be real.\n\nThe CIVIC ISSUE DATA can remain mock/demo data.\n\nUse real geographic coordinates for the mocked issues.\n\nExample:\n\nChennai:\n13.0827, 80.2707\n\nBengaluru:\n12.9716, 77.5946\n\nHyderabad:\n17.3850, 78.4867\n\nDelhi:\n28.6139, 77.2090\n\nMumbai:\n19.0760, 72.8777\n\nAdd many issue markers across India.\n\nDo not create random coordinates that appear to be in oceans or unrelated places.\n\n==================================================\n5. ISSUE MARKERS\n==================================================\n\nEvery issue in the existing mock dataset that has valid coordinates should appear on the map.\n\nMarker appearance should reflect priority:\n\nCRITICAL\n\342\206\222 Red\n\nHIGH\n\342\206\222 Orange\n\nMEDIUM\n\342\206\222 Yellow\n\nLOW\n\342\206\222 Green\n\nResolved issues may use a muted/neutral marker.\n\nDo not use excessive visual effects.\n\n==================================================\n6. MARKER POPUP\n==================================================\n\nClicking a marker must open a compact issue card/popover.\n\nShow:\n\nIssue ID\nIssue Type\nCity\nLocation\nAuthority\nDepartment\nPriority\nStatus\nCitizen Reports\n\nExample:\n\nCIV-10482\n\nOpen Manhole\n\nChennai\n\nGreater Chennai Corporation\nRoads / related department\n\nPriority:\nCRITICAL\n\nCitizen Reports:\n43\n\nStatus:\nBeing handled\n\nButton:\n\n\342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235\n\nClicking \342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235 must open the existing Government Issue Detail page for that exact issue.\n\n==================================================\n7. USE THE EXISTING MOCK DATA\n==================================================\n\nCRITICAL:\n\nDo NOT create a second independent map dataset.\n\nThe map must consume the SAME issue dataset already used by:\n\nGovernment Overview\nIssue Queue\nIssue Detail\nAnalytics\nRecurring Hotspots\n\nIf the issue data contains:\n\nid\nlatitude\nlongitude\ncategory\npriority\nstatus\ncity\nauthority\ndepartment\n\nuse those fields directly.\n\nThere must be ONE source of truth.\n\n==================================================\n8. MAP FILTERING\n==================================================\n\nThe existing Government Dashboard filters should control the map.\n\nFilters:\n\nCity\nState\nAuthority\nDepartment\nIssue Type\nPriority\nStatus\nLanguage\n\nExample:\n\nSelect:\nChennai\n\n\342\206\222 Only Chennai issue markers remain.\n\nSelect:\nCritical\n\n\342\206\222 Only critical markers remain.\n\nSelect:\nRoads Department\n\n\342\206\222 Only Roads Department markers remain.\n\nThe issue queue/table and map should remain synchronized where appropriate.\n\n==================================================\n9. MARKER CLUSTERING\n==================================================\n\nThere may be many mock reports in the same geographic area.\n\nUse marker clustering so that the map remains readable.\n\nFor example:\n\n\342\200\23427 issues\342\200\235\n\ncan appear as a cluster.\n\nWhen zooming in:\n\n\342\206\222 cluster expands into individual issues.\n\nThis is especially important for dense cities such as:\n\nChennai\nMumbai\nDelhi\nBengaluru\n\n==================================================\n10. MAP LEGEND\n==================================================\n\nAdd a simple map legend:\n\n\342\227\217 Critical\n\342\227\217 High\n\342\227\217 Medium\n\342\227\217 Low\n\342\227\217 Resolved\n\nKeep it compact.\n\n==================================================\n11. INDIA OVERVIEW\n==================================================\n\nWhen the Government Dashboard opens, show an India-wide view with visible clusters.\n\nThe map should immediately communicate:\n\n\342\200\234This system is capable of monitoring civic issues across multiple Indian cities.\342\200\235\n\nInclude realistic mock issue distribution across regions.\n\nDo not make all issues concentrated in one city.\n\n==================================================\n12. MAP CONTROLS\n==================================================\n\nAdd:\n\n- Zoom in/out\n- Re-center India\n- Optional \342\200\234Fit all issues\342\200\235\n- Marker clustering\n- Map/satellite toggle only if already supported reliably\n\nDo not add unnecessary controls.\n\n==================================================\n13. LIVE-DATA LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nBecause this is a prototype, do NOT falsely claim that the displayed civic issues are real live government reports.\n\nAdd a small label:\n\n\342\200\234Demo Data\342\200\235\n\nor:\n\n\342\200\234Prototype Data\342\200\235\n\nThe geographic base map is real and interactive.\nThe civic issue markers are simulated demonstration data.\n\nThis distinction must be clear.\n\n==================================================\n14. MAP LOADING / FAILURE STATE\n==================================================\n\nDo not show a blank panel when the map fails.\n\nShow a clear loading state:\n\n\342\200\234Loading India map\342\200\246\342\200\235\n\nIf the API fails:\n\n\342\200\234Map unavailable\342\200\235\n\nwith:\n\n\342\200\234Retry\342\200\235\n\nbutton.\n\nDo NOT display a broken blank container.\n\n==================================================\n15. FALLBACK MAP OPTION\n==================================================\n\nIf Google Maps cannot be initialized because no API key is configured, use a reliable alternative such as:\n\nLeaflet + OpenStreetMap-derived tiles\n\nfor development/demo purposes.\n\nIf using OpenStreetMap tiles, follow the current OSM tile policy:\n- Correct HTTPS tile URL\n- Visible \302\251 OpenStreetMap contributors attribution\n- Normal interactive tile usage only\n- No bulk downloading or prefetching\n\nDo not silently present a fake map.\n\n==================================================\nPART 3 \342\200\224 GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD MAP INTEGRATION\n==================================================\n\nUpdate the Government Overview page so the map is a functional operational component.\n\nLayout:\n\nLEFT:\nKPIs / priority information\n\nRIGHT / CENTER:\nLarge India map\n\nBelow:\nPriority Queue\n\nThe map should occupy a substantial part of the dashboard.\n\nDo not make it a tiny decorative widget.\n\n==================================================\n16. MAP + ISSUE QUEUE SYNCHRONIZATION\n==================================================\n\nWhen the user clicks an issue in the Issue Queue:\n\n\342\206\222 Map should automatically center on that issue\n\342\206\222 Highlight the marker\n\342\206\222 Open issue popup if appropriate\n\nWhen the user clicks a map marker:\n\n\342\206\222 Corresponding issue should open in the Issue Detail view.\n\nThis establishes a real relationship between spatial and operational data.\n\n==================================================\n17. HOTSPOT VISUALIZATION\n==================================================\n\nUse the existing recurring hotspot data to visually emphasize areas with repeated problems.\n\nFor example:\n\nMultiple pothole reports around one location\n\n\342\206\222 clustered marker / hotspot indicator\n\nDo not add an overcomplicated heatmap if it harms readability.\n\nThe goal is to demonstrate:\n\n\342\200\234Where are civic problems concentrated?\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\n18. GOVERNMENT AUTHORITY DATA\n==================================================\n\nUse the correct authority from the existing issue record.\n\nExamples:\n\nChennai road issue:\nGreater Chennai Corporation\n\nChennai water issue:\nChennai Metropolitan Water Supply and Sewerage Board (CMWSSB)\n\nState highway issue:\nRelevant Tamil Nadu Highways / PWD authority\n\nBengaluru issue:\nBruhat Bengaluru Mahanagara Palike (BBMP)\n\nMumbai issue:\nBrihanmumbai Municipal Corporation (BMC)\n\nDelhi issue:\nRelevant Delhi civic authority based on mock jurisdiction\n\nDo not use generic \342\200\234Government Authority\342\200\235 labels where a specific authority can be shown.\n\n==================================================\nPART 4 \342\200\224 DO NOT BREAK THE CURRENT SYSTEM\n==================================================\n\nPreserve all currently working functionality:\n\n- Tamil language\n- Hindi language\n- English language\n- GPS-based language default\n- Manual language switching\n- Persistent citizen account\n- Demo Aadhaar verification\n- Camera-first citizen reporting\n- Offline reporting simulation\n- Photo privacy / face blurring\n- Citizen tracking\n- Citizen resolution verification\n- Citizen reopening\n- Government dashboard\n- Analytics\n- Issue queue\n- Department data\n- Mock dataset\n\nDo NOT expose:\n- AI terminology\n- Internal workflow details\n\nto citizens.\n\nGovernment users may continue to see the detailed operational information already implemented.\n\n==================================================\nPART 5 \342\200\224 FINAL TESTS\n==================================================\n\nTEST ROLE SWITCHING:\n\n1. Open application\n2. Choose Citizen\n3. Enter Citizen Dashboard\n4. Profile \342\206\222 Sign Out\n5. Role Selection appears\n6. Choose Municipal Staff\n7. Enter Government Dashboard\n8. Government Profile \342\206\222 Sign Out\n9. Role Selection appears\n10. Choose Citizen\n11. Citizen Dashboard opens\n\nRepeat this multiple times.\n\nTEST MAP:\n\n1. Open Government Dashboard\n2. India map loads successfully\n3. Multiple cities are visible\n4. Issue markers appear\n5. Zoom works\n6. Pan works\n7. Marker clustering works\n8. Clicking marker opens issue\n9. \342\200\234View Issue\342\200\235 opens correct issue detail\n10. Filters update the map\n11. Issue Queue selection centers the map\n12. Map and dashboard use the same issue data\n13. Map loading failure has a visible fallback/error state\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe application must now provide TWO completely demonstrable environments:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 Sign In\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nGOVERNMENT\n\342\206\222 Sign In\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 India-wide interactive map\n\342\206\222 Civic issue markers\n\342\206\222 Filters\n\342\206\222 Issue details\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nThe Government Dashboard map should feel like a real municipal GIS operations map, while the underlying civic issues remain clearly marked as DEMO DATA.\n\nMost importantly:\n\nI must be able to demonstrate the entire product by switching:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\nwithout manually clearing browser storage or restarting the application."
    }
  }
}
