    thinking: "**Analyzing Logout Functionality**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `logout()` function within `AppContext.tsx`. My focus is on the specific actions it takes when the active app is \'CITIZEN\'. It\'s removing authentication and user data from local storage for the citizen app and then resetting `citizenUser` to `null`. I\'m starting to think about potential refinements, specifically around the user state reset.\n\n\n**Refining Logout Logic**\n\nI\'m now considering the implications of the logout process and how it handles the different application states. The primary adjustment involves unsetting `cscirr_active_app` to prevent immediate redirection after logout. This will allow for a role selection screen after logging out. I\'m focusing on ensuring this transition works consistently for both the CITIZEN and GOVERNMENT flows, which are currently diverging. I want the experience to be consistent no matter the starting application context.\n\n\n"
