    thinking: "**Listing Core Issues**\n\nI\'ve got the initial list of eight hardcoded issues: Pothole, Open Manhole, Sewage, Garbage accumulation, Road flooding, Broken streetlight, Stray animal hazard, and a yet unlisted one. I\'m focusing on defining the scope for these eight right now, for a basic implementation. Next, I\'ll need to figure out how to add more.\n\n\n**Assigning Visuals for Issues**\n\nI\'ve just added a \"Fallen tree\" to the list of issues. I\'m also finding before-and-after images for the listed issues, with the goal of adding them to the system. This will help illustrate the changes better. So far, potholes, open manholes, garbage accumulation, and road flooding all have example images.\n\n\n**Linking Images to Issues**\n\nI\'ve just added images for \"Broken streetlight\", \"Stray animal hazard\", and \"Fallen tree\". I\'m rethinking how to generate images for random issues. I tried Unsplash with a seed, but it might not be the best approach for the unique and relevant image requirement. I think using random UUIDs with picsum.photos would be better, but the relevancy is an issue still. I need to make the images visually correspond to the issue categories.\n\n\n**Refining Image Assignments**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a reliable method for unique image assignments. The previous idea of cycling through IDs wasn\'t sufficient. My latest thought is to create a list of Unsplash photo IDs for each issue category, ensuring each report has a distinct visual. This avoids random or irrelevant images. I\'ll search for real IDs and use a URL with the photo IDs for consistency. I\'m focusing on \"potholes,\" \"garbage,\" \"water leak,\" and \"broken streetlight\" for now.\n\n\n"
