  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Authentication Logic**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. The switch from CITIZEN to GOV causes an immediate `GovApp` load due to existing `cscirr_gov_auth` in localStorage. The core problem is that switching \"back\" to a different environment is impossible in the current design. Independent authentication mechanisms are needed to solve this.\n\n\n**Clarifying Sign-Out Behavior**\n\nI\'ve clarified the sign-out functionality. The key is `logout()` only unsets auth for the `activeApp`, not `activeApp` itself. Consequently, after sign-out, `activeApp` remains, but the user data is cleared. This triggers the `AuthFlow` and returns the user to role selection, which I now realize is the desired behavior! This means sign-out is fully implemented, even after the changes.\n\n\n**Confirming Seamless Switching**\n\nIt seems the logic I\'ve been working through allows seamless role switching after logout. If a user logs out of CITIZEN and returns to the Welcome screen, selecting \"Municipal Staff\" when already logged into GOV correctly triggers the `GovApp` rendering. The `App.tsx` component is re-evaluated, and detects that `authState` is `AUTHENTICATED` and the `user` is `govUser` and automatically renders the correct application. This is exactly as desired, and appears perfectly functional.\n\n\n**Verifying View Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `AuthFlow` component to confirm the view logic. Specifically, I\'m checking the changes to the `view` state within the `AuthFlow`. It\'s correctly initialized to \'WELCOME\'. If `AuthFlow` is remounted, `view` is reset to \'WELCOME\', which is as expected. This happens when `MainApp` switches from `CitizenApp` back to `AuthFlow` due to `user` becoming null. Seems great so far. I\'ll also double-check the switch role button.\n\n\n**Refining Role Switching**\n\nI\'m revisiting the \"Switch Role\" action. My prior logic called `logout()` and set `activeApp`. Now I realize, the goal is role switching *without* clearing persistent data. I\'m focusing on the interaction with `logout()` \342\200\223 clearing specific auth states versus persistent data, and the navigation flow. The current implementation clears CITIZEN auth after the switch, but also triggers a desired return to role selection and renders the Welcome screen, which may not be the optimal user experience. I need to modify this flow.\n\n\n**Revising Switch Functionality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Switch Role\" action and rethinking the current `logout()` approach. The global authenticated state is still problematic. If they click \"Switch to Municipal Staff,\" I now think they may just want a role switch, not a full logout. Changing `activeApp` alone could be enough, and the `AuthFlow` should render role selection. However, the existing logic sets `activeApp` along with logout. I need to avoid forcing a full logout. I\'m going to test the role switch without a logout.\n\n\n\n**Evaluating Switch Role Logic**\n\nI\'m now grappling with the implications of the \"Switch Role\" functionality. If I\'m authenticated in CITIZEN and select \"Switch Role,\" the current logic of setting `activeApp=\'GOV\'` will immediately render `GovApp` if I am already authenticated in GOV. This is a valid role switch, but not a redirect to the Role Selection screen as requested. Conversely, setting `activeApp` and being NOT authenticated in GOV correctly routes to Role Selection. I\'m exploring how to align this with the requirements. It appears I will need different behavior based on current authentication state in the *target* app!\n\n\n"
