  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the targeted functional fixes for the \"Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\" prototype, directly addressing the three unresolved problems while strictly preserving the existing design, identity, language settings, and core application flow.\n\n- **Unique and Relevant Mock Images**: I refactored the image generation logic inside the data model to ensure that **every single mock report now receives a unique, category-relevant image** (e.g., potholes look like actual potholes, garbage reports show garbage). This eliminates the repetition of generic civic images and gives the prototype a much more authentic, demonstrable feel.\n- **Independent Role Switching & Secure Sign Out**: I restructured the global `AuthFlow` and `AppContext` to create completely sandboxed authentication states.\n  - Signing out of either dashboard now correctly drops that specific session and routes you safely back to the new Role Selection entry screen.\n  - I integrated intuitive \"Switch to Municipal Staff\" and \"Switch to Citizen\" secondary actions into the profile menus. This allows you to toggle seamlessly between the two workflows without overwriting or trapping the opposite authenticated state, and without ever losing local data.\n- **Functional Government Map**: I fully replaced the static placeholder map on the Government Dashboard with a highly interactive, production-ready GIS implementation using `react-leaflet`. It directly consumes the live mock dataset, automatically clusters dense report areas, dynamically color-codes map pins based on issue priority (with visual pulse alerts for critical issues), and responds live to issue-type filters from the dashboard controls."
    modified_response: "I have completed the targeted functional fixes for the \"Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\" prototype, directly addressing the three unresolved problems while strictly preserving the existing design, identity, language settings, and core application flow.\n\n- **Unique and Relevant Mock Images**: I refactored the image generation logic inside the data model to ensure that **every single mock report now receives a unique, category-relevant image** (e.g., potholes look like actual potholes, garbage reports show garbage). This eliminates the repetition of generic civic images and gives the prototype a much more authentic, demonstrable feel.\n- **Independent Role Switching & Secure Sign Out**: I restructured the global `AuthFlow` and `AppContext` to create completely sandboxed authentication states.\n  - Signing out of either dashboard now correctly drops that specific session and routes you safely back to the new Role Selection entry screen.\n  - I integrated intuitive \"Switch to Municipal Staff\" and \"Switch to Citizen\" secondary actions into the profile menus. This allows you to toggle seamlessly between the two workflows without overwriting or trapping the opposite authenticated state, and without ever losing local data.\n- **Functional Government Map**: I fully replaced the static placeholder map on the Government Dashboard with a highly interactive, production-ready GIS implementation using `react-leaflet`. It directly consumes the live mock dataset, automatically clusters dense report areas, dynamically color-codes map pins based on issue priority (with visual pulse alerts for critical issues), and responds live to issue-type filters from the dashboard controls."
