:\n\nIf coordinates are specified, the address should correspond to the same city/area.\n\nDo NOT display:\n\n\342\200\234Random Street\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Sample Street\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Unknown Road\342\200\235\n\nor similar placeholder addresses.\n\n==================================================\n16. ADDRESS + COORDINATE CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nAudit all mock issues for:\n\nCity\nState\nAddress\nLatitude\nLongitude\n\nThese fields must be geographically consistent.\n\nExample:\n\nDO NOT:\n\nAddress:\nRandom Street, Delhi\n\nCoordinates:\n13.7463, 80.3801\n\nbecause these coordinates are not Delhi.\n\nInstead, correct either the coordinates or the address so they represent the same geographic area.\n\nEvery issue must have internally consistent location data.\n\n==================================================\n17. FIX BEFORE / AFTER PHOTO MISMATCH\n==================================================\n\nTHIS IS CRITICAL.\n\nThe current prototype displays completely unrelated before/after images.\n\nThe screenshot shows an example where:\n\nBEFORE:\nA forest/water scene\n\nAFTER:\nShoes on a beach\n\nThis is unacceptable for a civic resolution system.\n\nThe before and after photos MUST depict the SAME CIVIC ISSUE / SAME LOCATION.\n\nExamples:\n\nPOTHOLE:\n\nBefore:\nLarge pothole on a specific road\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME road/location after the pothole has been repaired\n\nGARBAGE:\n\nBefore:\nGarbage pile at a specific roadside location\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME location after garbage has been removed\n\nBROKEN STREETLIGHT:\n\nBefore:\nBroken streetlight at a specific road\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME streetlight repaired/replaced\n\nOPEN MANHOLE:\n\nBefore:\nOpen manhole at a specific location\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME manhole safely covered/repaired\n\nDRAIN:\n\nBefore:\nOverflowing drain at a specific location\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME drain after clearing\n\nWATER LEAK:\n\nBefore:\nLeaking pipe at a specific location\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME pipe after repair\n\n==================================================\n18. BEFORE / AFTER IMAGE DATA MODEL\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT randomly assign images to beforeImage and afterImage.\n\nEach canonical civic issue should have an evidence pair.\n\nExample:\n\nIssue CIV-10482:\n\nbeforeImage:\npothole_anna_nagar_before.jpg\n\nafterImage:\npothole_anna_nagar_after.jpg\n\nIssue CIV-10483:\n\nbeforeImage:\ngarbage_t_nagar_before.jpg\n\nafterImage:\ngarbage_t_nagar_after.jpg\n\nThe pair must belong to the SAME physical issue.\n\n==================================================\n19. VISUAL CONSISTENCY OF BEFORE / AFTER\n==================================================\n\nThe before and after image should match as closely as possible in:\n\n- Location\n- Perspective\n- Infrastructure object\n- Surroundings\n- Road/building context\n\nOnly the civic problem should be changed.\n\nFor example:\n\nBEFORE:\nSame road\nSame building\nSame streetlight\nBroken lamp\n\nAFTER:\nSame road\nSame building\nSame streetlight\nWorking lamp\n\nDo NOT use unrelated stock images simply because they represent the same category.\n\n==================================================\n20. AUDIT ALL EXISTING ISSUES\n==================================================\n\nPerform a complete data audit of every existing mock issue.\n\nFor each issue verify:\n\n\342\234\223 Relevant image\n\342\234\223 Unique image where appropriate\n\342\234\223 Valid before image\n\342\234\223 Valid after image\n\342\234\223 Before and after refer to same issue\n\342\234\223 Realistic address\n\342\234\223 Correct city\n\342\234\223 Correct state\n\342\234\223 Correct coordinates\n\342\234\223 Correct jurisdiction\n\342\234\223 Correct issue category\n\342\234\223 Consistent status\n\342\234\223 Consistent authority\n\342\234\223 Consistent department\n\nFix every record that violates these requirements.\n\n==================================================\n21. PHOTO FALLBACK\n==================================================\n\nKeep the existing image fallback behavior.\n\nIf a primary image cannot load:\n\n\342\206\222 use a relevant category-specific fallback.\n\nNever display a broken image.\n\nBut do NOT solve missing images by assigning the same generic image to every issue.\n\n==================================================\n22. GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD DATA CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nEnsure:\n\nGovernment Overview\nIssue Queue\nLive Map\nIssue Detail\nAnalytics\nRecurring Hotspots\n\nall use the same underlying dataset.\n\nIf CIV-10482 has:\n\nCity:\nChennai\n\nAddress:\nAnna Salai\n\nJurisdiction:\nGreater Chennai Corporation\n\nthen those values should be identical everywhere CIV-10482 appears.\n\n==================================================\n23. FINAL TESTING\n==================================================\n\nPerform these tests before finishing.\n\nAUTHENTICATION:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Government\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nAll must work.\n\nSEARCH:\n\nSearch:\nChennai\n\342\206\222 Chennai records\n\nSearch:\nPothole\n\342\206\222 Pothole records\n\nSearch:\nCIV-10482\n\342\206\222 Exact issue\n\nEXPORT:\n\nClick:\nExport Report\n\n\342\206\222 CSV file downloads\n\nVerify that the CSV contains actual mock records.\n\nLOGO:\n\nClick logo\n\342\206\222 Correct home/dashboard\n\nMAP:\n\nOpen Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 India map loads\n\nVerify:\n- Only India is the visible geographic focus\n- State boundaries are visible\n- Heatmap displays\n- Mock civic reports appear\n- Multiple cities have report concentrations\n- Zoom works\n- Pan works\n- Filters work\n- Issue markers correspond to dataset\n- Clicking an issue opens correct details\n\nIMAGE:\n\nOpen at least 10 different issue records.\n\nVerify:\n- Images are relevant\n- Images are not all identical\n- Before/after pairs are related\n- No random blur circles appear\n- No broken images appear\n\nLOCATION:\n\nVerify no issue contains contradictory values such as:\n\n\342\200\234Delhi\342\200\235\nwith Chennai coordinates.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe final prototype must communicate:\n\nCITIZEN SIDE:\nSimple\nAccessible\nMultilingual\nCamera-first\nPrivacy-conscious\n\nGOVERNMENT SIDE:\nIndia-wide\nDetailed\nData-rich\nSearchable\nExportable\nGeospatial\nOperational\n\nThe Government Dashboard should clearly demonstrate:\n\nREAL INDIA MAP\n+\nCITIZEN REPORT HEATMAP\n+\nINDIAN CIVIC ISSUE DATA\n+\nJURISDICTION INFORMATION\n+\nSEARCH\n+\nEXPORT\n+\nDETAILED ISSUE RECORDS\n\nThe citizen side should remain simple and should NOT expose:\n\nAI terminology\nInternal workflow\nPriority algorithms\nRouting logic\nTechnical system details\n\nFinally, preserve the exact official product name everywhere:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235\n\nDo not introduce or restore any alternative product name."
    items {
      text: "IMPORTANT:\nPerform a comprehensive BUG FIX + DATA QUALITY + NAVIGATION update on the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nDO NOT redesign the application from scratch.\nDO NOT change the existing visual identity, typography, spacing system, citizen UX, government dashboard structure, language system, authentication concept, or overall layout.\n\nThe goal is to FIX the following specific issues and improve the realism/consistency of the existing prototype.\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE THE CURRENT FACE-BLUR EFFECT\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nCompletely REMOVE the current automated face-blurring visual effect from the prototype for now.\n\nThe current implementation is placing circular blur overlays randomly over images and is incorrectly blurring non-face objects.\n\nThe screenshot demonstrates this problem.\n\nREMOVE:\n\n- Random blur circles\n- Random privacy overlays\n- Incorrect face detection visualizations\n- Any fake blur positioned on arbitrary parts of images\n\nDo NOT attempt to improve or repair the current face detection implementation yet.\n\nFor now:\n\nOriginal image\n\342\206\222 No artificial blur overlay\n\nThe existing \342\200\234Privacy Protected\342\200\235 concept may remain as text if already part of the UI, but there must be NO incorrect visual blur applied to photos.\n\nWe will implement proper face detection and blurring later.\n\n==================================================\n2. FIX \342\200\234SWITCH TO CITIZEN\342\200\235 BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nThe current:\n\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nbutton does not work.\n\nMake it fully functional.\n\nWhen a government user clicks:\n\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nshow:\n\n\342\200\234Switch account type?\342\200\235\n\nButtons:\n\nCancel\nContinue\n\nOn Continue:\n\n- End the current government session\n- Clear current role\n- Navigate to the Role Selection screen\n\nThe Role Selection screen must provide:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nSelecting Citizen must open the citizen demo authentication flow.\n\nDo NOT require the user to manually clear browser storage.\n\n==================================================\n3. FIX SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nThe current Sign Out functionality still does not work correctly.\n\nImplement a fully functional sign-out system for BOTH roles.\n\nCITIZEN:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nMake sure:\n\n- Authentication state is cleared correctly\n- Current role is cleared\n- User is redirected correctly\n- Dashboard cannot remain accessible as an authenticated user after sign out\n- Mock data is NOT deleted\n- Language preference is NOT deleted\n- Reports are NOT deleted\n- Issue data is NOT deleted\n\n==================================================\n4. ROLE SWITCHING MUST WORK WITHOUT RESTARTING\n==================================================\n\nThe following MUST work repeatedly:\n\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nThen:\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nAlso:\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nAnd:\n\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Government\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nNo refresh should be required.\n\nNo browser storage clearing should be required.\n\n==================================================\n5. GOVERNMENT MAP \342\200\224 INDIA ONLY\n==================================================\n\nThe Government Dashboard map must show ONLY INDIA.\n\nDo NOT show:\n- Pakistan\n- Bangladesh\n- Sri Lanka\n- Nepal\n- China\n- Any other surrounding country\n\nThe map viewport should be constrained/initially positioned so that India is the clear geographic focus.\n\nUse a detailed real interactive map.\n\nThe map must include:\n\n- Indian state boundaries\n- Major cities\n- Major roads where supported\n- Detailed geographic context\n- Zoom controls\n- Pan controls\n\nThe map should initially fit India.\n\nThe interface should make the map clearly read as:\n\n\342\200\234INDIA CIVIC ISSUE MAP\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\n6. INDIA-WIDE CIVIC HEATMAP\n==================================================\n\nReplace the current simplistic marker-focused visualization with a more convincing civic issue heatmap.\n\nThe underlying geographic map must be real.\n\nThe civic data may remain DEMO DATA.\n\nGenerate realistic mock citizen-report density across India.\n\nExample concentrations:\n\nChennai\nBengaluru\nHyderabad\nMumbai\nDelhi\nKolkata\nPune\nAhmedabad\nCoimbatore\nMadurai\nJaipur\nLucknow\nKochi\netc.\n\nDo NOT make the entire country uniformly covered.\n\nCreate realistic clusters around urban areas.\n\nUse a heatmap to represent:\n\n\342\200\234Citizen Report Density\342\200\235\n\nThe heatmap should become denser where more reports exist.\n\nSuggested intensity:\n\nLow reports \342\206\222 light intensity\nModerate reports \342\206\222 medium intensity\nHigh reports \342\206\222 strong intensity\n\nThe user should visually understand:\n\n\342\200\234Where are citizens reporting the most civic problems?\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\n7. HEATMAP + INDIVIDUAL ISSUE VIEW\n==================================================\n\nAllow the government user to switch between:\n\n\342\200\234Heatmap\342\200\235\n\nand:\n\n\342\200\234Issue Markers\342\200\235\n\nHeatmap:\nShows report density.\n\nMarkers:\nShows individual civic issues.\n\nIf supported, provide:\n\n[ Heatmap ] [ Issues ]\n\nDo not make this overly complicated.\n\n==================================================\n8. MAP DATA MUST COME FROM THE EXISTING DATASET\n==================================================\n\nThe map MUST use the same underlying civic issue/report dataset used by:\n\n- Government Dashboard\n- Issue Queue\n- Issue Detail\n- Analytics\n- Recurring Hotspots\n\nDo NOT create a completely separate set of map-only data.\n\nEvery report should have:\n\nlatitude\nlongitude\ncity\nstate\nissueType\nstatus\npriority\nauthority\ndepartment\n\nUse these to construct the map.\n\n==================================================\n9. REMOVE AUTOMATED JURISDICTION ROUTING\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nRemove the CURRENT automated jurisdiction routing behaviour.\n\nThe system should NOT claim to automatically determine or route the issue to the correct authority.\n\nDo NOT display:\n\n\342\200\234Automatically routed to\342\200\246\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234AI selected department\342\200\246\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Automatically assigned\342\200\246\342\200\235\n\nInstead, simply DISPLAY the jurisdiction information associated with the mock issue.\n\nFor example:\n\nJurisdiction:\nGreater Chennai Corporation\n\nZone:\nZone 8\n\nWard:\nWard 181\n\nOr:\n\nJurisdiction:\nBruhat Bengaluru Mahanagara Palike (BBMP)\n\nWard:\n...\n\nThe architecture can retain jurisdiction data, but it should be presented as:\n\n\342\200\234Jurisdiction\342\200\235\n\nrather than:\n\n\342\200\234Automatically Routed Authority\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\n10. JURISDICTION DISPLAY\n==================================================\n\nFor every government issue, show:\n\nJurisdiction\nZone\nWard\nAuthority\n\nExample:\n\nJurisdiction:\nGreater Chennai Corporation\n\nZone:\nZone 8\n\nWard:\nWard 181\n\nKeep this separate from:\n\nDepartment\n\nDepartment can still exist as issue metadata where appropriate.\n\nDo not claim the platform autonomously determined the authority.\n\n==================================================\n11. FIX EXPORT REPORT BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nThe existing:\n\n\342\200\234Export Report\342\200\235\n\nbutton currently does nothing.\n\nMake it functional.\n\nWhen clicked, export the COMPLETE MOCK DATASET currently being displayed by the Government Dashboard.\n\nPreferred format:\n\nCSV\n\nInclude fields such as:\n\nReport ID\nIssue ID\nIssue Type\nOriginal Language\nDescription\nCity\nState\nAddress\nLatitude\nLongitude\nJurisdiction\nWard\nDepartment\nPriority\nStatus\nCitizen Report Count\nAssigned Team\nCreated Date\nUpdated Date\n\nThe downloaded file should contain the actual current mock data.\n\nDo NOT export placeholder text.\n\nIf filters are currently applied, provide:\n\n\342\200\234Export Current View\342\200\235\n\nso the exported data matches the current filtered dashboard.\n\nAlso provide:\n\n\342\200\234Export All Data\342\200\235\n\nif practical.\n\nAt minimum, one fully functional export option must exist.\n\n==================================================\n12. NAME CHANGE\n==================================================\n\nChange the current displayed user name to:\n\n\342\200\234Sathyendhar B\342\200\235\n\nUse this consistently across the citizen-facing authenticated experience.\n\nWhere a citizen profile is displayed, show:\n\nSathyendhar B\n\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nDo not leave old demo names such as:\nArun Kumar\n\nanywhere visible in the citizen interface.\n\n==================================================\n13. FIX SEARCH BAR\n==================================================\n\nThe Government Dashboard search bar currently does not work.\n\nMake it functional.\n\nThe search should be able to search across the current civic issue dataset.\n\nAllow searches by:\n\nIssue ID\nReport ID\nIssue Type\nCity\nState\nJurisdiction\nWard\nDepartment\nStatus\nDescription\n\nExamples:\n\nSearch:\n\342\200\234CIV-10482\342\200\235\n\n\342\206\222 Show matching issue.\n\nSearch:\n\342\200\234Chennai\342\200\235\n\n\342\206\222 Show Chennai-related issues.\n\nSearch:\n\342\200\234Pothole\342\200\235\n\n\342\206\222 Show pothole issues.\n\nSearch:\n\342\200\234Hindi\342\200\235\n\n\342\206\222 Show reports submitted in Hindi if language is searchable.\n\nThe search should update the relevant table/list/map where practical.\n\nInclude a clear \342\200\234No results found\342\200\235 state.\n\n==================================================\n14. CLICKING THE LOGO MUST RETURN HOME\n==================================================\n\nThe product logo/header must be clickable.\n\nWhen the user clicks the logo:\n\nCITIZEN:\n\342\206\222 Citizen Home Dashboard\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\342\206\222 Government Overview Dashboard\n\nDo NOT redirect to a login screen unless the user is actually signed out.\n\nThe logo should function as a standard \342\200\234Home\342\200\235 navigation control.\n\n==================================================\n15. FIX ALL MOCK ADDRESSES\n==================================================\n\nThere are currently unrealistic placeholders such as:\n\n\342\200\234Random Street, Delhi\342\200\235\n\nRemove these.\n\nEvery issue must use a realistic street/address corresponding to its actual mock geographic location.\n\nExamples:\n\nChennai:\nAnna Salai\nArcot Road\nPoonamallee High Road\nOMR\nVelachery Main Road\nMount Road\n\nBengaluru:\nOuter Ring Road\nM.G. Road\nWhitefield Main Road\nHosur Road\n\nMumbai:\nWestern Express Highway\nS.V. Road\nLBS Marg\n\nDelhi:\nRing Road\nMG Road\nMathura Road\n\nOnly use an address that is plausible for the city/location specified in the dataset.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nIf coordinates are specified, the address should correspond to the same city/area.\n\nDo NOT display:\n\n\342\200\234Random Street\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Sample Street\342\200\235\n\n\342\200\234Unknown Road\342\200\235\n\nor similar placeholder addresses.\n\n==================================================\n16. ADDRESS + COORDINATE CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nAudit all mock issues for:\n\nCity\nState\nAddress\nLatitude\nLongitude\n\nThese fields must be geographically consistent.\n\nExample:\n\nDO NOT:\n\nAddress:\nRandom Street, Delhi\n\nCoordinates:\n13.7463, 80.3801\n\nbecause these coordinates are not Delhi.\n\nInstead, correct either the coordinates or the address so they represent the same geographic area.\n\nEvery issue must have internally consistent location data.\n\n==================================================\n17. FIX BEFORE / AFTER PHOTO MISMATCH\n==================================================\n\nTHIS IS CRITICAL.\n\nThe current prototype displays completely unrelated before/after images.\n\nThe screenshot shows an example where:\n\nBEFORE:\nA forest/water scene\n\nAFTER:\nShoes on a beach\n\nThis is unacceptable for a civic resolution system.\n\nThe before and after photos MUST depict the SAME CIVIC ISSUE / SAME LOCATION.\n\nExamples:\n\nPOTHOLE:\n\nBefore:\nLarge pothole on a specific road\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME road/location after the pothole has been repaired\n\nGARBAGE:\n\nBefore:\nGarbage pile at a specific roadside location\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME location after garbage has been removed\n\nBROKEN STREETLIGHT:\n\nBefore:\nBroken streetlight at a specific road\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME streetlight repaired/replaced\n\nOPEN MANHOLE:\n\nBefore:\nOpen manhole at a specific location\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME manhole safely covered/repaired\n\nDRAIN:\n\nBefore:\nOverflowing drain at a specific location\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME drain after clearing\n\nWATER LEAK:\n\nBefore:\nLeaking pipe at a specific location\n\nAfter:\nThe SAME pipe after repair\n\n==================================================\n18. BEFORE / AFTER IMAGE DATA MODEL\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT randomly assign images to beforeImage and afterImage.\n\nEach canonical civic issue should have an evidence pair.\n\nExample:\n\nIssue CIV-10482:\n\nbeforeImage:\npothole_anna_nagar_before.jpg\n\nafterImage:\npothole_anna_nagar_after.jpg\n\nIssue CIV-10483:\n\nbeforeImage:\ngarbage_t_nagar_before.jpg\n\nafterImage:\ngarbage_t_nagar_after.jpg\n\nThe pair must belong to the SAME physical issue.\n\n==================================================\n19. VISUAL CONSISTENCY OF BEFORE / AFTER\n==================================================\n\nThe before and after image should match as closely as possible in:\n\n- Location\n- Perspective\n- Infrastructure object\n- Surroundings\n- Road/building context\n\nOnly the civic problem should be changed.\n\nFor example:\n\nBEFORE:\nSame road\nSame building\nSame streetlight\nBroken lamp\n\nAFTER:\nSame road\nSame building\nSame streetlight\nWorking lamp\n\nDo NOT use unrelated stock images simply because they represent the same category.\n\n==================================================\n20. AUDIT ALL EXISTING ISSUES\n==================================================\n\nPerform a complete data audit of every existing mock issue.\n\nFor each issue verify:\n\n\342\234\223 Relevant image\n\342\234\223 Unique image where appropriate\n\342\234\223 Valid before image\n\342\234\223 Valid after image\n\342\234\223 Before and after refer to same issue\n\342\234\223 Realistic address\n\342\234\223 Correct city\n\342\234\223 Correct state\n\342\234\223 Correct coordinates\n\342\234\223 Correct jurisdiction\n\342\234\223 Correct issue category\n\342\234\223 Consistent status\n\342\234\223 Consistent authority\n\342\234\223 Consistent department\n\nFix every record that violates these requirements.\n\n==================================================\n21. PHOTO FALLBACK\n==================================================\n\nKeep the existing image fallback behavior.\n\nIf a primary image cannot load:\n\n\342\206\222 use a relevant category-specific fallback.\n\nNever display a broken image.\n\nBut do NOT solve missing images by assigning the same generic image to every issue.\n\n==================================================\n22. GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD DATA CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nEnsure:\n\nGovernment Overview\nIssue Queue\nLive Map\nIssue Detail\nAnalytics\nRecurring Hotspots\n\nall use the same underlying dataset.\n\nIf CIV-10482 has:\n\nCity:\nChennai\n\nAddress:\nAnna Salai\n\nJurisdiction:\nGreater Chennai Corporation\n\nthen those values should be identical everywhere CIV-10482 appears.\n\n==================================================\n23. FINAL TESTING\n==================================================\n\nPerform these tests before finishing.\n\nAUTHENTICATION:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Government\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nAll must work.\n\nSEARCH:\n\nSearch:\nChennai\n\342\206\222 Chennai records\n\nSearch:\nPothole\n\342\206\222 Pothole records\n\nSearch:\nCIV-10482\n\342\206\222 Exact issue\n\nEXPORT:\n\nClick:\nExport Report\n\n\342\206\222 CSV file downloads\n\nVerify that the CSV contains actual mock records.\n\nLOGO:\n\nClick logo\n\342\206\222 Correct home/dashboard\n\nMAP:\n\nOpen Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 India map loads\n\nVerify:\n- Only India is the visible geographic focus\n- State boundaries are visible\n- Heatmap displays\n- Mock civic reports appear\n- Multiple cities have report concentrations\n- Zoom works\n- Pan works\n- Filters work\n- Issue markers correspond to dataset\n- Clicking an issue opens correct details\n\nIMAGE:\n\nOpen at least 10 different issue records.\n\nVerify:\n- Images are relevant\n- Images are not all identical\n- Before/after pairs are related\n- No random blur circles appear\n- No broken images appear\n\nLOCATION:\n\nVerify no issue contains contradictory values such as:\n\n\342\200\234Delhi\342\200\235\nwith Chennai coordinates.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe final prototype must communicate:\n\nCITIZEN SIDE:\nSimple\nAccessible\nMultilingual\nCamera-first\nPrivacy-conscious\n\nGOVERNMENT SIDE:\nIndia-wide\nDetailed\nData-rich\nSearchable\nExportable\nGeospatial\nOperational\n\nThe Government Dashboard should clearly demonstrate:\n\nREAL INDIA MAP\n+\nCITIZEN REPORT HEATMAP\n+\nINDIAN CIVIC ISSUE DATA\n+\nJURISDICTION INFORMATION\n+\nSEARCH\n+\nEXPORT\n+\nDETAILED ISSUE RECORDS\n\nThe citizen side should remain simple and should NOT expose:\n\nAI terminology\nInternal workflow\nPriority algorithms\nRouting logic\nTechnical system details\n\nFinally, preserve the exact official product name everywhere:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235\n\nDo not introduce or restore any alternative product name."
