    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m zeroing in on defining the precise scope for the fix, quality, and navigation enhancements. The goal is a truly comprehensive update. I\'m prioritizing key areas for the \"Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\" prototype. I need to be exact.\n\n\n**Refining the Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics: removing the face blur, fixing the role-switching buttons, and ensuring the Gov Map focuses exclusively on India with a heatmap. I\'m also streamlining the terminology, making the export button functional, and implementing other straightforward updates like a clickable logo and a functional search bar. I need to make sure the addresses are realistic.\n\n\n**Mapping the Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m analyzing the codebase to solidify the implementation plan. I\'m focusing on the auth logic in `Flow.tsx` and app state management within `AppContext.tsx`. Citizen and Gov side components are also being assessed, focusing on routing via state (`currentScreen`) and identifying where the face blur function exists. I\'m planning to focus on the Auth and Navigation updates next. I will need to make sure the app correctly supports the Sign Out and Role switch, which means reviewing `logout` and `setActiveApp` in `AppContext.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing the Switch**\n\nI\'m implementing the switch now. The role-switching logic will utilize `window.confirm` to provide confirmation before triggering `logout()` and updating the active application via `setActiveApp(...)`. I\'m starting work on removing the face-blur effect by seeking elements in `IssueDetail.tsx` and citizen-facing image displays. I am using `blur`, `privacyProcessed`, `facesBlurred`, `canvas`, or filter elements as keywords.\nI am also starting updates to mock data to have realistic coordinates, streets, and to use matched or identical images with grayscale. I will use `loremflickr` or similar trick.\n\n\n**Addressing Image Matching**\n\nI am now addressing the image matching challenge. Since I can\'t generate new images, I\'ll employ known pairs if available. For unresolved issues, I\'ll only show the \"before\" image. For resolved issues, I\'ll show the same image for \"before\" and \"after,\" potentially with a CSS tweak to simulate the change. My focus is on ensuring the \"before\" and \"after\" images represent the same physical issue, respecting the user\'s constraints. I may omit the after photo on open issues.\n\n\n**Focusing on Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the search and export features for the government dashboard, specifically within `IssueQueue.tsx` and `Overview.tsx` respectively. I\'m also working on the India-specific map in `LiveMap.tsx`, focusing on setting the correct bounds and integrating a heatmap layer to visualize citizen report density. I will need to ensure a good map experience. I have updated the data so that the screenshots show matching images.\n\n\n"
