  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Authentication Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining the authentication flow in `MainApp`. The conditional rendering `if (authState !== \'AUTHENTICATED\' || !user) { return <AuthFlow />; }` is crucial. The `authState` state is derived from `useApp()`, specifically, `activeApp`, `citizenAuthState` and `govUser` variables, which may reveal opportunities for improving the logic.\n\n\n**Refining Authentication Flow**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `logout()` function\'s behavior in relation to app switching. It seems it only clears the session for the currently active app, leaving the other potentially authenticated. This means if a user switches from GOV to CITIZEN after previously being authenticated as a citizen, the authentication check bypasses the `AuthFlow` component and renders directly into the `CitizenApp`, which is a potential security vulnerability.\n\n\n**Implementing Session Clearing**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring a clean logout process across both user roles. Currently, the `logout()` function only clears the active session. To resolve this, I\'m modifying `logout()` to clear both the government and citizen sessions. This will ensure that a switch between accounts always results in a fully authenticated state change. The primary goal is a complete sign-out for each role, resetting the user to the welcome screen for either sign-in, or role selection.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 111816657
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
