steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787858263
      nanos: 209948654
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "IMPORTANT:\nPerform a TARGETED FUNCTIONAL FIX on the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nDO NOT redesign the application.\nDO NOT change the existing visual identity.\nDO NOT remove existing citizen or government functionality.\n\nFix ONLY these four issues:\n\n1. Citizen Sign Out still does not work.\n2. \342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235 still does not work.\n3. Government map is blocked by \342\200\234API key required\342\200\235.\n4. India map / heatmap needs to be much more detailed and geographically restricted.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 COMPLETELY FIX SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nThe current Sign Out button still does not work.\n\nDo NOT simply add another button.\nAudit the CURRENT authentication, state management, event handlers and routing.\n\nThe sign-out action MUST actually:\n\n1. Clear the active authenticated session.\n2. Clear the current role.\n3. Update application state immediately.\n4. Redirect to the ROLE SELECTION screen.\n5. Prevent access to the authenticated dashboard after sign-out.\n6. Work without refreshing the browser.\n7. Work repeatedly.\n\nUse separate state for:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated\ngovernmentAuthenticated\ncurrentRole\n\nDo NOT use one shared:\n\nauthenticated = true\n\nstate for both environments.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCITIZEN SIGN OUT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\nThen:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated = false\ncurrentRole = null\n\nRedirect to:\n\nROLE SELECTION\n\nDo NOT delete:\n\n- Citizen account\n- Reports\n- Language preference\n- Mock data\n- Images\n- Issue history\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nGOVERNMENT SIGN OUT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\nThen:\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated = false\ncurrentRole = null\n\nRedirect to:\n\nROLE SELECTION\n\nDo NOT delete any civic data.\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 COMPLETELY FIX \342\200\234SWITCH TO CITIZEN\342\200\235\n==================================================\n\nThe existing:\n\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nbutton does nothing.\n\nMake it functional.\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Clear government session\n\342\206\222 Clear currentRole\n\342\206\222 Navigate to Role Selection\n\nRole Selection:\n\n[CITIZEN]\n[MUNICIPAL STAFF]\n\nClick:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Demo Authentication\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nThis must work WITHOUT:\n\n- browser refresh\n- manually clearing localStorage\n- restarting the app\n- closing/reopening the browser\n\nAlso implement the reverse:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\n==================================================\nPART 3 \342\200\224 BUILD A RELIABLE ROLE SELECTION ROUTE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a dedicated route/state for:\n\nROLE SELECTION\n\nExample:\n\n/select-role\n\nDisplay:\n\nCrowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\n\nChoose how you want to continue:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nThe role-selection screen must be reachable after sign-out.\n\nMake sure the routing logic actually allows the user to reach this screen from both dashboards.\n\n==================================================\nPART 4 \342\200\224 REMOVE THE GOOGLE MAPS API KEY DEPENDENCY\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Government Dashboard map says:\n\n\342\200\234API key required\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT leave the application dependent on an unavailable Google Maps API key.\n\nFor this prototype, REPLACE the Google Maps implementation with:\n\nLEAFLET + OPENSTREETMAP\n\nUse:\n\nLeaflet\n+\nOpenStreetMap map tiles\n+\nLeaflet Heatmap / Leaflet.heat or equivalent reliable heatmap implementation\n\nThis should work without a Google Maps API key.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT use a fake/static image pretending to be a map.\n\nThe map must be genuinely interactive.\n\nUsers must be able to:\n\n- Zoom\n- Pan within India\n- Click issue locations\n- View issue details\n- Use heatmap visualization\n\nInclude proper OpenStreetMap attribution:\n\n\302\251 OpenStreetMap contributors\n\n==================================================\nPART 5 \342\200\224 INDIA-ONLY MAP\n==================================================\n\nThe map must be geographically restricted to INDIA.\n\nThe user must NOT be able to:\n\n- Pan into Pakistan\n- Pan into Bangladesh\n- Pan into Nepal\n- Pan into Bhutan\n- Pan into Sri Lanka\n- Pan into China\n- Pan to Europe / Africa / other countries\n\nUse Leaflet maxBounds / equivalent geographic constraints.\n\nDefine appropriate bounds around India\'s territory and set:\n\nmaxBounds\n\nand\n\nmaxBoundsViscosity\n\nso the map cannot be freely dragged outside the India region.\n\nAlso set a minimum zoom level that keeps the viewport reasonably focused on India.\n\nDo NOT make the map so zoomed out that large amounts of neighbouring countries are visible.\n\n==================================================\nPART 6 \342\200\224 INITIAL MAP VIEW\n==================================================\n\nWhen the Government Dashboard loads:\n\nCenter the map on INDIA.\n\nFit the map to India\'s geographic bounds.\n\nIndia should occupy most of the visible map.\n\nDo NOT initially show the entire South Asia region.\n\nThe visual focus must clearly be India.\n\n==================================================\nPART 7 \342\200\224 DETAILED INDIA MAP\n==================================================\n\nThe map should have useful geographic detail.\n\nShow where supported:\n\n- Indian state boundaries\n- Major cities\n- Major roads\n- Urban areas\n- Geographic context\n\nAt normal zoom levels the user should be able to clearly distinguish major Indian regions and cities.\n\nUse appropriate OpenStreetMap tiles and Leaflet layers.\n\nDo NOT add unnecessary map clutter.\n\n==================================================\nPART 8 \342\200\224 DETAILED CIVIC REPORT HEATMAP\n==================================================\n\nImprove the current heatmap substantially.\n\nThe heatmap should represent:\n\nCITIZEN REPORT DENSITY\n\nThe mock report dataset should provide:\n\nlatitude\nlongitude\nissueType\npriority\nstatus\ncity\nstate\ntimestamp\n\nGenerate a significantly larger mock dataset.\n\nUse at least:\n\n150\342\200\223300 mock citizen reports\n\ndistributed across multiple Indian urban areas.\n\nInclude concentrations in cities such as:\n\nChennai\nCoimbatore\nMadurai\nBengaluru\nHyderabad\nMumbai\nDelhi\nKolkata\nPune\nAhmedabad\nJaipur\nLucknow\nKochi\nPune\nVisakhapatnam\n\nDo NOT distribute reports uniformly across India.\n\nCreate realistic urban concentrations.\n\nFor example:\n\nMajor city:\nHigh concentration\n\nSmaller city:\nModerate concentration\n\nRural / low-data areas:\nLow concentration\n\n==================================================\nPART 9 \342\200\224 MAKE THE HEATMAP MORE DETAILED\n==================================================\n\nUse a smoother density visualization.\n\nIncrease:\n\n- Point count\n- Resolution\n- Radius tuning\n- Blur tuning\n- Intensity variation\n\nThe heatmap should visibly show:\n\nLow-density zones\nModerate-density zones\nHigh-density hotspots\n\nDo NOT simply place giant circles over cities.\n\nThe density must be generated from individual report coordinates.\n\nExample:\n\n50 reports around Chennai Central\n\342\206\222 dense hotspot\n\n15 reports around Coimbatore\n\342\206\222 moderate hotspot\n\n5 reports around Madurai\n\342\206\222 smaller hotspot\n\n==================================================\nPART 10 \342\200\224 HEATMAP SHOULD REPRESENT REPORTS, NOT JUST ISSUES\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe heatmap should represent the NUMBER / DENSITY of citizen reports.\n\nIf 100 citizens report nearby civic problems:\n\n\342\206\222 stronger heat intensity\n\nIf only 5 reports exist:\n\n\342\206\222 weaker heat intensity\n\nThis should make the heatmap a visual representation of:\n\n\342\200\234Where are citizens reporting civic problems?\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nPART 11 \342\200\224 ISSUE MARKER MODE\n==================================================\n\nKeep an option to switch between:\n\n[ Heatmap ]\n\n[ Issues ]\n\nHEATMAP:\nShows overall citizen-report density.\n\nISSUES:\nShows individual canonical civic issues.\n\nMarkers should use priority/status indicators.\n\nCritical:\nRed\n\nHigh:\nOrange\n\nMedium:\nYellow\n\nLow:\nGreen\n\nResolved:\nMuted / neutral\n\nDo not clutter the map.\n\n==================================================\nPART 12 \342\200\224 MAP FILTERS\n==================================================\n\nThe existing Government filters should control the map.\n\nFilters:\n\nCity\nState\nIssue Type\nPriority\nStatus\nDepartment\nLanguage\n\nExample:\n\nFilter:\nChennai\n\n\342\206\222 Heatmap updates to Chennai data\n\342\206\222 Issue markers update to Chennai\n\nFilter:\nCritical\n\n\342\206\222 Heatmap updates accordingly\n\342\206\222 Critical issue markers remain\n\nFilter:\nPothole\n\n\342\206\222 Heatmap shows pothole-report density\n\nThe map must use the SAME underlying dataset as:\n\nGovernment Overview\nIssue Queue\nIssue Details\nAnalytics\nRecurring Hotspots\n\nDo not create a disconnected map-only dataset.\n\n==================================================\nPART 13 \342\200\224 MAP \342\206\224 ISSUE QUEUE SYNCHRONIZATION\n==================================================\n\nWhen a user clicks an issue in the Issue Queue:\n\n\342\206\222 Center map on that issue\n\342\206\222 Highlight its marker\n\342\206\222 Open issue information if appropriate\n\nWhen a user clicks a map issue marker:\n\n\342\206\222 Open the corresponding Issue Detail screen\n\nBoth must reference the same issue object.\n\n==================================================\nPART 14 \342\200\224 INDIA MAP LEGEND\n==================================================\n\nAdd a compact legend:\n\nHEATMAP:\nLow reports\n\342\206\222 High reports\n\nISSUES:\nCritical\nHigh\nMedium\nLow\nResolved\n\nKeep the legend unobtrusive.\n\n==================================================\nPART 15 \342\200\224 REALISTIC INDIAN GEOGRAPHIC DATA\n==================================================\n\nEnsure every mock report has geographically consistent:\n\nlatitude\nlongitude\ncity\nstate\naddress\n\nFor example:\n\nChennai coordinates\n\342\206\222 Chennai address\n\nDelhi coordinates\n\342\206\222 Delhi address\n\nMumbai coordinates\n\342\206\222 Mumbai address\n\nDo NOT use contradictory combinations.\n\nRemove any remaining placeholder addresses such as:\n\nRandom Street\nSample Street\nUnknown Road\n\n==================================================\nPART 16 \342\200\224 MAP DATA SHOULD BE CLEARLY MARKED AS DEMO DATA\n==================================================\n\nThe base map is real.\n\nThe civic report data is simulated.\n\nShow a small label:\n\n\342\200\234Demo Civic Data\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT imply these are real live municipal reports.\n\n==================================================\nPART 17 \342\200\224 MAP FAILURE HANDLING\n==================================================\n\nThe map must NEVER show:\n\n\342\200\234API key required\342\200\235\n\nas the normal application state.\n\nIf the tile provider fails, show:\n\n\342\200\234Map temporarily unavailable\342\200\235\n\nwith:\n\n\342\200\234Retry\342\200\235\n\nbutton.\n\nBut under normal conditions, Leaflet + OpenStreetMap must load without requiring a Google Maps API key.\n\n==================================================\nPART 18 \342\200\224 DO NOT BREAK CURRENT FEATURES\n==================================================\n\nPreserve:\n\n- Tamil language\n- Hindi language\n- English language\n- GPS-based language selection\n- Manual language switching\n- Persistent citizen account\n- Demo Aadhaar verification\n- Camera-first reporting\n- Offline reporting\n- Citizen issue tracking\n- Citizen resolution verification\n- Citizen reopening\n- Privacy feature\n- Government dashboard\n- Government issue queue\n- Government analytics\n- Existing mock data\n- Unique report images\n- Before/after evidence\n- Official product name\n\nDo NOT reintroduce:\n\n- AI terminology on citizen screens\n- Internal workflow on citizen screens\n- Automated jurisdiction routing\n\nJurisdiction should remain displayed as issue information only.\n\n==================================================\nPART 19 \342\200\224 FINAL AUTHENTICATION TEST\n==================================================\n\nPerform these exact tests:\n\nTEST 1:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nTEST 2:\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nTEST 3:\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nTEST 4:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nTEST 5:\n\nCitizen Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirm browser storage still contains data\n\342\206\222 Login as Government\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard works\n\nTEST 6:\n\nGovernment Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Login as Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard works\n\n==================================================\nPART 20 \342\200\224 FINAL MAP TEST\n==================================================\n\nPerform these tests:\n\n1. Open Government Dashboard\n2. India is the initial map view\n3. Only India is visible as the geographic focus\n4. User cannot freely pan into neighbouring countries\n5. Map zoom works\n6. Map pan works inside India\n7. State boundaries are visible\n8. Heatmap loads\n9. Heatmap contains many civic-report concentrations\n10. Multiple Indian cities have report clusters\n11. Filters change the heatmap\n12. Issue mode displays individual reports/issues\n13. Clicking an issue opens the correct issue\n14. Issue Queue can center the map on an issue\n15. No API key warning appears\n16. No broken map container appears\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe final Government Dashboard should provide:\n\nREAL INTERACTIVE INDIA MAP\n+\nINDIA-ONLY NAVIGATION\n+\nDETAILED GEOGRAPHIC CONTEXT\n+\nHIGH-DENSITY CIVIC REPORT HEATMAP\n+\nINDIVIDUAL ISSUE MODE\n+\nFILTERING\n+\nISSUE INTERACTION\n+\nSHARED MOCK DATA\n\nAnd the application must allow seamless:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 SIGN OUT\n\342\206\222 ROLE SELECTION\n\342\206\222 GOVERNMENT\n\342\206\222 SIGN OUT\n\342\206\222 ROLE SELECTION\n\342\206\222 CITIZEN\n\nwithout restarting or manually clearing browser storage.\n\nDo NOT change the official product name:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    items {
      text: "IMPORTANT:\nPerform a TARGETED FUNCTIONAL FIX on the existing\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nDO NOT redesign the application.\nDO NOT change the existing visual identity.\nDO NOT remove existing citizen or government functionality.\n\nFix ONLY these four issues:\n\n1. Citizen Sign Out still does not work.\n2. \342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235 still does not work.\n3. Government map is blocked by \342\200\234API key required\342\200\235.\n4. India map / heatmap needs to be much more detailed and geographically restricted.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 COMPLETELY FIX SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nThe current Sign Out button still does not work.\n\nDo NOT simply add another button.\nAudit the CURRENT authentication, state management, event handlers and routing.\n\nThe sign-out action MUST actually:\n\n1. Clear the active authenticated session.\n2. Clear the current role.\n3. Update application state immediately.\n4. Redirect to the ROLE SELECTION screen.\n5. Prevent access to the authenticated dashboard after sign-out.\n6. Work without refreshing the browser.\n7. Work repeatedly.\n\nUse separate state for:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated\ngovernmentAuthenticated\ncurrentRole\n\nDo NOT use one shared:\n\nauthenticated = true\n\nstate for both environments.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCITIZEN SIGN OUT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nCitizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\nThen:\n\ncitizenAuthenticated = false\ncurrentRole = null\n\nRedirect to:\n\nROLE SELECTION\n\nDo NOT delete:\n\n- Citizen account\n- Reports\n- Language preference\n- Mock data\n- Images\n- Issue history\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nGOVERNMENT SIGN OUT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\nThen:\n\ngovernmentAuthenticated = false\ncurrentRole = null\n\nRedirect to:\n\nROLE SELECTION\n\nDo NOT delete any civic data.\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 COMPLETELY FIX \342\200\234SWITCH TO CITIZEN\342\200\235\n==================================================\n\nThe existing:\n\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nbutton does nothing.\n\nMake it functional.\n\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\342\206\222 Clear government session\n\342\206\222 Clear currentRole\n\342\206\222 Navigate to Role Selection\n\nRole Selection:\n\n[CITIZEN]\n[MUNICIPAL STAFF]\n\nClick:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Demo Authentication\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nThis must work WITHOUT:\n\n- browser refresh\n- manually clearing localStorage\n- restarting the app\n- closing/reopening the browser\n\nAlso implement the reverse:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\n==================================================\nPART 3 \342\200\224 BUILD A RELIABLE ROLE SELECTION ROUTE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a dedicated route/state for:\n\nROLE SELECTION\n\nExample:\n\n/select-role\n\nDisplay:\n\nCrowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\n\nChoose how you want to continue:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nThe role-selection screen must be reachable after sign-out.\n\nMake sure the routing logic actually allows the user to reach this screen from both dashboards.\n\n==================================================\nPART 4 \342\200\224 REMOVE THE GOOGLE MAPS API KEY DEPENDENCY\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Government Dashboard map says:\n\n\342\200\234API key required\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT leave the application dependent on an unavailable Google Maps API key.\n\nFor this prototype, REPLACE the Google Maps implementation with:\n\nLEAFLET + OPENSTREETMAP\n\nUse:\n\nLeaflet\n+\nOpenStreetMap map tiles\n+\nLeaflet Heatmap / Leaflet.heat or equivalent reliable heatmap implementation\n\nThis should work without a Google Maps API key.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT use a fake/static image pretending to be a map.\n\nThe map must be genuinely interactive.\n\nUsers must be able to:\n\n- Zoom\n- Pan within India\n- Click issue locations\n- View issue details\n- Use heatmap visualization\n\nInclude proper OpenStreetMap attribution:\n\n\302\251 OpenStreetMap contributors\n\n==================================================\nPART 5 \342\200\224 INDIA-ONLY MAP\n==================================================\n\nThe map must be geographically restricted to INDIA.\n\nThe user must NOT be able to:\n\n- Pan into Pakistan\n- Pan into Bangladesh\n- Pan into Nepal\n- Pan into Bhutan\n- Pan into Sri Lanka\n- Pan into China\n- Pan to Europe / Africa / other countries\n\nUse Leaflet maxBounds / equivalent geographic constraints.\n\nDefine appropriate bounds around India\'s territory and set:\n\nmaxBounds\n\nand\n\nmaxBoundsViscosity\n\nso the map cannot be freely dragged outside the India region.\n\nAlso set a minimum zoom level that keeps the viewport reasonably focused on India.\n\nDo NOT make the map so zoomed out that large amounts of neighbouring countries are visible.\n\n==================================================\nPART 6 \342\200\224 INITIAL MAP VIEW\n==================================================\n\nWhen the Government Dashboard loads:\n\nCenter the map on INDIA.\n\nFit the map to India\'s geographic bounds.\n\nIndia should occupy most of the visible map.\n\nDo NOT initially show the entire South Asia region.\n\nThe visual focus must clearly be India.\n\n==================================================\nPART 7 \342\200\224 DETAILED INDIA MAP\n==================================================\n\nThe map should have useful geographic detail.\n\nShow where supported:\n\n- Indian state boundaries\n- Major cities\n- Major roads\n- Urban areas\n- Geographic context\n\nAt normal zoom levels the user should be able to clearly distinguish major Indian regions and cities.\n\nUse appropriate OpenStreetMap tiles and Leaflet layers.\n\nDo NOT add unnecessary map clutter.\n\n==================================================\nPART 8 \342\200\224 DETAILED CIVIC REPORT HEATMAP\n==================================================\n\nImprove the current heatmap substantially.\n\nThe heatmap should represent:\n\nCITIZEN REPORT DENSITY\n\nThe mock report dataset should provide:\n\nlatitude\nlongitude\nissueType\npriority\nstatus\ncity\nstate\ntimestamp\n\nGenerate a significantly larger mock dataset.\n\nUse at least:\n\n150\342\200\223300 mock citizen reports\n\ndistributed across multiple Indian urban areas.\n\nInclude concentrations in cities such as:\n\nChennai\nCoimbatore\nMadurai\nBengaluru\nHyderabad\nMumbai\nDelhi\nKolkata\nPune\nAhmedabad\nJaipur\nLucknow\nKochi\nPune\nVisakhapatnam\n\nDo NOT distribute reports uniformly across India.\n\nCreate realistic urban concentrations.\n\nFor example:\n\nMajor city:\nHigh concentration\n\nSmaller city:\nModerate concentration\n\nRural / low-data areas:\nLow concentration\n\n==================================================\nPART 9 \342\200\224 MAKE THE HEATMAP MORE DETAILED\n==================================================\n\nUse a smoother density visualization.\n\nIncrease:\n\n- Point count\n- Resolution\n- Radius tuning\n- Blur tuning\n- Intensity variation\n\nThe heatmap should visibly show:\n\nLow-density zones\nModerate-density zones\nHigh-density hotspots\n\nDo NOT simply place giant circles over cities.\n\nThe density must be generated from individual report coordinates.\n\nExample:\n\n50 reports around Chennai Central\n\342\206\222 dense hotspot\n\n15 reports around Coimbatore\n\342\206\222 moderate hotspot\n\n5 reports around Madurai\n\342\206\222 smaller hotspot\n\n==================================================\nPART 10 \342\200\224 HEATMAP SHOULD REPRESENT REPORTS, NOT JUST ISSUES\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe heatmap should represent the NUMBER / DENSITY of citizen reports.\n\nIf 100 citizens report nearby civic problems:\n\n\342\206\222 stronger heat intensity\n\nIf only 5 reports exist:\n\n\342\206\222 weaker heat intensity\n\nThis should make the heatmap a visual representation of:\n\n\342\200\234Where are citizens reporting civic problems?\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nPART 11 \342\200\224 ISSUE MARKER MODE\n==================================================\n\nKeep an option to switch between:\n\n[ Heatmap ]\n\n[ Issues ]\n\nHEATMAP:\nShows overall citizen-report density.\n\nISSUES:\nShows individual canonical civic issues.\n\nMarkers should use priority/status indicators.\n\nCritical:\nRed\n\nHigh:\nOrange\n\nMedium:\nYellow\n\nLow:\nGreen\n\nResolved:\nMuted / neutral\n\nDo not clutter the map.\n\n==================================================\nPART 12 \342\200\224 MAP FILTERS\n==================================================\n\nThe existing Government filters should control the map.\n\nFilters:\n\nCity\nState\nIssue Type\nPriority\nStatus\nDepartment\nLanguage\n\nExample:\n\nFilter:\nChennai\n\n\342\206\222 Heatmap updates to Chennai data\n\342\206\222 Issue markers update to Chennai\n\nFilter:\nCritical\n\n\342\206\222 Heatmap updates accordingly\n\342\206\222 Critical issue markers remain\n\nFilter:\nPothole\n\n\342\206\222 Heatmap shows pothole-report density\n\nThe map must use the SAME underlying dataset as:\n\nGovernment Overview\nIssue Queue\nIssue Details\nAnalytics\nRecurring Hotspots\n\nDo not create a disconnected map-only dataset.\n\n==================================================\nPART 13 \342\200\224 MAP \342\206\224 ISSUE QUEUE SYNCHRONIZATION\n==================================================\n\nWhen a user clicks an issue in the Issue Queue:\n\n\342\206\222 Center map on that issue\n\342\206\222 Highlight its marker\n\342\206\222 Open issue information if appropriate\n\nWhen a user clicks a map issue marker:\n\n\342\206\222 Open the corresponding Issue Detail screen\n\nBoth must reference the same issue object.\n\n==================================================\nPART 14 \342\200\224 INDIA MAP LEGEND\n==================================================\n\nAdd a compact legend:\n\nHEATMAP:\nLow reports\n\342\206\222 High reports\n\nISSUES:\nCritical\nHigh\nMedium\nLow\nResolved\n\nKeep the legend unobtrusive.\n\n==================================================\nPART 15 \342\200\224 REALISTIC INDIAN GEOGRAPHIC DATA\n==================================================\n\nEnsure every mock report has geographically consistent:\n\nlatitude\nlongitude\ncity\nstate\naddress\n\nFor example:\n\nChennai coordinates\n\342\206\222 Chennai address\n\nDelhi coordinates\n\342\206\222 Delhi address\n\nMumbai coordinates\n\342\206\222 Mumbai address\n\nDo NOT use contradictory combinations.\n\nRemove any remaining placeholder addresses such as:\n\nRandom Street\nSample Street\nUnknown Road\n\n==================================================\nPART 16 \342\200\224 MAP DATA SHOULD BE CLEARLY MARKED AS DEMO DATA\n==================================================\n\nThe base map is real.\n\nThe civic report data is simulated.\n\nShow a small label:\n\n\342\200\234Demo Civic Data\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT imply these are real live municipal reports.\n\n==================================================\nPART 17 \342\200\224 MAP FAILURE HANDLING\n==================================================\n\nThe map must NEVER show:\n\n\342\200\234API key required\342\200\235\n\nas the normal application state.\n\nIf the tile provider fails, show:\n\n\342\200\234Map temporarily unavailable\342\200\235\n\nwith:\n\n\342\200\234Retry\342\200\235\n\nbutton.\n\nBut under normal conditions, Leaflet + OpenStreetMap must load without requiring a Google Maps API key.\n\n==================================================\nPART 18 \342\200\224 DO NOT BREAK CURRENT FEATURES\n==================================================\n\nPreserve:\n\n- Tamil language\n- Hindi language\n- English language\n- GPS-based language selection\n- Manual language switching\n- Persistent citizen account\n- Demo Aadhaar verification\n- Camera-first reporting\n- Offline reporting\n- Citizen issue tracking\n- Citizen resolution verification\n- Citizen reopening\n- Privacy feature\n- Government dashboard\n- Government issue queue\n- Government analytics\n- Existing mock data\n- Unique report images\n- Before/after evidence\n- Official product name\n\nDo NOT reintroduce:\n\n- AI terminology on citizen screens\n- Internal workflow on citizen screens\n- Automated jurisdiction routing\n\nJurisdiction should remain displayed as issue information only.\n\n==================================================\nPART 19 \342\200\224 FINAL AUTHENTICATION TEST\n==================================================\n\nPerform these exact tests:\n\nTEST 1:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nTEST 2:\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nTEST 3:\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nTEST 4:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nTEST 5:\n\nCitizen Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirm browser storage still contains data\n\342\206\222 Login as Government\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard works\n\nTEST 6:\n\nGovernment Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Login as Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard works\n\n==================================================\nPART 20 \342\200\224 FINAL MAP TEST\n==================================================\n\nPerform these tests:\n\n1. Open Government Dashboard\n2. India is the initial map view\n3. Only India is visible as the geographic focus\n4. User cannot freely pan into neighbouring countries\n5. Map zoom works\n6. Map pan works inside India\n7. State boundaries are visible\n8. Heatmap loads\n9. Heatmap contains many civic-report concentrations\n10. Multiple Indian cities have report clusters\n11. Filters change the heatmap\n12. Issue mode displays individual reports/issues\n13. Clicking an issue opens the correct issue\n14. Issue Queue can center the map on an issue\n15. No API key warning appears\n16. No broken map container appears\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe final Government Dashboard should provide:\n\nREAL INTERACTIVE INDIA MAP\n+\nINDIA-ONLY NAVIGATION\n+\nDETAILED GEOGRAPHIC CONTEXT\n+\nHIGH-DENSITY CIVIC REPORT HEATMAP\n+\nINDIVIDUAL ISSUE MODE\n+\nFILTERING\n+\nISSUE INTERACTION\n+\nSHARED MOCK DATA\n\nAnd the application must allow seamless:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 SIGN OUT\n\342\206\222 ROLE SELECTION\n\342\206\222 GOVERNMENT\n\342\206\222 SIGN OUT\n\342\206\222 ROLE SELECTION\n\342\206\222 CITIZEN\n\nwithout restarting or manually clearing browser storage.\n\nDo NOT change the official product name:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    }
  }
}
