  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Data Relationships**\n\nI\'ve realized `MyReports` displays all issues, not those specific to a user. This prototype doesn\'t link issues to user IDs; it uses global mock issues. Therefore, creating a new `mockUser` on login doesn\'t clear any existing reports or history! The \"Citizen account\" is completely\342\200\246\n\n\n**Verifying Control Flow**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the \"Citizen\" login flow is perfect! Setting `cscirr_citizen_auth` to `\'false\'` simulates a complete sign-out, as the `activeApp` gets reset. Clicking \"Citizen\" then sets `activeApp=\'CITIZEN\'` and forces the citizen demo auth screen due to the `cscirr_citizen_auth` value. This is exactly what\'s needed for the \"Citizen\" flow. The `MainApp` logic is solid, ensuring the correct authentication screen is shown.\n\n\n**Confirming Login Logic**\n\nThe \"Citizen\" authentication flow is now completely verified! I\'ve confirmed that the logic in `MainApp` correctly routes to `<AuthFlow />` when `authState` is `\'NOT_AUTHENTICATED\'` and `activeApp` is `\'CITIZEN\'`, as expected. The `loginCitizen` function seamlessly updates state, leading to the display of `<CitizenApp />` after successful authentication. The removal of `setCitizenUser(null)` does not affect functionality, as `authState` correctly drives the rendering. This makes the `fix_citizen_account.cjs` changes redundant.\n\n\n**Validating Logout Functionality**\n\nI\'m now verifying the functionality of `govLogout`. It correctly sets `cscirr_gov_auth` to false. Clicking \"Municipal Staff\" in Role Selection will trigger the `GOV_AUTH` screen because `authState` will be `NOT_AUTHENTICATED`. I\'ve double-checked the `useEffect` hook in `AppContext.tsx` for localStorage; if `storedCitizenAuth` is false, it won\'t...\n\n\n**Reviewing System Requirements**\n\nI\'m now completely confident in the current state. The `logout` function remains intact and functional. Everything aligns with the prompt\'s instructions. Citizen sign-out works perfectly via `citizenLogout`, and switching to Citizen works via `govLogout`, redirecting correctly. The government map is appropriately blocked by the required API key, as expected. I\'ve finished a quick review of all the final requirements.\n\n\n**Finalizing Map Implementation**\n\nI\'ve completed the India map. It now features much greater detail within geographic bounds, focusing on major cities with a cluster of 250 reports. The heatmap represents reports, using `reportsCount` for weight. Markers and heatmaps can be toggled. Map filters are integrated, and the issue queue synchronizes perfectly. I\'ve added a demo data overlay, implemented a tile error handler, and ensured no AI terminology appears on citizen screens.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 475225719
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
