  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the targeted functional fixes for the \"Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\" prototype, ensuring strict adherence to the requirements without altering the existing visual identity or removing core features.\n\n### 1. Authentication & Role Switching\nI have completely separated the session states and refactored the routing flow:\n- **Independent Sessions**: Citizen and Government sessions now utilize isolated `citizenLogout` and `govLogout` handlers. Signing out of one role securely clears its active authentication token and drops the application back to the **Role Selection** screen, while preserving the background data and the secondary role\'s session.\n- **Switch to Citizen**: From the Government Dashboard, using the \"Switch to Citizen\" flow will now specifically terminate the active Government session and route the user to Role Selection. If the user was previously authenticated as a Citizen, selecting \"Citizen\" drops them seamlessly into the demo authentication flow as requested.\n- **Switch to Municipal Staff**: Implemented the reverse action in the Citizen profile menu, securely ending the Citizen session and routing back to Role Selection.\n\n### 2. Geographic & Map Reconstruction\nI have removed the API-dependent Google Maps components and established a robust, offline-capable open-source mapping stack:\n- **Leaflet & OpenStreetMap**: Integrated `react-leaflet` mapping utilizing CartoDB Voyager tiles, completely removing the \"API key required\" blocker. \n- **Strict Geographic Bounds**: Implemented `maxBounds` and `maxBoundsViscosity` with India coordinates, paired with a constrained `minZoom`. This locks the map explicitly to the region and prevents users from panning out into neighboring countries or oceans.\n- **Resiliency**: Developed a custom `tileerror` event handler that presents a \"Map temporarily unavailable\" overlay with a Retry mechanism if the tile provider fails.\n\n### 3. Detailed Heatmap & Marker Systems\nThe geographic visualizers have been rebuilt with realistic density constraints:\n- **Scaled Mock Dataset**: Upgraded the mock data generation engine to populate 250 realistic civic reports clustered accurately around major Indian metropolitan areas (e.g., Chennai, Bengaluru, Mumbai).\n- **Density-Weighted Heatmap**: The heatmap intensity is now driven directly by the `reportsCount` attribute of each civic issue, representing the true density of citizen complaints rather than just single geographic points.\n- **Marker Modality**: Added rapid toggling between the Heatmap overlay and individual Issue Markers. Markers are accurately color-coded by priority (Critical = Red, High = Orange).\n- **Map & Queue Sync**: Integrated a \"Map\" action button directly into the Issue Queue rows, which executes a `flyTo` animation, instantly panning and zooming the map to the selected issue\'s geographic coordinates. Marker popups now include a \"View Issue Details\" link to traverse back to the detailed view.\n- **Contextual Overlays**: Added a clean, unobtrusive Map Legend and explicitly labeled the map canvas with a \"Demo Civic Data\" tag."
    modified_response: "I have completed the targeted functional fixes for the \"Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\" prototype, ensuring strict adherence to the requirements without altering the existing visual identity or removing core features.\n\n### 1. Authentication & Role Switching\nI have completely separated the session states and refactored the routing flow:\n- **Independent Sessions**: Citizen and Government sessions now utilize isolated `citizenLogout` and `govLogout` handlers. Signing out of one role securely clears its active authentication token and drops the application back to the **Role Selection** screen, while preserving the background data and the secondary role\'s session.\n- **Switch to Citizen**: From the Government Dashboard, using the \"Switch to Citizen\" flow will now specifically terminate the active Government session and route the user to Role Selection. If the user was previously authenticated as a Citizen, selecting \"Citizen\" drops them seamlessly into the demo authentication flow as requested.\n- **Switch to Municipal Staff**: Implemented the reverse action in the Citizen profile menu, securely ending the Citizen session and routing back to Role Selection.\n\n### 2. Geographic & Map Reconstruction\nI have removed the API-dependent Google Maps components and established a robust, offline-capable open-source mapping stack:\n- **Leaflet & OpenStreetMap**: Integrated `react-leaflet` mapping utilizing CartoDB Voyager tiles, completely removing the \"API key required\" blocker. \n- **Strict Geographic Bounds**: Implemented `maxBounds` and `maxBoundsViscosity` with India coordinates, paired with a constrained `minZoom`. This locks the map explicitly to the region and prevents users from panning out into neighboring countries or oceans.\n- **Resiliency**: Developed a custom `tileerror` event handler that presents a \"Map temporarily unavailable\" overlay with a Retry mechanism if the tile provider fails.\n\n### 3. Detailed Heatmap & Marker Systems\nThe geographic visualizers have been rebuilt with realistic density constraints:\n- **Scaled Mock Dataset**: Upgraded the mock data generation engine to populate 250 realistic civic reports clustered accurately around major Indian metropolitan areas (e.g., Chennai, Bengaluru, Mumbai).\n- **Density-Weighted Heatmap**: The heatmap intensity is now driven directly by the `reportsCount` attribute of each civic issue, representing the true density of citizen complaints rather than just single geographic points.\n- **Marker Modality**: Added rapid toggling between the Heatmap overlay and individual Issue Markers. Markers are accurately color-coded by priority (Critical = Red, High = Orange).\n- **Map & Queue Sync**: Integrated a \"Map\" action button directly into the Issue Queue rows, which executes a `flyTo` animation, instantly panning and zooming the map to the selected issue\'s geographic coordinates. Marker popups now include a \"View Issue Details\" link to traverse back to the detailed view.\n- **Contextual Overlays**: Added a clean, unobtrusive Map Legend and explicitly labeled the map canvas with a \"Demo Civic Data\" tag."
