  user_input {
    user_response: "CRITICAL ENGINEERING FIX \342\200\224 REBUILD THE ROLE SWITCHING AND SIGN-OUT SYSTEM\n\nThe existing \342\200\234Sign Out\342\200\235 and \342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235 functionality is still broken despite multiple fixes.\n\nDO NOT PATCH THE EXISTING BUTTON HANDLERS AGAIN.\n\nInstead, perform a deeper architectural fix:\nREPLACE the current authentication/session/navigation implementation with a single, centralized, deterministic authentication and role-state manager.\n\nThe existing UI and all existing application data must remain intact.\n\n==================================================\n1. ROOT CAUSE ASSUMPTION\n==================================================\n\nAssume the current application has one or more of these problems:\n\n- Multiple competing authentication states\n- Authentication state duplicated across components\n- Role stored separately from authentication\n- React/frontend state not synchronized with localStorage\n- Navigation performed before state is cleared\n- Sign-out handler attached to the wrong component\n- Profile menu unmounting before the click handler executes\n- Browser history causing the old dashboard to remain visible\n- Protected routes restoring the old session immediately\n- Citizen and government sessions sharing the same storage key\n- A router guard automatically forcing the user back into the previous dashboard\n\nDo NOT attempt another superficial button fix.\n\nBuild one authoritative authentication/session system and make every screen use it.\n\n==================================================\n2. CREATE ONE CENTRAL AUTHENTICATION MANAGER\n==================================================\n\nCreate a single centralized authentication store/provider.\n\nExample conceptual state:\n\nAuthState:\n{\n  citizenSession: null | {\n    userId,\n    name,\n    verified,\n    language\n  },\n\n  governmentSession: null | {\n    userId,\n    name,\n    role,\n    department\n  },\n\n  activeRole: \"none\" | \"citizen\" | \"government\"\n}\n\nThere must be ONE source of truth.\n\nDo NOT allow individual pages/components to maintain their own copies of:\n\nisLoggedIn\nauthenticated\ncurrentUser\nrole\nuser\nsession\n\nAll pages must read authentication state from the centralized manager.\n\n==================================================\n3. USE UNIQUE STORAGE KEYS\n==================================================\n\nUse completely separate persistent storage keys.\n\nCitizen:\n\ncivicpulse_citizen_session\n\nGovernment:\n\ncivicpulse_government_session\n\nActive role:\n\ncivicpulse_active_role\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nauthenticated\n\nisLoggedIn\n\nuser\n\nsession\n\ncurrentUser\n\nfor both roles.\n\nThe final implementation must not contain a shared global authentication key.\n\n==================================================\n4. DO NOT STORE \342\200\234LOGGED IN\342\200\235 AS A SIMPLE BOOLEAN\n==================================================\n\nDo not rely solely on:\n\nauthenticated = true\n\nInstead use a session object with an explicit role.\n\nExample:\n\n{\n  authenticated: true,\n  role: \"citizen\",\n  userId: \"citizen-demo-001\"\n}\n\nand:\n\n{\n  authenticated: true,\n  role: \"government\",\n  userId: \"gov-demo-001\"\n}\n\nThe role and identity must be explicitly tied to the session.\n\n==================================================\n5. DEFINE EXPLICIT APPLICATION ROUTES\n==================================================\n\nCreate separate route namespaces.\n\nPUBLIC:\n\n/\n /select-role\n\nCITIZEN:\n\n/citizen\n/citizen/home\n/citizen/report\n/citizen/reports\n/citizen/profile\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\n/government\n/government/dashboard\n/government/issues\n/government/map\n/government/analytics\n/government/settings\n\nAUTHENTICATION:\n\n/citizen/login\n/government/login\n\nDo not let citizen routes and government routes share generic dashboard routes.\n\n==================================================\n6. BUILD REAL PROTECTED ROUTE GUARDS\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nCitizenRouteGuard\n\nGovernmentRouteGuard\n\nBehavior:\n\nIf user opens /citizen/*\n\nAND citizen session exists:\n\n\342\206\222 allow access\n\nIf citizen session does NOT exist:\n\n\342\206\222 redirect to /citizen/login\n\nSimilarly:\n\nIf user opens /government/*\n\nAND government session exists:\n\n\342\206\222 allow access\n\nOtherwise:\n\n\342\206\222 redirect to /government/login\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nRoute guards must NEVER resurrect a session after logout.\n\n==================================================\n7. IMPLEMENT LOGOUT AS A FULL STATE TRANSITION\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT merely hide the UI.\n\nCreate a dedicated central function:\n\nlogoutCitizen()\n\nThis function must perform ALL of the following in this exact order:\n\n1. Clear citizen session from memory.\n2. Remove civicpulse_citizen_session from localStorage.\n3. If activeRole === \"citizen\", set activeRole = \"none\".\n4. Remove civicpulse_active_role if its value is \"citizen\".\n5. Force authentication context to re-render.\n6. Navigate to /select-role.\n7. Replace browser history rather than pushing the old dashboard route.\n\nEquivalent function:\n\nlogoutGovernment()\n\nDo the same for the government session.\n\n==================================================\n8. CLEAR STATE BEFORE NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT navigate first and clear state afterward.\n\nWRONG:\n\nnavigate(\"/select-role\")\nsetAuthenticated(false)\n\nCORRECT:\n\nclear session\n\342\206\223\nupdate global auth state\n\342\206\223\nclear active role\n\342\206\223\nnavigate(\"/select-role\", { replace: true })\n\nThis is critical.\n\n==================================================\n9. USE HISTORY REPLACEMENT\n==================================================\n\nAfter sign out:\n\nDO NOT use normal push navigation.\n\nUse history replacement:\n\nreplace(\"/select-role\")\n\nThis prevents the browser Back button from immediately taking the user back into the authenticated dashboard.\n\n==================================================\n10. HANDLE BROWSER BACK BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nAfter logout, pressing browser Back must NOT restore the authenticated dashboard.\n\nIf the user signs out of:\n\n/government/dashboard\n\nthen:\n\nBack\n\nmust NOT return them to the dashboard.\n\nThe same applies to the citizen dashboard.\n\nProtected route guards must redirect them back to the appropriate login/role-selection screen.\n\n==================================================\n11. IMPLEMENT A HARD SESSION INVALIDATION TOKEN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a session version or session ID.\n\nExample:\n\ncitizenSessionId\ngovernmentSessionId\n\nWhen logging out:\n\nInvalidate the current session.\n\nAny stale component still holding the previous session must be ignored.\n\nThis prevents old React component state from restoring a logged-out session.\n\n==================================================\n12. FORCE AUTH CONTEXT SYNCHRONIZATION\n==================================================\n\nAfter every authentication change:\n\n- Update React/global state\n- Update localStorage\n- Notify all relevant components\n- Recalculate current route permissions\n\nThe application must never have:\n\nlocalStorage = logged out\n\nwhile:\n\nReact state = logged in\n\nBoth must always agree.\n\n==================================================\n13. DO NOT LET DASHBOARDS SELF-AUTHENTICATE\n==================================================\n\nAudit the Citizen Dashboard and Government Dashboard.\n\nThey must NEVER contain logic equivalent to:\n\n\342\200\234If no user exists, create demo user automatically.\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT automatically recreate a session when:\n\n- A dashboard mounts\n- A route loads\n- The page refreshes\n- A component initializes\n\nOnly these actions can create a session:\n\nCitizen:\n- Citizen login\n- Citizen demo login\n- Valid citizen account creation\n\nGovernment:\n- Government login\n- Government demo login\n\n==================================================\n14. DEMO LOGIN MUST BE EXPLICIT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Demo Citizen\342\200\235\n\nand:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Municipal Officer\342\200\235\n\nThese functions must explicitly create their respective sessions.\n\nDemo Citizen:\n\nsetCitizenSession(...)\nsetActiveRole(\"citizen\")\nnavigate(\"/citizen/home\", { replace: true })\n\nDemo Government:\n\nsetGovernmentSession(...)\nsetActiveRole(\"government\")\nnavigate(\"/government/dashboard\", { replace: true })\n\n==================================================\n15. FIX SWITCH TO CITIZEN AS A ROLE TRANSITION\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT implement:\n\nnavigate(\"/citizen\")\n\nalone.\n\nInstead:\n\nswitchToCitizen()\n\nmust:\n\n1. Clear government session from memory.\n2. Remove civicpulse_government_session.\n3. Set activeRole = none.\n4. Update auth context.\n5. Navigate to /select-role using replace().\n6. User selects Citizen.\n7. Citizen login/demo authentication creates citizen session.\n8. Navigate to /citizen/home.\n\nThis prevents role leakage.\n\n==================================================\n16. ALSO IMPLEMENT SWITCH TO MUNICIPAL STAFF\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nswitchToGovernment()\n\nwith the same structure.\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Clear citizen session\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government authentication\n\342\206\222 /government/dashboard\n\n==================================================\n17. ROLE SELECTION MUST NEVER REQUIRE A REFRESH\n==================================================\n\nThe following flow MUST work in one browser session:\n\nCitizen login\n\342\206\222 Citizen dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign out\n\342\206\222 Role selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign out\n\342\206\222 Role selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen dashboard\n\nNo page refresh.\n\nNo application restart.\n\nNo clearing localStorage manually.\n\n==================================================\n18. MAKE SIGN OUT BUTTON A DIRECT AUTH ACTION\n==================================================\n\nThe Sign Out button must directly call the centralized:\n\nlogoutCitizen()\n\nor:\n\nlogoutGovernment()\n\nfunction.\n\nDo NOT wrap sign-out logic in page-specific state.\n\nDo NOT create separate sign-out implementations for different pages.\n\nEvery Sign Out button must call the same centralized function.\n\n==================================================\n19. PROFILE MENU\n==================================================\n\nCitizen profile:\n\nSathyendhar B\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nMenu:\n\nProfile\nMy Reports\nLanguage\nPrivacy & Security\nSign Out\n\nGovernment profile:\n\nGovernment user\n\342\234\223 Municipal Officer\n\nMenu:\n\nProfile\nSettings\nSwitch to Citizen\nSign Out\n\nThese buttons must invoke centralized functions.\n\n==================================================\n20. ADD A VISIBLE EXIT CONTROL\n==================================================\n\nTo guarantee the demo can always return to the role selector, add a small secondary control in the profile menu:\n\n\342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235\n\nThis should:\n\n- Clear current role\n- Clear current active session\n- Navigate to /select-role\n\nThis is NOT a replacement for Sign Out.\n\nIt is a reliable demo navigation escape hatch.\n\n==================================================\n21. AUTHENTICATION DEBUG PANEL \342\200\224 DEVELOPMENT ONLY\n==================================================\n\nAdd a hidden or development-only diagnostics panel.\n\nDo not expose it prominently.\n\nIt should show:\n\nActive Role:\ncitizen / government / none\n\nCitizen Session:\nACTIVE / NONE\n\nGovernment Session:\nACTIVE / NONE\n\nCurrent Route:\n/citizen/home\nor\n/government/dashboard\n\nStorage:\n\ncivicpulse_citizen_session\ncivicpulse_government_session\ncivicpulse_active_role\n\nInclude buttons:\n\n\342\200\234Clear Citizen Session\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Clear Government Session\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Clear All Sessions\342\200\235\n\nThis is for diagnosing authentication issues during development.\n\nMake sure this panel can be hidden/disabled for the final presentation.\n\n==================================================\n22. DO NOT DELETE CIVIC DATA ON LOGOUT\n==================================================\n\nLogout must ONLY clear authentication/session state.\n\nNever delete:\n\n- Reports\n- Issues\n- Mock dataset\n- Images\n- Analytics data\n- Language preference\n- Demo data\n- Issue history\n\nThe government dashboard should contain the same data when the government user logs in again.\n\n==================================================\n23. PRESERVE LANGUAGE PREFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nSigning out must NOT reset:\n\nselectedLanguage\n\nThe user\'s selected Tamil/Hindi/English preference should remain stored separately.\n\nExample:\n\ncivic_language = \"ta\"\n\nLogout must not delete it.\n\n==================================================\n24. HARD ROUTE TEST\n==================================================\n\nPerform these exact tests programmatically and manually:\n\nTEST A:\n\nOpen /citizen/home without citizen session.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /citizen/login\n\nTEST B:\n\nOpen /government/dashboard without government session.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /government/login\n\nTEST C:\n\nCitizen login.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /citizen/home\n\nTEST D:\n\nCitizen logout.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\nThen press browser Back.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 MUST NOT return to citizen dashboard.\n\nTEST E:\n\nGovernment login.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /government/dashboard\n\nTEST F:\n\nGovernment logout.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\nThen press browser Back.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 MUST NOT return to government dashboard.\n\nTEST G:\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nTEST H:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nTEST I:\n\nRefresh after citizen login.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nTEST J:\n\nRefresh after government login.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nTEST K:\n\nCitizen logout\n\342\206\222 Government login\n\nExpected:\nGovernment Dashboard works.\n\nTEST L:\n\nGovernment logout\n\342\206\222 Citizen login\n\nExpected:\nCitizen Dashboard works.\n\n==================================================\n25. AUDIT ALL EXISTING CODE\n==================================================\n\nSearch the entire application for references to:\n\nauthenticated\nisLoggedIn\nlogin\nlogout\ncurrentUser\nuser\nrole\nsession\nlocalStorage\nsessionStorage\nnavigate\nwindow.location\n\nIdentify duplicate authentication logic.\n\nConsolidate it into the central authentication manager.\n\nRemove or refactor conflicting implementations.\n\nThere must be ONE authoritative authentication system.\n\n==================================================\n26. DO NOT USE FULL PAGE RELOADS AS THE FIX\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT solve this using:\n\nwindow.location.reload()\n\nor:\n\nwindow.location.href = ...\n\nunless absolutely necessary for a final hard redirect.\n\nThe application must transition cleanly through frontend routing and state updates.\n\n==================================================\n27. FINAL EXPECTED ARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nThe final session architecture should conceptually be:\n\n                  AUTH MANAGER\n                       \342\224\202\n           \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n           \342\224\202                       \342\224\202\n     CITIZEN SESSION        GOVERNMENT SESSION\n           \342\224\202                       \342\224\202\n      Citizen Routes          Government Routes\n           \342\224\202                       \342\224\202\n      Citizen UI              Government UI\n\n                       \342\224\202\n                  Active Role\n                       \342\224\202\n          \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\274\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n          \342\224\202            \342\224\202            \342\224\202\n       Citizen      Government      None\n\nWhen role = None:\n\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\n==================================================\n28. FINAL SUCCESS CRITERIA\n==================================================\n\nThe authentication system is considered FIXED ONLY when ALL of these are true:\n\n\342\234\223 Citizen Sign Out works\n\342\234\223 Government Sign Out works\n\342\234\223 Switch to Citizen works\n\342\234\223 Switch to Municipal Staff works\n\342\234\223 Role Selection is always reachable\n\342\234\223 Browser Back cannot resurrect authenticated pages\n\342\234\223 Refresh preserves the correct active session\n\342\234\223 Citizen and government sessions are completely isolated\n\342\234\223 Authentication state and routing state remain synchronized\n\342\234\223 Mock civic data survives logout\n\342\234\223 Language preference survives logout\n\342\234\223 No manual localStorage clearing is needed\n\342\234\223 No page restart is needed\n\342\234\223 No browser refresh is required to switch roles\n\342\234\223 No dashboard auto-creates a session\n\342\234\223 All protected routes enforce the correct role\n\342\234\223 Both environments can be demonstrated repeatedly in one session\n\nDO NOT merely modify the existing buttons.\n\nREBUILD THE SESSION, AUTHENTICATION, ROLE, AND ROUTING LOGIC AS ONE CENTRALIZED SYSTEM AND CONNECT THE EXISTING UI TO IT.\n\nPreserve the official product name exactly:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    items {
      text: "CRITICAL ENGINEERING FIX \342\200\224 REBUILD THE ROLE SWITCHING AND SIGN-OUT SYSTEM\n\nThe existing \342\200\234Sign Out\342\200\235 and \342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235 functionality is still broken despite multiple fixes.\n\nDO NOT PATCH THE EXISTING BUTTON HANDLERS AGAIN.\n\nInstead, perform a deeper architectural fix:\nREPLACE the current authentication/session/navigation implementation with a single, centralized, deterministic authentication and role-state manager.\n\nThe existing UI and all existing application data must remain intact.\n\n==================================================\n1. ROOT CAUSE ASSUMPTION\n==================================================\n\nAssume the current application has one or more of these problems:\n\n- Multiple competing authentication states\n- Authentication state duplicated across components\n- Role stored separately from authentication\n- React/frontend state not synchronized with localStorage\n- Navigation performed before state is cleared\n- Sign-out handler attached to the wrong component\n- Profile menu unmounting before the click handler executes\n- Browser history causing the old dashboard to remain visible\n- Protected routes restoring the old session immediately\n- Citizen and government sessions sharing the same storage key\n- A router guard automatically forcing the user back into the previous dashboard\n\nDo NOT attempt another superficial button fix.\n\nBuild one authoritative authentication/session system and make every screen use it.\n\n==================================================\n2. CREATE ONE CENTRAL AUTHENTICATION MANAGER\n==================================================\n\nCreate a single centralized authentication store/provider.\n\nExample conceptual state:\n\nAuthState:\n{\n  citizenSession: null | {\n    userId,\n    name,\n    verified,\n    language\n  },\n\n  governmentSession: null | {\n    userId,\n    name,\n    role,\n    department\n  },\n\n  activeRole: \"none\" | \"citizen\" | \"government\"\n}\n\nThere must be ONE source of truth.\n\nDo NOT allow individual pages/components to maintain their own copies of:\n\nisLoggedIn\nauthenticated\ncurrentUser\nrole\nuser\nsession\n\nAll pages must read authentication state from the centralized manager.\n\n==================================================\n3. USE UNIQUE STORAGE KEYS\n==================================================\n\nUse completely separate persistent storage keys.\n\nCitizen:\n\ncivicpulse_citizen_session\n\nGovernment:\n\ncivicpulse_government_session\n\nActive role:\n\ncivicpulse_active_role\n\nDo NOT use:\n\nauthenticated\n\nisLoggedIn\n\nuser\n\nsession\n\ncurrentUser\n\nfor both roles.\n\nThe final implementation must not contain a shared global authentication key.\n\n==================================================\n4. DO NOT STORE \342\200\234LOGGED IN\342\200\235 AS A SIMPLE BOOLEAN\n==================================================\n\nDo not rely solely on:\n\nauthenticated = true\n\nInstead use a session object with an explicit role.\n\nExample:\n\n{\n  authenticated: true,\n  role: \"citizen\",\n  userId: \"citizen-demo-001\"\n}\n\nand:\n\n{\n  authenticated: true,\n  role: \"government\",\n  userId: \"gov-demo-001\"\n}\n\nThe role and identity must be explicitly tied to the session.\n\n==================================================\n5. DEFINE EXPLICIT APPLICATION ROUTES\n==================================================\n\nCreate separate route namespaces.\n\nPUBLIC:\n\n/\n /select-role\n\nCITIZEN:\n\n/citizen\n/citizen/home\n/citizen/report\n/citizen/reports\n/citizen/profile\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\n/government\n/government/dashboard\n/government/issues\n/government/map\n/government/analytics\n/government/settings\n\nAUTHENTICATION:\n\n/citizen/login\n/government/login\n\nDo not let citizen routes and government routes share generic dashboard routes.\n\n==================================================\n6. BUILD REAL PROTECTED ROUTE GUARDS\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nCitizenRouteGuard\n\nGovernmentRouteGuard\n\nBehavior:\n\nIf user opens /citizen/*\n\nAND citizen session exists:\n\n\342\206\222 allow access\n\nIf citizen session does NOT exist:\n\n\342\206\222 redirect to /citizen/login\n\nSimilarly:\n\nIf user opens /government/*\n\nAND government session exists:\n\n\342\206\222 allow access\n\nOtherwise:\n\n\342\206\222 redirect to /government/login\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nRoute guards must NEVER resurrect a session after logout.\n\n==================================================\n7. IMPLEMENT LOGOUT AS A FULL STATE TRANSITION\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT merely hide the UI.\n\nCreate a dedicated central function:\n\nlogoutCitizen()\n\nThis function must perform ALL of the following in this exact order:\n\n1. Clear citizen session from memory.\n2. Remove civicpulse_citizen_session from localStorage.\n3. If activeRole === \"citizen\", set activeRole = \"none\".\n4. Remove civicpulse_active_role if its value is \"citizen\".\n5. Force authentication context to re-render.\n6. Navigate to /select-role.\n7. Replace browser history rather than pushing the old dashboard route.\n\nEquivalent function:\n\nlogoutGovernment()\n\nDo the same for the government session.\n\n==================================================\n8. CLEAR STATE BEFORE NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT navigate first and clear state afterward.\n\nWRONG:\n\nnavigate(\"/select-role\")\nsetAuthenticated(false)\n\nCORRECT:\n\nclear session\n\342\206\223\nupdate global auth state\n\342\206\223\nclear active role\n\342\206\223\nnavigate(\"/select-role\", { replace: true })\n\nThis is critical.\n\n==================================================\n9. USE HISTORY REPLACEMENT\n==================================================\n\nAfter sign out:\n\nDO NOT use normal push navigation.\n\nUse history replacement:\n\nreplace(\"/select-role\")\n\nThis prevents the browser Back button from immediately taking the user back into the authenticated dashboard.\n\n==================================================\n10. HANDLE BROWSER BACK BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nAfter logout, pressing browser Back must NOT restore the authenticated dashboard.\n\nIf the user signs out of:\n\n/government/dashboard\n\nthen:\n\nBack\n\nmust NOT return them to the dashboard.\n\nThe same applies to the citizen dashboard.\n\nProtected route guards must redirect them back to the appropriate login/role-selection screen.\n\n==================================================\n11. IMPLEMENT A HARD SESSION INVALIDATION TOKEN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a session version or session ID.\n\nExample:\n\ncitizenSessionId\ngovernmentSessionId\n\nWhen logging out:\n\nInvalidate the current session.\n\nAny stale component still holding the previous session must be ignored.\n\nThis prevents old React component state from restoring a logged-out session.\n\n==================================================\n12. FORCE AUTH CONTEXT SYNCHRONIZATION\n==================================================\n\nAfter every authentication change:\n\n- Update React/global state\n- Update localStorage\n- Notify all relevant components\n- Recalculate current route permissions\n\nThe application must never have:\n\nlocalStorage = logged out\n\nwhile:\n\nReact state = logged in\n\nBoth must always agree.\n\n==================================================\n13. DO NOT LET DASHBOARDS SELF-AUTHENTICATE\n==================================================\n\nAudit the Citizen Dashboard and Government Dashboard.\n\nThey must NEVER contain logic equivalent to:\n\n\342\200\234If no user exists, create demo user automatically.\342\200\235\n\nDo NOT automatically recreate a session when:\n\n- A dashboard mounts\n- A route loads\n- The page refreshes\n- A component initializes\n\nOnly these actions can create a session:\n\nCitizen:\n- Citizen login\n- Citizen demo login\n- Valid citizen account creation\n\nGovernment:\n- Government login\n- Government demo login\n\n==================================================\n14. DEMO LOGIN MUST BE EXPLICIT\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Demo Citizen\342\200\235\n\nand:\n\n\342\200\234Continue as Municipal Officer\342\200\235\n\nThese functions must explicitly create their respective sessions.\n\nDemo Citizen:\n\nsetCitizenSession(...)\nsetActiveRole(\"citizen\")\nnavigate(\"/citizen/home\", { replace: true })\n\nDemo Government:\n\nsetGovernmentSession(...)\nsetActiveRole(\"government\")\nnavigate(\"/government/dashboard\", { replace: true })\n\n==================================================\n15. FIX SWITCH TO CITIZEN AS A ROLE TRANSITION\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT implement:\n\nnavigate(\"/citizen\")\n\nalone.\n\nInstead:\n\nswitchToCitizen()\n\nmust:\n\n1. Clear government session from memory.\n2. Remove civicpulse_government_session.\n3. Set activeRole = none.\n4. Update auth context.\n5. Navigate to /select-role using replace().\n6. User selects Citizen.\n7. Citizen login/demo authentication creates citizen session.\n8. Navigate to /citizen/home.\n\nThis prevents role leakage.\n\n==================================================\n16. ALSO IMPLEMENT SWITCH TO MUNICIPAL STAFF\n==================================================\n\nCreate:\n\nswitchToGovernment()\n\nwith the same structure.\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Clear citizen session\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government authentication\n\342\206\222 /government/dashboard\n\n==================================================\n17. ROLE SELECTION MUST NEVER REQUIRE A REFRESH\n==================================================\n\nThe following flow MUST work in one browser session:\n\nCitizen login\n\342\206\222 Citizen dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign out\n\342\206\222 Role selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign out\n\342\206\222 Role selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen dashboard\n\nNo page refresh.\n\nNo application restart.\n\nNo clearing localStorage manually.\n\n==================================================\n18. MAKE SIGN OUT BUTTON A DIRECT AUTH ACTION\n==================================================\n\nThe Sign Out button must directly call the centralized:\n\nlogoutCitizen()\n\nor:\n\nlogoutGovernment()\n\nfunction.\n\nDo NOT wrap sign-out logic in page-specific state.\n\nDo NOT create separate sign-out implementations for different pages.\n\nEvery Sign Out button must call the same centralized function.\n\n==================================================\n19. PROFILE MENU\n==================================================\n\nCitizen profile:\n\nSathyendhar B\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nMenu:\n\nProfile\nMy Reports\nLanguage\nPrivacy & Security\nSign Out\n\nGovernment profile:\n\nGovernment user\n\342\234\223 Municipal Officer\n\nMenu:\n\nProfile\nSettings\nSwitch to Citizen\nSign Out\n\nThese buttons must invoke centralized functions.\n\n==================================================\n20. ADD A VISIBLE EXIT CONTROL\n==================================================\n\nTo guarantee the demo can always return to the role selector, add a small secondary control in the profile menu:\n\n\342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235\n\nThis should:\n\n- Clear current role\n- Clear current active session\n- Navigate to /select-role\n\nThis is NOT a replacement for Sign Out.\n\nIt is a reliable demo navigation escape hatch.\n\n==================================================\n21. AUTHENTICATION DEBUG PANEL \342\200\224 DEVELOPMENT ONLY\n==================================================\n\nAdd a hidden or development-only diagnostics panel.\n\nDo not expose it prominently.\n\nIt should show:\n\nActive Role:\ncitizen / government / none\n\nCitizen Session:\nACTIVE / NONE\n\nGovernment Session:\nACTIVE / NONE\n\nCurrent Route:\n/citizen/home\nor\n/government/dashboard\n\nStorage:\n\ncivicpulse_citizen_session\ncivicpulse_government_session\ncivicpulse_active_role\n\nInclude buttons:\n\n\342\200\234Clear Citizen Session\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Clear Government Session\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Clear All Sessions\342\200\235\n\nThis is for diagnosing authentication issues during development.\n\nMake sure this panel can be hidden/disabled for the final presentation.\n\n==================================================\n22. DO NOT DELETE CIVIC DATA ON LOGOUT\n==================================================\n\nLogout must ONLY clear authentication/session state.\n\nNever delete:\n\n- Reports\n- Issues\n- Mock dataset\n- Images\n- Analytics data\n- Language preference\n- Demo data\n- Issue history\n\nThe government dashboard should contain the same data when the government user logs in again.\n\n==================================================\n23. PRESERVE LANGUAGE PREFERENCE\n==================================================\n\nSigning out must NOT reset:\n\nselectedLanguage\n\nThe user\'s selected Tamil/Hindi/English preference should remain stored separately.\n\nExample:\n\ncivic_language = \"ta\"\n\nLogout must not delete it.\n\n==================================================\n24. HARD ROUTE TEST\n==================================================\n\nPerform these exact tests programmatically and manually:\n\nTEST A:\n\nOpen /citizen/home without citizen session.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /citizen/login\n\nTEST B:\n\nOpen /government/dashboard without government session.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /government/login\n\nTEST C:\n\nCitizen login.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /citizen/home\n\nTEST D:\n\nCitizen logout.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\nThen press browser Back.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 MUST NOT return to citizen dashboard.\n\nTEST E:\n\nGovernment login.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /government/dashboard\n\nTEST F:\n\nGovernment logout.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\nThen press browser Back.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 MUST NOT return to government dashboard.\n\nTEST G:\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nTEST H:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 /select-role\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nTEST I:\n\nRefresh after citizen login.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nTEST J:\n\nRefresh after government login.\n\nExpected:\n\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nTEST K:\n\nCitizen logout\n\342\206\222 Government login\n\nExpected:\nGovernment Dashboard works.\n\nTEST L:\n\nGovernment logout\n\342\206\222 Citizen login\n\nExpected:\nCitizen Dashboard works.\n\n==================================================\n25. AUDIT ALL EXISTING CODE\n==================================================\n\nSearch the entire application for references to:\n\nauthenticated\nisLoggedIn\nlogin\nlogout\ncurrentUser\nuser\nrole\nsession\nlocalStorage\nsessionStorage\nnavigate\nwindow.location\n\nIdentify duplicate authentication logic.\n\nConsolidate it into the central authentication manager.\n\nRemove or refactor conflicting implementations.\n\nThere must be ONE authoritative authentication system.\n\n==================================================\n26. DO NOT USE FULL PAGE RELOADS AS THE FIX\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT solve this using:\n\nwindow.location.reload()\n\nor:\n\nwindow.location.href = ...\n\nunless absolutely necessary for a final hard redirect.\n\nThe application must transition cleanly through frontend routing and state updates.\n\n==================================================\n27. FINAL EXPECTED ARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nThe final session architecture should conceptually be:\n\n                  AUTH MANAGER\n                       \342\224\202\n           \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n           \342\224\202                       \342\224\202\n     CITIZEN SESSION        GOVERNMENT SESSION\n           \342\224\202                       \342\224\202\n      Citizen Routes          Government Routes\n           \342\224\202                       \342\224\202\n      Citizen UI              Government UI\n\n                       \342\224\202\n                  Active Role\n                       \342\224\202\n          \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\274\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n          \342\224\202            \342\224\202            \342\224\202\n       Citizen      Government      None\n\nWhen role = None:\n\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\n==================================================\n28. FINAL SUCCESS CRITERIA\n==================================================\n\nThe authentication system is considered FIXED ONLY when ALL of these are true:\n\n\342\234\223 Citizen Sign Out works\n\342\234\223 Government Sign Out works\n\342\234\223 Switch to Citizen works\n\342\234\223 Switch to Municipal Staff works\n\342\234\223 Role Selection is always reachable\n\342\234\223 Browser Back cannot resurrect authenticated pages\n\342\234\223 Refresh preserves the correct active session\n\342\234\223 Citizen and government sessions are completely isolated\n\342\234\223 Authentication state and routing state remain synchronized\n\342\234\223 Mock civic data survives logout\n\342\234\223 Language preference survives logout\n\342\234\223 No manual localStorage clearing is needed\n\342\234\223 No page restart is needed\n\342\234\223 No browser refresh is required to switch roles\n\342\234\223 No dashboard auto-creates a session\n\342\234\223 All protected routes enforce the correct role\n\342\234\223 Both environments can be demonstrated repeatedly in one session\n\nDO NOT merely modify the existing buttons.\n\nREBUILD THE SESSION, AUTHENTICATION, ROLE, AND ROUTING LOGIC AS ONE CENTRALIZED SYSTEM AND CONNECT THE EXISTING UI TO IT.\n\nPreserve the official product name exactly:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    }
  }
}
