    thinking: "**Addressing the Bug**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a crucial bug in the logout process, specifically within `AppContext.tsx`. While `logoutCitizen` and `logoutGov` correctly retain user objects, they only nullify the `auth.citizenSession`. This creates a problem: navigating to `/select-role` post-logout bypasses the intended logout state, I am currently exploring solutions, so the logout stays effective.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Behavior**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the behavior of the system regarding logout and login, and the key is that upon refresh, `AppContext` initializes from `localStorage`. I\'m starting to understand how a citizen session might be preserved after a refresh, given how we\'re storing and retrieving the sessions. The core logic of the system relies on `localStorage` in the `AppContext` initialization function.\n\n\n**Clarifying Persistence Strategy**\n\nNow I think I\'ve cracked it. Removing `civicpulse_citizen_session` from `localStorage` effectively \"logs out\" the citizen, as it is removed from the storage completely. The system fulfills the prompt requirements because: Logging in as a demo citizen requires `loginCitizen(mockUser)` which means the account is recreated and a new session is stored. I am confident I\'m on the right track; the tests E, K, and L should all pass, based on the current implementation.\n\n\n"
