  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully restored the environment and completed the architectural rebuild of the authentication and routing systems. \n\nThe application now features strict session isolation between the **Citizen Portal** and the **Municipal Staff Dashboard**. \n\nHere is a summary of the completed structural improvements:\n- **Centralized Auth Engine**: Rebuilt the application context to distinctly manage `citizenSession` and `governmentSession` with independent storage boundaries. Logging out of one role cleanly wipes only its respective session footprint.\n- **Dedicated Route Namespaces**: Migrated the single-page toggle state to strict standard routing:\n  - `/select-role`: Public landing and onboarding gateway.\n  - `/citizen/*`: Exclusive, protected namespace for the Citizen app.\n  - `/government/*`: Exclusive, protected namespace for the Government app.\n- **Hard Route Guards**: Added explicit route wrapper protection. Attempting to load a secure view without the correct corresponding session will forcefully redirect the user back to the role selection gateway.\n- **Demarcated Navigation Escapes**: Added dedicated \"Exit to Role Selection\" controls inside the sidebars of both portals, allowing safe manual abatement of a demo session to instantly switch roles without cross-leaking identity. \n- **Preservation of Mock Data**: The rebuild cleanly isolates session termination from the core mock database, ensuring civic issue tracking, timeline updates, and generated reports persist across different role logins for testing.\n\nThe application has been successfully compiled and is actively running. You can interact with the live preview to test the isolated navigation pathways."
    modified_response: "I have successfully restored the environment and completed the architectural rebuild of the authentication and routing systems. \n\nThe application now features strict session isolation between the **Citizen Portal** and the **Municipal Staff Dashboard**. \n\nHere is a summary of the completed structural improvements:\n- **Centralized Auth Engine**: Rebuilt the application context to distinctly manage `citizenSession` and `governmentSession` with independent storage boundaries. Logging out of one role cleanly wipes only its respective session footprint.\n- **Dedicated Route Namespaces**: Migrated the single-page toggle state to strict standard routing:\n  - `/select-role`: Public landing and onboarding gateway.\n  - `/citizen/*`: Exclusive, protected namespace for the Citizen app.\n  - `/government/*`: Exclusive, protected namespace for the Government app.\n- **Hard Route Guards**: Added explicit route wrapper protection. Attempting to load a secure view without the correct corresponding session will forcefully redirect the user back to the role selection gateway.\n- **Demarcated Navigation Escapes**: Added dedicated \"Exit to Role Selection\" controls inside the sidebars of both portals, allowing safe manual abatement of a demo session to instantly switch roles without cross-leaking identity. \n- **Preservation of Mock Data**: The rebuild cleanly isolates session termination from the core mock database, ensuring civic issue tracking, timeline updates, and generated reports persist across different role logins for testing.\n\nThe application has been successfully compiled and is actively running. You can interact with the live preview to test the isolated navigation pathways."
