steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1787861157
      nanos: 478617032
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "CRITICAL UI + NAVIGATION FIX\n\nFix the existing \342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nDO NOT redesign the product.\nDO NOT remove existing functionality.\nDO NOT create another workaround on top of the current broken implementation.\n\nThere are TWO major unresolved issues:\n\n1. GOVERNMENT DATA TABLES ARE BEING CUT OFF / HORIZONTALLY CLIPPED.\n2. CITIZEN ACCESS IS STILL BLOCKED BECAUSE SIGN OUT / SWITCH TO CITIZEN / ROLE NAVIGATION DO NOT WORK.\n\nTreat this as an architectural correction, not a cosmetic patch.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 FIX ALL TABLES GLOBALLY\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Government Issue Queue table is wider than its container and is being visually cut off.\n\nThe screenshot shows:\n- The right side of the table is outside the visible area.\n- Action buttons are partially inaccessible.\n- The table is forcing the page into an awkward horizontal overflow.\n- Only part of the content is visible.\n\nThis must be fixed for EVERY table in the application.\n\nDo not fix only the visible Issue Queue.\n\nAudit ALL tables, including:\n\n- Issue Queue\n- Citizen Reports\n- Department tables\n- Field Operations\n- SLA & Escalations\n- Analytics tables\n- User / Administration tables\n- Any other table introduced anywhere in the government dashboard\n\n==================================================\n1. USE A RESPONSIVE TABLE CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nEvery data table must exist inside a dedicated responsive container.\n\nConceptually:\n\nTableContainer\n\342\206\222 width: 100%\n\342\206\222 overflow-x: auto\n\342\206\222 overflow-y: visible\n\nThe table itself may be wider than the viewport if necessary, BUT:\n\n- It must never be clipped by the parent.\n- The user must be able to access EVERY column.\n- Horizontal scrolling must occur INSIDE the table container, not across the entire application page.\n- The sidebar/header/footer must NOT move sideways because of a table.\n- The table must never cause the entire dashboard layout to overflow horizontally.\n\nThe horizontal scrollbar shown at the very bottom of the screenshot is NOT acceptable.\n\nThe page itself should remain within the viewport.\n\n==================================================\n2. NEVER CLIP TABLE CONTENT\n==================================================\n\nRemove any CSS that causes:\n\noverflow: hidden\n\nor similar clipping on table parents when it causes columns to disappear.\n\nAudit:\n\n- overflow\n- width\n- min-width\n- max-width\n- flex\n- grid\n- position\n- white-space\n\nfor all table containers.\n\nDo not use arbitrary fixed widths that exceed the dashboard content area.\n\n==================================================\n3. KEEP IMPORTANT COLUMNS VISIBLE\n==================================================\n\nFor wide tables, prioritize usability.\n\nThe following columns should remain easy to access:\n\nPriority\nIssue ID\nDetails\nLocation\nAssignment\nStatus\nAction\n\nOther columns can remain horizontally scrollable.\n\nThe Action column must NEVER be partially hidden.\n\nDo not allow buttons to extend outside their cell.\n\n==================================================\n4. STICKY ACTION COLUMN\n==================================================\n\nFor wide Government tables, make the ACTION column sticky on the right side when appropriate.\n\nExample:\n\n| Priority | Issue | Location | ... | Status | ACTION |\n\nThe Action column remains visible while horizontally scrolling.\n\nUse:\n\nposition: sticky\nright: 0\n\nwith appropriate background and border/shadow so it remains visually distinct.\n\nDo NOT make the entire table sticky.\n\nOnly use sticky columns when it improves usability.\n\n==================================================\n5. RESPONSIVE COLUMN BEHAVIOUR\n==================================================\n\nFor medium-width screens:\n\nReduce unnecessary whitespace.\n\nFor smaller desktop windows:\n\nAllow horizontal scrolling INSIDE the table container.\n\nFor very small screens:\n\nUse a stacked/card representation where appropriate instead of creating a giant inaccessible table.\n\nGovernment dashboard is desktop-first, but it must still behave correctly when the browser width changes.\n\n==================================================\n6. DO NOT SHRINK TEXT TO SOLVE THE PROBLEM\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT solve table overflow by making text microscopic.\n\nMaintain readable:\n\n- Font size\n- Line height\n- Row height\n- Button size\n\nUse wrapping / truncation where appropriate.\n\nExample:\n\nLocation:\n\342\200\234Koramangala 5th Block, Bengaluru...\342\200\235\n\nwith tooltip/full value on hover.\n\n==================================================\n7. ACTION BUTTONS\n==================================================\n\nMake action buttons compact but fully visible.\n\nExample:\n\n[Map]\n[Assign]\n[View]\n\nIf there are too many actions, use:\n\n[Actions \342\226\276]\n\ninstead of letting the buttons overflow outside the cell.\n\n==================================================\n8. AUDIT THE ENTIRE GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD\n==================================================\n\nSearch the entire application for:\n\n<table>\noverflow-x\noverflow\nmin-width\nwidth:\nwhitespace\nflex\ngrid\nsticky\n\nIdentify every location where a table can overflow its parent.\n\nApply one reusable:\n\nResponsiveTableContainer\n\ncomponent/pattern to all tables.\n\nDo not implement separate inconsistent fixes.\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 REBUILD AUTHENTICATION / ROLE NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Sign Out and Switch to Citizen controls still do not reliably work.\n\nAs a result, I cannot access the Citizen version after entering the Government version.\n\nSTOP PATCHING THE EXISTING BUTTON HANDLERS.\n\nReplace the current role/navigation implementation with a SIMPLE, DETERMINISTIC DEMO ROLE SYSTEM.\n\nSince this is a frontend-only prototype, prioritize reliability and demonstrability.\n\n==================================================\n9. CREATE A SINGLE ROLE SELECTION ENTRY SCREEN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a dedicated route:\n\n/select-role\n\nThis page must ALWAYS be accessible.\n\nDisplay:\n\nCrowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\n\n\342\200\234Choose your experience\342\200\235\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nThe buttons must directly navigate to their respective demo environments.\n\n==================================================\n10. CITIZEN DEMO ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nClick:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n\342\206\222 /citizen/login\n\nOn this screen provide:\n\n[ Continue as Demo Citizen ]\n\nThis MUST immediately create the citizen session and open:\n\n/citizen/home\n\nDo not require real OTP.\n\nDo not require external authentication.\n\nDo not require any backend.\n\n==================================================\n11. GOVERNMENT DEMO ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nClick:\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\n\342\206\222 /government/login\n\nProvide:\n\n[ Continue as Municipal Officer ]\n\nThis MUST immediately create the government session and open:\n\n/government/dashboard\n\nDo not require external authentication.\n\n==================================================\n12. CREATE A SINGLE CENTRAL SESSION STORE\n==================================================\n\nRemove competing authentication logic.\n\nCreate ONE auth/session provider or store.\n\nState:\n\n{\n  activeRole: \"none\" | \"citizen\" | \"government\",\n\n  citizenSession: null | {\n    id,\n    name,\n    verified\n  },\n\n  governmentSession: null | {\n    id,\n    name,\n    role,\n    department\n  }\n}\n\nEvery page must read authentication state from this single source.\n\n==================================================\n13. REMOVE CONFLICTING AUTH VARIABLES\n==================================================\n\nAudit the entire application for:\n\nauthenticated\nisLoggedIn\nuser\ncurrentUser\nsession\nrole\ncurrentRole\n\nIf different components maintain their own authentication state, refactor them.\n\nThere must NOT be:\n\nPage A:\nisLoggedIn = true\n\nPage B:\nauthenticated = false\n\nPage C:\ncurrentRole = government\n\nwhile localStorage says citizen.\n\nUse the central auth store.\n\n==================================================\n14. SEPARATE STORAGE KEYS\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\ncivic_citizen_session\n\ncivic_government_session\n\ncivic_active_role\n\nNever use one shared key such as:\n\nauthenticated\n\nfor both roles.\n\n==================================================\n15. HARD SIGN-OUT FUNCTION\n==================================================\n\nCreate exactly two centralized functions:\n\nlogoutCitizen()\n\nlogoutGovernment()\n\nCITIZEN:\n\nlogoutCitizen()\n\nmust:\n\n1. Delete civic_citizen_session\n2. Set citizenSession = null\n3. If activeRole == citizen:\n   set activeRole = none\n4. Delete civic_active_role\n5. Update global application state immediately\n6. Navigate to /select-role using route replacement\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\nlogoutGovernment()\n\nmust:\n\n1. Delete civic_government_session\n2. Set governmentSession = null\n3. If activeRole == government:\n   set activeRole = none\n4. Delete civic_active_role\n5. Update global application state immediately\n6. Navigate to /select-role using route replacement\n\nDO NOT navigate before clearing the session.\n\n==================================================\n16. SWITCH TO CITIZEN\n==================================================\n\nThe Government Dashboard currently has:\n\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nMake it call the central:\n\nswitchToCitizen()\n\nfunction.\n\nImplementation logic:\n\nswitchToCitizen():\n\n1. Clear government session\n2. Set governmentSession = null\n3. Set activeRole = none\n4. Clear active role storage\n5. Navigate to /select-role using replace()\n6. User selects Citizen\n7. Continue as Demo Citizen\n8. Open /citizen/home\n\nDO NOT directly navigate from Government Dashboard to:\n\n/citizen/home\n\nwithout establishing the citizen session.\n\n==================================================\n17. SWITCH TO MUNICIPAL STAFF\n==================================================\n\nImplement the reverse:\n\nswitchToGovernment()\n\nlogic:\n\n1. Clear citizen session\n2. Set citizenSession = null\n3. Set activeRole = none\n4. Clear active role storage\n5. Navigate to /select-role\n6. User selects Municipal Staff\n7. Continue as Demo Officer\n8. Open /government/dashboard\n\n==================================================\n18. REMOVE BROWSER-HISTORY PROBLEM\n==================================================\n\nAfter sign out or role switch:\n\nUse route replacement, not normal push navigation.\n\nFor example:\n\nreplace(\"/select-role\")\n\nThe user should NOT be able to press Back and instantly return to the authenticated dashboard.\n\nProtected routes must also reject the old session.\n\n==================================================\n19. PROTECTED ROUTES\n==================================================\n\nCITIZEN:\n\n/citizen/home\n/citizen/report\n/citizen/reports\n/citizen/profile\n\nRequire:\n\ncitizenSession != null\n\nOtherwise:\n\n\342\206\222 /citizen/login\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\n/government/dashboard\n/government/issues\n/government/map\n/government/analytics\n/government/settings\n\nRequire:\n\ngovernmentSession != null\n\nOtherwise:\n\n\342\206\222 /government/login\n\n==================================================\n20. CRITICAL: DO NOT AUTO-LOGIN\n==================================================\n\nThis is likely causing the current problem.\n\nRemove any code that automatically recreates a demo session when:\n\n- Citizen dashboard loads\n- Government dashboard loads\n- Route changes\n- Component mounts\n- Page refreshes\n- User visits a dashboard path\n\nA session may ONLY be created by:\n\nCitizen:\nContinue as Demo Citizen\n\nGovernment:\nContinue as Municipal Officer\n\nor the explicitly simulated authentication flow.\n\n==================================================\n21. MAKE PROFILE BUTTONS RELIABLE\n==================================================\n\nThe profile menu must not disappear before the action is processed.\n\nCitizen:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\342\206\222 logoutCitizen()\n\nGovernment:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\342\206\222 logoutGovernment()\n\nSwitch:\n\nGovernment Profile\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 switchToCitizen()\n\nDo not duplicate these handlers in multiple components.\n\n==================================================\n22. ADD A GUARANTEED ROLE-SWITCH BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nFor demonstration purposes, add a small secondary action:\n\n\342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235\n\nThis must call:\n\nexitToRoleSelection()\n\nFunction:\n\n- Clear current role\n- Clear current session\n- Update global auth state\n- replace(\"/select-role\")\n\nThis is a reliable escape route for the demo.\n\n==================================================\n23. AUTHENTICATION DEBUG MODE\n==================================================\n\nAdd a development-only diagnostic panel.\n\nDisplay:\n\nActive Role:\nCitizen / Government / None\n\nCitizen Session:\nACTIVE / NONE\n\nGovernment Session:\nACTIVE / NONE\n\nCurrent Route:\n...\n\nButtons:\n\nClear Citizen Session\nClear Government Session\nClear All Sessions\nGo to Role Selection\n\nKeep this hidden behind:\n\nDevelopment / Debug\n\nDo not show it in the final normal user interface.\n\nThis is essential for diagnosing state problems while developing.\n\n==================================================\nPART 3 \342\200\224 MAKE CITIZEN ACCESS EASY TO DEMONSTRATE\n==================================================\n\nThe final navigation must be:\n\nOPEN APPLICATION\n\342\206\223\nROLE SELECTION\n\342\206\223\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202                      \342\224\202\nCitizen          Municipal Staff\n\342\224\202                      \342\224\202\n\342\206\223                      \342\206\223\nCitizen Login     Government Login\n\342\224\202                      \342\224\202\n\342\206\223                      \342\206\223\nDemo Citizen      Demo Officer\n\342\224\202                      \342\224\202\n\342\206\223                      \342\206\223\nCitizen Home       Government Dashboard\n\n==================================================\n24. EXACT DEMO SWITCHING FLOW\n==================================================\n\nThis exact sequence MUST work:\n\n1. Open application.\n2. Select Municipal Staff.\n3. Enter Government Dashboard.\n4. Open profile.\n5. Click Switch to Citizen.\n6. Confirm.\n7. Role Selection appears.\n8. Select Citizen.\n9. Click Continue as Demo Citizen.\n10. Citizen Home appears.\n\nThen:\n\n11. Open Citizen profile.\n12. Click Sign Out.\n13. Role Selection appears.\n14. Select Municipal Staff.\n15. Click Continue as Municipal Officer.\n16. Government Dashboard appears.\n\nRepeat this sequence multiple times.\n\n==================================================\n25. DATA MUST SURVIVE ROLE CHANGES\n==================================================\n\nSwitching roles must NOT remove:\n\n- Civic reports\n- Civic issues\n- Government dashboard data\n- Analytics\n- Images\n- Issue history\n- Mock citizen records\n- Language preference\n\nOnly authentication/session state changes.\n\n==================================================\nPART 4 \342\200\224 FINAL APPLICATION AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nBefore finishing, audit the application for:\n\nA. TABLES\n\nEvery table must:\n\n\342\234\223 Fit inside its page layout\n\342\234\223 Never clip columns\n\342\234\223 Keep Action accessible\n\342\234\223 Use internal horizontal scroll when needed\n\342\234\223 Never cause whole-page horizontal scrolling\n\342\234\223 Maintain readable text\n\342\234\223 Work at different desktop widths\n\nB. AUTHENTICATION\n\n\342\234\223 Citizen login works\n\342\234\223 Government login works\n\342\234\223 Citizen sign out works\n\342\234\223 Government sign out works\n\342\234\223 Switch to Citizen works\n\342\234\223 Switch to Municipal Staff works\n\342\234\223 Role Selection works\n\342\234\223 Browser Back cannot restore logged-out dashboard\n\342\234\223 Refresh preserves active session\n\342\234\223 Sessions are separated\n\342\234\223 Data survives logout\n\342\234\223 No automatic session recreation\n\342\234\223 No manual localStorage clearing required\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThere must be TWO fully usable environments:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 Simple citizen interface\n\342\206\222 Camera-first reporting\n\342\206\222 Reports\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\nGOVERNMENT\n\342\206\222 Detailed municipal dashboard\n\342\206\222 All data\n\342\206\222 Tables\n\342\206\222 Map\n\342\206\222 Analytics\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\nAnd the user must be able to move between them repeatedly:\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Government\n\nwith NO:\n\n- browser restart\n- page refresh\n- manual storage clearing\n- broken route\n- stuck session\n- dead button\n\nFinally, preserve the exact official product name:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    items {
      text: "CRITICAL UI + NAVIGATION FIX\n\nFix the existing \342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235 prototype.\n\nDO NOT redesign the product.\nDO NOT remove existing functionality.\nDO NOT create another workaround on top of the current broken implementation.\n\nThere are TWO major unresolved issues:\n\n1. GOVERNMENT DATA TABLES ARE BEING CUT OFF / HORIZONTALLY CLIPPED.\n2. CITIZEN ACCESS IS STILL BLOCKED BECAUSE SIGN OUT / SWITCH TO CITIZEN / ROLE NAVIGATION DO NOT WORK.\n\nTreat this as an architectural correction, not a cosmetic patch.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 FIX ALL TABLES GLOBALLY\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Government Issue Queue table is wider than its container and is being visually cut off.\n\nThe screenshot shows:\n- The right side of the table is outside the visible area.\n- Action buttons are partially inaccessible.\n- The table is forcing the page into an awkward horizontal overflow.\n- Only part of the content is visible.\n\nThis must be fixed for EVERY table in the application.\n\nDo not fix only the visible Issue Queue.\n\nAudit ALL tables, including:\n\n- Issue Queue\n- Citizen Reports\n- Department tables\n- Field Operations\n- SLA & Escalations\n- Analytics tables\n- User / Administration tables\n- Any other table introduced anywhere in the government dashboard\n\n==================================================\n1. USE A RESPONSIVE TABLE CONTAINER\n==================================================\n\nEvery data table must exist inside a dedicated responsive container.\n\nConceptually:\n\nTableContainer\n\342\206\222 width: 100%\n\342\206\222 overflow-x: auto\n\342\206\222 overflow-y: visible\n\nThe table itself may be wider than the viewport if necessary, BUT:\n\n- It must never be clipped by the parent.\n- The user must be able to access EVERY column.\n- Horizontal scrolling must occur INSIDE the table container, not across the entire application page.\n- The sidebar/header/footer must NOT move sideways because of a table.\n- The table must never cause the entire dashboard layout to overflow horizontally.\n\nThe horizontal scrollbar shown at the very bottom of the screenshot is NOT acceptable.\n\nThe page itself should remain within the viewport.\n\n==================================================\n2. NEVER CLIP TABLE CONTENT\n==================================================\n\nRemove any CSS that causes:\n\noverflow: hidden\n\nor similar clipping on table parents when it causes columns to disappear.\n\nAudit:\n\n- overflow\n- width\n- min-width\n- max-width\n- flex\n- grid\n- position\n- white-space\n\nfor all table containers.\n\nDo not use arbitrary fixed widths that exceed the dashboard content area.\n\n==================================================\n3. KEEP IMPORTANT COLUMNS VISIBLE\n==================================================\n\nFor wide tables, prioritize usability.\n\nThe following columns should remain easy to access:\n\nPriority\nIssue ID\nDetails\nLocation\nAssignment\nStatus\nAction\n\nOther columns can remain horizontally scrollable.\n\nThe Action column must NEVER be partially hidden.\n\nDo not allow buttons to extend outside their cell.\n\n==================================================\n4. STICKY ACTION COLUMN\n==================================================\n\nFor wide Government tables, make the ACTION column sticky on the right side when appropriate.\n\nExample:\n\n| Priority | Issue | Location | ... | Status | ACTION |\n\nThe Action column remains visible while horizontally scrolling.\n\nUse:\n\nposition: sticky\nright: 0\n\nwith appropriate background and border/shadow so it remains visually distinct.\n\nDo NOT make the entire table sticky.\n\nOnly use sticky columns when it improves usability.\n\n==================================================\n5. RESPONSIVE COLUMN BEHAVIOUR\n==================================================\n\nFor medium-width screens:\n\nReduce unnecessary whitespace.\n\nFor smaller desktop windows:\n\nAllow horizontal scrolling INSIDE the table container.\n\nFor very small screens:\n\nUse a stacked/card representation where appropriate instead of creating a giant inaccessible table.\n\nGovernment dashboard is desktop-first, but it must still behave correctly when the browser width changes.\n\n==================================================\n6. DO NOT SHRINK TEXT TO SOLVE THE PROBLEM\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT solve table overflow by making text microscopic.\n\nMaintain readable:\n\n- Font size\n- Line height\n- Row height\n- Button size\n\nUse wrapping / truncation where appropriate.\n\nExample:\n\nLocation:\n\342\200\234Koramangala 5th Block, Bengaluru...\342\200\235\n\nwith tooltip/full value on hover.\n\n==================================================\n7. ACTION BUTTONS\n==================================================\n\nMake action buttons compact but fully visible.\n\nExample:\n\n[Map]\n[Assign]\n[View]\n\nIf there are too many actions, use:\n\n[Actions \342\226\276]\n\ninstead of letting the buttons overflow outside the cell.\n\n==================================================\n8. AUDIT THE ENTIRE GOVERNMENT DASHBOARD\n==================================================\n\nSearch the entire application for:\n\n<table>\noverflow-x\noverflow\nmin-width\nwidth:\nwhitespace\nflex\ngrid\nsticky\n\nIdentify every location where a table can overflow its parent.\n\nApply one reusable:\n\nResponsiveTableContainer\n\ncomponent/pattern to all tables.\n\nDo not implement separate inconsistent fixes.\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 REBUILD AUTHENTICATION / ROLE NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nCURRENT PROBLEM:\n\nThe Sign Out and Switch to Citizen controls still do not reliably work.\n\nAs a result, I cannot access the Citizen version after entering the Government version.\n\nSTOP PATCHING THE EXISTING BUTTON HANDLERS.\n\nReplace the current role/navigation implementation with a SIMPLE, DETERMINISTIC DEMO ROLE SYSTEM.\n\nSince this is a frontend-only prototype, prioritize reliability and demonstrability.\n\n==================================================\n9. CREATE A SINGLE ROLE SELECTION ENTRY SCREEN\n==================================================\n\nCreate a dedicated route:\n\n/select-role\n\nThis page must ALWAYS be accessible.\n\nDisplay:\n\nCrowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\n\n\342\200\234Choose your experience\342\200\235\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nThe buttons must directly navigate to their respective demo environments.\n\n==================================================\n10. CITIZEN DEMO ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nClick:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n\342\206\222 /citizen/login\n\nOn this screen provide:\n\n[ Continue as Demo Citizen ]\n\nThis MUST immediately create the citizen session and open:\n\n/citizen/home\n\nDo not require real OTP.\n\nDo not require external authentication.\n\nDo not require any backend.\n\n==================================================\n11. GOVERNMENT DEMO ENTRY\n==================================================\n\nClick:\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\n\342\206\222 /government/login\n\nProvide:\n\n[ Continue as Municipal Officer ]\n\nThis MUST immediately create the government session and open:\n\n/government/dashboard\n\nDo not require external authentication.\n\n==================================================\n12. CREATE A SINGLE CENTRAL SESSION STORE\n==================================================\n\nRemove competing authentication logic.\n\nCreate ONE auth/session provider or store.\n\nState:\n\n{\n  activeRole: \"none\" | \"citizen\" | \"government\",\n\n  citizenSession: null | {\n    id,\n    name,\n    verified\n  },\n\n  governmentSession: null | {\n    id,\n    name,\n    role,\n    department\n  }\n}\n\nEvery page must read authentication state from this single source.\n\n==================================================\n13. REMOVE CONFLICTING AUTH VARIABLES\n==================================================\n\nAudit the entire application for:\n\nauthenticated\nisLoggedIn\nuser\ncurrentUser\nsession\nrole\ncurrentRole\n\nIf different components maintain their own authentication state, refactor them.\n\nThere must NOT be:\n\nPage A:\nisLoggedIn = true\n\nPage B:\nauthenticated = false\n\nPage C:\ncurrentRole = government\n\nwhile localStorage says citizen.\n\nUse the central auth store.\n\n==================================================\n14. SEPARATE STORAGE KEYS\n==================================================\n\nUse:\n\ncivic_citizen_session\n\ncivic_government_session\n\ncivic_active_role\n\nNever use one shared key such as:\n\nauthenticated\n\nfor both roles.\n\n==================================================\n15. HARD SIGN-OUT FUNCTION\n==================================================\n\nCreate exactly two centralized functions:\n\nlogoutCitizen()\n\nlogoutGovernment()\n\nCITIZEN:\n\nlogoutCitizen()\n\nmust:\n\n1. Delete civic_citizen_session\n2. Set citizenSession = null\n3. If activeRole == citizen:\n   set activeRole = none\n4. Delete civic_active_role\n5. Update global application state immediately\n6. Navigate to /select-role using route replacement\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\nlogoutGovernment()\n\nmust:\n\n1. Delete civic_government_session\n2. Set governmentSession = null\n3. If activeRole == government:\n   set activeRole = none\n4. Delete civic_active_role\n5. Update global application state immediately\n6. Navigate to /select-role using route replacement\n\nDO NOT navigate before clearing the session.\n\n==================================================\n16. SWITCH TO CITIZEN\n==================================================\n\nThe Government Dashboard currently has:\n\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nMake it call the central:\n\nswitchToCitizen()\n\nfunction.\n\nImplementation logic:\n\nswitchToCitizen():\n\n1. Clear government session\n2. Set governmentSession = null\n3. Set activeRole = none\n4. Clear active role storage\n5. Navigate to /select-role using replace()\n6. User selects Citizen\n7. Continue as Demo Citizen\n8. Open /citizen/home\n\nDO NOT directly navigate from Government Dashboard to:\n\n/citizen/home\n\nwithout establishing the citizen session.\n\n==================================================\n17. SWITCH TO MUNICIPAL STAFF\n==================================================\n\nImplement the reverse:\n\nswitchToGovernment()\n\nlogic:\n\n1. Clear citizen session\n2. Set citizenSession = null\n3. Set activeRole = none\n4. Clear active role storage\n5. Navigate to /select-role\n6. User selects Municipal Staff\n7. Continue as Demo Officer\n8. Open /government/dashboard\n\n==================================================\n18. REMOVE BROWSER-HISTORY PROBLEM\n==================================================\n\nAfter sign out or role switch:\n\nUse route replacement, not normal push navigation.\n\nFor example:\n\nreplace(\"/select-role\")\n\nThe user should NOT be able to press Back and instantly return to the authenticated dashboard.\n\nProtected routes must also reject the old session.\n\n==================================================\n19. PROTECTED ROUTES\n==================================================\n\nCITIZEN:\n\n/citizen/home\n/citizen/report\n/citizen/reports\n/citizen/profile\n\nRequire:\n\ncitizenSession != null\n\nOtherwise:\n\n\342\206\222 /citizen/login\n\nGOVERNMENT:\n\n/government/dashboard\n/government/issues\n/government/map\n/government/analytics\n/government/settings\n\nRequire:\n\ngovernmentSession != null\n\nOtherwise:\n\n\342\206\222 /government/login\n\n==================================================\n20. CRITICAL: DO NOT AUTO-LOGIN\n==================================================\n\nThis is likely causing the current problem.\n\nRemove any code that automatically recreates a demo session when:\n\n- Citizen dashboard loads\n- Government dashboard loads\n- Route changes\n- Component mounts\n- Page refreshes\n- User visits a dashboard path\n\nA session may ONLY be created by:\n\nCitizen:\nContinue as Demo Citizen\n\nGovernment:\nContinue as Municipal Officer\n\nor the explicitly simulated authentication flow.\n\n==================================================\n21. MAKE PROFILE BUTTONS RELIABLE\n==================================================\n\nThe profile menu must not disappear before the action is processed.\n\nCitizen:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\342\206\222 logoutCitizen()\n\nGovernment:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\342\206\222 logoutGovernment()\n\nSwitch:\n\nGovernment Profile\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\342\206\222 switchToCitizen()\n\nDo not duplicate these handlers in multiple components.\n\n==================================================\n22. ADD A GUARANTEED ROLE-SWITCH BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nFor demonstration purposes, add a small secondary action:\n\n\342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235\n\nThis must call:\n\nexitToRoleSelection()\n\nFunction:\n\n- Clear current role\n- Clear current session\n- Update global auth state\n- replace(\"/select-role\")\n\nThis is a reliable escape route for the demo.\n\n==================================================\n23. AUTHENTICATION DEBUG MODE\n==================================================\n\nAdd a development-only diagnostic panel.\n\nDisplay:\n\nActive Role:\nCitizen / Government / None\n\nCitizen Session:\nACTIVE / NONE\n\nGovernment Session:\nACTIVE / NONE\n\nCurrent Route:\n...\n\nButtons:\n\nClear Citizen Session\nClear Government Session\nClear All Sessions\nGo to Role Selection\n\nKeep this hidden behind:\n\nDevelopment / Debug\n\nDo not show it in the final normal user interface.\n\nThis is essential for diagnosing state problems while developing.\n\n==================================================\nPART 3 \342\200\224 MAKE CITIZEN ACCESS EASY TO DEMONSTRATE\n==================================================\n\nThe final navigation must be:\n\nOPEN APPLICATION\n\342\206\223\nROLE SELECTION\n\342\206\223\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202                      \342\224\202\nCitizen          Municipal Staff\n\342\224\202                      \342\224\202\n\342\206\223                      \342\206\223\nCitizen Login     Government Login\n\342\224\202                      \342\224\202\n\342\206\223                      \342\206\223\nDemo Citizen      Demo Officer\n\342\224\202                      \342\224\202\n\342\206\223                      \342\206\223\nCitizen Home       Government Dashboard\n\n==================================================\n24. EXACT DEMO SWITCHING FLOW\n==================================================\n\nThis exact sequence MUST work:\n\n1. Open application.\n2. Select Municipal Staff.\n3. Enter Government Dashboard.\n4. Open profile.\n5. Click Switch to Citizen.\n6. Confirm.\n7. Role Selection appears.\n8. Select Citizen.\n9. Click Continue as Demo Citizen.\n10. Citizen Home appears.\n\nThen:\n\n11. Open Citizen profile.\n12. Click Sign Out.\n13. Role Selection appears.\n14. Select Municipal Staff.\n15. Click Continue as Municipal Officer.\n16. Government Dashboard appears.\n\nRepeat this sequence multiple times.\n\n==================================================\n25. DATA MUST SURVIVE ROLE CHANGES\n==================================================\n\nSwitching roles must NOT remove:\n\n- Civic reports\n- Civic issues\n- Government dashboard data\n- Analytics\n- Images\n- Issue history\n- Mock citizen records\n- Language preference\n\nOnly authentication/session state changes.\n\n==================================================\nPART 4 \342\200\224 FINAL APPLICATION AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nBefore finishing, audit the application for:\n\nA. TABLES\n\nEvery table must:\n\n\342\234\223 Fit inside its page layout\n\342\234\223 Never clip columns\n\342\234\223 Keep Action accessible\n\342\234\223 Use internal horizontal scroll when needed\n\342\234\223 Never cause whole-page horizontal scrolling\n\342\234\223 Maintain readable text\n\342\234\223 Work at different desktop widths\n\nB. AUTHENTICATION\n\n\342\234\223 Citizen login works\n\342\234\223 Government login works\n\342\234\223 Citizen sign out works\n\342\234\223 Government sign out works\n\342\234\223 Switch to Citizen works\n\342\234\223 Switch to Municipal Staff works\n\342\234\223 Role Selection works\n\342\234\223 Browser Back cannot restore logged-out dashboard\n\342\234\223 Refresh preserves active session\n\342\234\223 Sessions are separated\n\342\234\223 Data survives logout\n\342\234\223 No automatic session recreation\n\342\234\223 No manual localStorage clearing required\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThere must be TWO fully usable environments:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 Simple citizen interface\n\342\206\222 Camera-first reporting\n\342\206\222 Reports\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\nGOVERNMENT\n\342\206\222 Detailed municipal dashboard\n\342\206\222 All data\n\342\206\222 Tables\n\342\206\222 Map\n\342\206\222 Analytics\n\342\206\222 Profile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Switch to Citizen\n\nAnd the user must be able to move between them repeatedly:\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Government\n\nwith NO:\n\n- browser restart\n- page refresh\n- manual storage clearing\n- broken route\n- stuck session\n- dead button\n\nFinally, preserve the exact official product name:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    }
  }
}
