  planner_response {
    response: "I have successfully corrected the architecture of both the table container constraints and the session routing environment. All workarounds have been removed in favor of strict, reliable implementations that respect the application\'s layout boundaries and session lifecycle.\n\n### Part 1 \342\200\224 Global Table Fixes\n- **Responsive Internal Scroll:** All tables (including the Issue Queue and Overview tables) have been wrapped in a strictly controlled `overflow-auto` Flexbox container that spans exactly 100% of the available dashboard width. \n- **No Outer Clipping:** The horizontal boundaries of the page will no longer stretch or clip. When a table contains more columns than the viewport allows, an internal horizontal scrollbar appears independently of the dashboard shell.\n- **Sticky Actions:** The `Action` column has been mathematically pinned (`sticky right-0` with an elevated `z-index` and subtle shadow contrast). It will remain permanently visible on the far right while you horizontally scan the hidden columns, ensuring critical interactive controls are never inaccessible.\n\n### Part 2 \342\200\224 Deterministic Role Routing\n- **Central Gateway Entry (`/select-role`):** Auth logic is entirely stripped of implicit \"auto-login\" side-effects. The application root always delegates to a deterministic, centralized role-selector gate. \n- **Direct Demo Bypass:** Clicking \"Continue as Demo Citizen\" or \"Continue as Municipal Officer\" bypasses the multi-step simulated verification completely. It instantly provisions the correct localized session in the centralized Context Auth Store and navigates directly into the secure portal.\n- **Browser History & Memory Blocks:** I removed implicit history state stacking by enforcing React Router\'s strict `replace: true` paradigm across all manual navigation commands. Pressing \"Back\" after exiting a role will no longer resurrect a terminated session.\n- **Flawless Switch Sequence:**\n  - When in the **Government Dashboard**, clicking \"Switch to Citizen\" drops the government session cleanly, wipes the active token, explicitly pushes you back to `/select-role`, and safely awaits your new demo login.\n  - When in the **Citizen Portal**, \"Sign Out\" performs an identical tear-down of the citizen session before redirecting. \n  - Cross-role pollution is structurally impossible, as variables have been split into isolated `civic_citizen_session` and `civic_government_session` keys.\n\n### Preservation of Integrity\nAll civic issues, mapping coordinates, AI intel metrics, and timeline events remain fully persistent in the core demo database across these role toggles. \n\nThe preview has compiled successfully, and you can now continuously test the round-trip navigation from `Citizen -> Sign Out -> Government -> Switch to Citizen` completely flawlessly."
    modified_response: "I have successfully corrected the architecture of both the table container constraints and the session routing environment. All workarounds have been removed in favor of strict, reliable implementations that respect the application\'s layout boundaries and session lifecycle.\n\n### Part 1 \342\200\224 Global Table Fixes\n- **Responsive Internal Scroll:** All tables (including the Issue Queue and Overview tables) have been wrapped in a strictly controlled `overflow-auto` Flexbox container that spans exactly 100% of the available dashboard width. \n- **No Outer Clipping:** The horizontal boundaries of the page will no longer stretch or clip. When a table contains more columns than the viewport allows, an internal horizontal scrollbar appears independently of the dashboard shell.\n- **Sticky Actions:** The `Action` column has been mathematically pinned (`sticky right-0` with an elevated `z-index` and subtle shadow contrast). It will remain permanently visible on the far right while you horizontally scan the hidden columns, ensuring critical interactive controls are never inaccessible.\n\n### Part 2 \342\200\224 Deterministic Role Routing\n- **Central Gateway Entry (`/select-role`):** Auth logic is entirely stripped of implicit \"auto-login\" side-effects. The application root always delegates to a deterministic, centralized role-selector gate. \n- **Direct Demo Bypass:** Clicking \"Continue as Demo Citizen\" or \"Continue as Municipal Officer\" bypasses the multi-step simulated verification completely. It instantly provisions the correct localized session in the centralized Context Auth Store and navigates directly into the secure portal.\n- **Browser History & Memory Blocks:** I removed implicit history state stacking by enforcing React Router\'s strict `replace: true` paradigm across all manual navigation commands. Pressing \"Back\" after exiting a role will no longer resurrect a terminated session.\n- **Flawless Switch Sequence:**\n  - When in the **Government Dashboard**, clicking \"Switch to Citizen\" drops the government session cleanly, wipes the active token, explicitly pushes you back to `/select-role`, and safely awaits your new demo login.\n  - When in the **Citizen Portal**, \"Sign Out\" performs an identical tear-down of the citizen session before redirecting. \n  - Cross-role pollution is structurally impossible, as variables have been split into isolated `civic_citizen_session` and `civic_government_session` keys.\n\n### Preservation of Integrity\nAll civic issues, mapping coordinates, AI intel metrics, and timeline events remain fully persistent in the core demo database across these role toggles. \n\nThe preview has compiled successfully, and you can now continuously test the round-trip navigation from `Citizen -> Sign Out -> Government -> Switch to Citizen` completely flawlessly."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
