    user_response: "CRITICAL PRODUCT + FUNCTIONALITY FIX\n\nUpdate the existing:\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235\n\nDO NOT redesign the application.\nDO NOT remove existing working functionality.\nDO NOT change the current visual identity unnecessarily.\n\nThis is a targeted correction of the following problems:\n\n1. Manual map pin placement does not work.\n2. Stray cattle report is showing a dog image.\n3. Citizens must NOT be able to switch directly to Municipal Staff.\n4. Remove \342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235.\n5. Language must be automatically determined from GPS location + Indian state.\n6. The top of the citizen screen is being cut off.\n7. Citizen identity data must be represented as securely hashed in the prototype.\n8. Sign Out is still broken.\n9. I currently cannot reliably reach the Government Portal.\n\nTreat the authentication/session issue as a HIGH-PRIORITY ARCHITECTURAL FIX.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 FIX AUTHENTICATION ARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nThe current role switching behavior is incorrect.\n\nA CITIZEN must NEVER have a direct \342\200\234Switch to Municipal Staff\342\200\235 action while still authenticated as a citizen.\n\nThe correct security model is:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nNOT:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nSimilarly:\n\nGOVERNMENT\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE \342\200\234SWITCH TO CITIZEN\342\200\235 FROM GOVERNMENT\n==================================================\n\nRemove the current:\n\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nbutton/action from the authenticated Government experience.\n\nIt must NOT exist inside:\n\n- Government profile menu\n- Government dashboard\n- Government navigation\n- Government settings\n\nA government user must also sign out before changing account type.\n\n==================================================\n2. REMOVE \342\200\234SWITCH TO MUNICIPAL STAFF\342\200\235 FROM CITIZEN\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT expose any direct citizen \342\206\222 government switching action.\n\nA citizen can only reach the Government Portal after:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nThis is an intentional access-control requirement.\n\n==================================================\n3. REMOVE \342\200\234EXIT TO ROLE SELECTION\342\200\235\n==================================================\n\nCompletely remove:\n\n\342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235\n\nfrom the application.\n\nDo not replace it with another equivalent shortcut.\n\nThe ONLY normal way to leave an authenticated environment should be:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection / Login\n\n==================================================\n4. FIX SIGN OUT AT THE ROOT LEVEL\n==================================================\n\nThe existing Sign Out button still does not work.\n\nDo NOT patch the visual button.\n\nAudit the entire authentication and routing implementation.\n\nCreate one central authentication/session manager.\n\nUse:\n\ncitizenSession\ngovernmentSession\nactiveRole\n\nDo NOT use a single global:\n\nauthenticated\n\nstate for both roles.\n\n==================================================\n5. CITIZEN SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nCitizen:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\nAfter confirmation:\n\n1. Remove citizen session from memory.\n2. Remove citizen session from localStorage.\n3. Set citizenSession = null.\n4. Set activeRole = null / none.\n5. Update global authentication state.\n6. Replace current route with the ROLE SELECTION page.\n\nThen:\n\nRole Selection:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nThe user can now explicitly choose another environment.\n\n==================================================\n6. GOVERNMENT SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nGovernment:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\nAfter confirmation:\n\n1. Remove government session from memory.\n2. Remove government session from localStorage.\n3. Set governmentSession = null.\n4. Set activeRole = null / none.\n5. Update global authentication state.\n6. Replace current route with ROLE SELECTION.\n\n==================================================\n7. ROLE SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nCreate/retain:\n\n/select-role\n\nDisplay:\n\nCrowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\n\nChoose your portal:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThis page must ONLY be reached from:\n- Initial application entry\n- Successful Sign Out\n\nIt must NOT be reachable as a \342\200\234switch account\342\200\235 shortcut while authenticated.\n\n==================================================\n8. GOVERNMENT LOGIN MUST BE RECOVERABLE\n==================================================\n\nI currently cannot reliably access the Government Portal.\n\nGuarantee the following path:\n\nOpen application\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Continue as Demo Municipal Officer\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nDo not require real OTP.\nDo not require external authentication.\n\nUse the existing demo authentication mechanism.\n\nThe Government Login route must always be reachable from the Role Selection page after logout.\n\n==================================================\n9. PROTECTED ROUTES\n==================================================\n\nCitizen pages:\n\n/citizen/home\n/citizen/report\n/citizen/reports\n/citizen/profile\n\nmust require:\n\ncitizenSession != null\n\nGovernment pages:\n\n/government/dashboard\n/government/issues\n/government/map\n/government/analytics\n/government/settings\n\nmust require:\n\ngovernmentSession != null\n\nIf authentication does not exist:\n\nCitizen route\n\342\206\222 /citizen/login\n\nGovernment route\n\342\206\222 /government/login\n\nNever automatically recreate a session.\n\n==================================================\n10. BROWSER BACK BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nAfter logout:\n\nThe user must NOT be able to press browser Back and regain access to the authenticated dashboard.\n\nUse route replacement rather than normal navigation when logging out.\n\nProtected routes must also reject stale sessions.\n\n==================================================\n11. AUTHENTICATION TEST\n==================================================\n\nThe following exact sequence MUST work:\n\nSTART\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Demo Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Demo Municipal Officer\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Demo Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nRepeat this sequence multiple times without:\n- refreshing\n- restarting\n- clearing localStorage\n- reopening the browser\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 FIX MANUAL MAP PIN\n==================================================\n\nThe manual map pin functionality currently does not work.\n\nOn the citizen Report Issue location screen:\n\nShow:\n\n\360\237\223\215 Current Location\n\nand:\n\n\342\200\234Adjust location\342\200\235\n\nWhen the user selects \342\200\234Adjust location\342\200\235:\n\nOpen a real interactive map.\n\nThe citizen must be able to:\n\n- Drag the map\n- Tap/click a location\n- Move a marker\n- Confirm the selected position\n\nAfter choosing a position:\n\nSave:\n\nlatitude\nlongitude\n\nUpdate the displayed address.\n\nExample:\n\nSelected Location:\n13.0827, 80.2707\n\nAddress:\nAnna Salai, Chennai\n\nButton:\n\n\342\200\234Use This Location\342\200\235\n\nThis button MUST actually update the report location and return to the report flow.\n\n==================================================\n3. MANUAL PIN FALLBACK\n==================================================\n\nIf GPS is unavailable or inaccurate:\n\nAllow:\n\nUse Current Location\n\nOR\n\nPlace Pin Manually\n\nManual pin placement must work independently of GPS.\n\n==================================================\n4. LOCATION CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nWhen the user manually moves the pin:\n\nUpdate:\n\nLatitude\nLongitude\nAddress\nCity\nState\n\nbased on the selected location.\n\nDo not leave the old address while the coordinates change.\n\n==================================================\nPART 3 \342\200\224 FIX STRAY CATTLE IMAGE\n==================================================\n\nThere is a data integrity problem.\n\nA report with:\n\nIssue:\nStray Cattle\n\nis displaying an image of a dog.\n\nThis is incorrect.\n\nAudit every existing mock report.\n\nThe image must correspond to the actual issue type.\n\nFor Stray Cattle:\n\nUse an image showing:\n- Cow\n- Cattle\n- Buffalo\n- Stray livestock\n\nDo NOT use:\n- Dog\n- Cat\n- Generic animal\n- Unrelated street scene\n\nLikewise verify all categories:\n\nPothole\n\342\206\222 pothole image\n\nGarbage\n\342\206\222 garbage image\n\nStreetlight\n\342\206\222 streetlight image\n\nDrain\n\342\206\222 drain image\n\nOpen Manhole\n\342\206\222 open manhole image\n\nStray Cattle\n\342\206\222 cattle image\n\nWater Leakage\n\342\206\222 water leakage image\n\nFallen Tree\n\342\206\222 fallen tree image\n\netc.\n\n==================================================\n5. IMAGE DATA VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate a category-to-image validation mapping.\n\nBefore rendering an image, verify that the image belongs to the issue category.\n\nDo not randomly assign images.\n\nEvery mock record must have:\n\nissueType\nimage\nbeforeImage\nafterImage\n\nwith matching semantic content.\n\n==================================================\nPART 4 \342\200\224 GPS + STATE-BASED DEFAULT LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nThe default language must be determined by:\n\nUSER GPS LOCATION\n+\nINDIAN STATE\n\nDo NOT simply use browser language.\n\nDo NOT simply hardcode:\nIndia \342\206\222 English.\n\n==================================================\n6. LOCATION \342\206\222 STATE \342\206\222 LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nUse the user\'s approximate geographic location.\n\nDetermine:\n\nLatitude\nLongitude\n\342\206\223\nState\n\342\206\223\nDefault Language\n\nCreate a state-to-language mapping for major Indian states/regions.\n\nExamples:\n\nTamil Nadu\n\342\206\222 Tamil\n\nKerala\n\342\206\222 Malayalam\n\nKarnataka\n\342\206\222 Kannada\n\nAndhra Pradesh\n\342\206\222 Telugu\n\nTelangana\n\342\206\222 Telugu\n\nMaharashtra\n\342\206\222 Marathi\n\nGujarat\n\342\206\222 Gujarati\n\nWest Bengal\n\342\206\222 Bengali\n\nPunjab\n\342\206\222 Punjabi\n\nRajasthan\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nUttar Pradesh\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nMadhya Pradesh\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nBihar\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nDelhi\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nHaryana\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nand so on.\n\nIf a state has multiple commonly used languages, choose the most appropriate default but ALWAYS allow manual change.\n\n==================================================\n7. PRIORITY OF LANGUAGE SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nUse exactly this order:\n\n1. Previously saved user language preference\n2. Otherwise GPS-based state detection\n3. Otherwise English fallback\n\nExample:\n\nUser in Tamil Nadu\n\342\206\222 default Tamil\n\nUser changes language to Hindi\n\342\206\222 Hindi becomes persistent preference\n\nLater:\n\342\206\222 continue using Hindi\n\nManual user preference must ALWAYS override GPS.\n\n==================================================\n8. LOCATION PERMISSION FAILURE\n==================================================\n\nIf location permission is denied:\n\nDo NOT break the application.\n\nFallback to:\n\nEnglish\n\nThen allow manual language selection.\n\nDo not repeatedly ask for GPS permission.\n\n==================================================\n9. LANGUAGE SHOULD BE SELECTED SILENTLY\n==================================================\n\nDo not make the user manually choose a language during onboarding.\n\nThe application should automatically determine the default language.\n\nThe user can change it later through:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Language\n\n==================================================\nPART 5 \342\200\224 FIX SCREEN / VIEWPORT CLIPPING\n==================================================\n\nThe screenshot shows the top portion of the citizen interface being cut off.\n\nAudit the entire citizen application for viewport and layout issues.\n\nThe following must NEVER be hidden behind the browser/device edge:\n\n- Header\n- Logo\n- Profile icon\n- Notification icon\n- Page title\n- First card\n- Navigation controls\n\n==================================================\n10. SAFE AREA + VIEWPORT\n==================================================\n\nEnsure the mobile citizen application respects:\n\n- Browser viewport\n- Mobile safe area\n- Header height\n- Bottom navigation height\n\nDo NOT allow content to render underneath the fixed header.\n\nUse appropriate top padding/margin.\n\nIf using:\n\nposition: fixed\n\nfor header/navigation:\n\nensure content has sufficient spacing.\n\n==================================================\n11. BOTTOM NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nThe bottom navigation must also remain fully visible.\n\nEnsure the page content has enough bottom padding so the final card is not hidden behind:\n\nHome\nReport\nMy Reports\nProfile\n\n==================================================\n12. RESPONSIVE TEST\n==================================================\n\nTest the citizen UI at:\n\n320px\n375px\n390px\n412px\n768px\n\nThe interface must remain usable.\n\nNo:\n\n- Cropped header\n- Hidden content\n- Horizontal page overflow\n- Cards extending beyond screen\n- Buttons cut off\n\n==================================================\nPART 6 \342\200\224 SECURE USER DATA DEMONSTRATION\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nI want the prototype to visibly demonstrate secure handling of sensitive identity information.\n\nDo NOT store or display a full Aadhaar number.\n\nDo NOT store real Aadhaar information.\n\nFor the frontend prototype, simulate secure storage using an irreversible cryptographic hash.\n\nUse an appropriate browser cryptographic API where available, such as:\n\nWeb Crypto API / crypto.subtle\n\nFor demonstration:\n\nAadhaar / phone input\n\342\206\223\nHashing\n\342\206\223\nOnly hash retained in the mock secure record\n\nDo NOT store:\n\nfull Aadhaar number\nraw OTP\nfull phone number\n\nin the simulated secure identity record.\n\n==================================================\n13. HASHING\n==================================================\n\nUse SHA-256 or another appropriate cryptographic hash for demonstration.\n\nPrefer:\n\ncrypto.subtle.digest()\n\nDo not manually implement SHA-256.\n\nDo not put sensitive values directly into:\n\nlocalStorage\n\nas plain text.\n\nFor the prototype:\n\nRaw input:\nNEVER displayed after verification\n\nStored representation:\nhashed identity value\n\n==================================================\n14. IMPORTANT DISTINCTION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT claim:\n\n\342\200\234Aadhaar is encrypted with hashing.\342\200\235\n\nHashing is NOT encryption.\n\nUse correct UI terminology:\n\n\342\200\234Identity identifier hashed\342\200\235\n\nor:\n\n\342\200\234Sensitive identifier stored as a one-way hash in this prototype.\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\n15. SECURITY DEMONSTRATION PANEL\n==================================================\n\nAdd a small:\n\n\342\200\234Privacy & Security\342\200\235\n\nsection inside the citizen profile.\n\nShow something like:\n\nIDENTITY\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nAADHAAR\n\342\234\223 Identifier protected\n\342\200\234Stored as one-way hash\342\200\235\n\nPHONE\n\342\234\223 Protected\n\342\200\234Stored securely\342\200\235\n\nPHOTO PRIVACY\n\342\234\223 Faces will be protected before evidence sharing\n(Do not apply the currently removed fake blur effect.)\n\nDo NOT reveal the actual hash unless useful for the prototype.\n\nIf you show it, display only a shortened representation:\n\nHash:\na81f\342\200\24693c2\n\nThis is for demonstration only.\n\n==================================================\n16. GOVERNMENT VIEW OF CITIZEN IDENTITY\n==================================================\n\nGovernment users should NOT see:\n\nFull Aadhaar number\nRaw phone number\nSensitive authentication information\n\nThey should only see:\n\nCitizen:\nSathyendhar B\n\nVerification:\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nCitizen ID:\nCIT-10482\n\nKeep sensitive identity data protected.\n\n==================================================\nPART 7 \342\200\224 GLOBAL DATA INTEGRITY AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nAudit ALL mock data.\n\nFor every report validate:\n\nIssue Type\nImage\nBefore Image\nAfter Image\nDescription\nLanguage\nCity\nState\nAddress\nLatitude\nLongitude\nJurisdiction\nAuthority\nDepartment\nStatus\n\nThey must be internally consistent.\n\nExamples:\n\nStray Cattle\n\342\206\222 cattle image\n\342\206\222 cattle description\n\nChennai\n\342\206\222 Chennai address\n\342\206\222 Chennai coordinates\n\342\206\222 Tamil report where appropriate\n\nDelhi\n\342\206\222 Delhi address\n\342\206\222 Delhi coordinates\n\342\206\222 Hindi report where appropriate\n\n==================================================\nPART 8 \342\200\224 DO NOT REINTRODUCE PREVIOUSLY REMOVED FEATURES\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT reintroduce:\n\n- Face blur overlays\n- Random blur circles\n- \342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n- \342\200\234Switch to Municipal Staff\342\200\235\n- \342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235\n- Automated jurisdiction routing\n- AI terminology on citizen screens\n- Internal government workflow on citizen screens\n\nThe citizen should remain simple.\n\n==================================================\nPART 9 \342\200\224 FINAL FUNCTIONAL TEST\n==================================================\n\nTEST AUTHENTICATION:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nRepeat several times.\n\nTEST ACCESS CONTROL:\n\nAuthenticated Citizen\n\342\206\222 No \342\200\234Switch to Municipal Staff\342\200\235\n\nAuthenticated Government\n\342\206\222 No \342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nNo \342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235 anywhere.\n\nTEST MAP:\n\nReport Issue\n\342\206\222 Location\n\342\206\222 Adjust Location\n\342\206\222 Map\n\342\206\222 Place Pin\n\342\206\222 Move Pin\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\342\206\222 Address updates\n\342\206\222 Report continues\n\nTEST LANGUAGE:\n\nLocation in Tamil Nadu\n\342\206\222 Default Tamil\n\nLocation in Hindi-speaking state\n\342\206\222 Default Hindi\n\nManual language change\n\342\206\222 Interface changes\n\nRefresh\n\342\206\222 Selected language persists\n\nTEST DATA:\n\nOpen Stray Cattle report\n\342\206\222 Cattle image\n\nOpen Pothole report\n\342\206\222 Pothole image\n\nOpen Garbage report\n\342\206\222 Garbage image\n\nVerify all existing records.\n\nTEST SCREEN:\n\nMobile width\n\342\206\222 Header fully visible\n\nMobile width\n\342\206\222 Bottom navigation fully visible\n\nNo content clipped.\n\nTEST SECURITY:\n\nSensitive identity information\n\342\206\222 Not displayed in raw form after verification\n\nStorage representation\n\342\206\222 One-way hash\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Shows verification status, not sensitive raw values.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe citizen experience must be:\n\nOPEN\n\342\206\223\nAuthenticate once\n\342\206\223\nCamera\n\342\206\223\nTake Photo\n\342\206\223\nDescribe Problem\n\342\206\223\nLocation Automatically Detected\n\342\206\223\nAdjust Pin if Needed\n\342\206\223\nSubmit\n\342\206\223\nTrack\n\342\206\223\nVerify Resolution\n\nThe government experience must be:\n\nRole Selection\n\342\206\223\nMunicipal Staff\n\342\206\223\nGovernment Login\n\342\206\223\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\223\nOperations\n\nAnd switching between environments MUST require logout:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nNo direct role switching while authenticated.\n\nFinally, preserve the exact official product name everywhere:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
    items {
      text: "CRITICAL PRODUCT + FUNCTIONALITY FIX\n\nUpdate the existing:\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235\n\nDO NOT redesign the application.\nDO NOT remove existing working functionality.\nDO NOT change the current visual identity unnecessarily.\n\nThis is a targeted correction of the following problems:\n\n1. Manual map pin placement does not work.\n2. Stray cattle report is showing a dog image.\n3. Citizens must NOT be able to switch directly to Municipal Staff.\n4. Remove \342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235.\n5. Language must be automatically determined from GPS location + Indian state.\n6. The top of the citizen screen is being cut off.\n7. Citizen identity data must be represented as securely hashed in the prototype.\n8. Sign Out is still broken.\n9. I currently cannot reliably reach the Government Portal.\n\nTreat the authentication/session issue as a HIGH-PRIORITY ARCHITECTURAL FIX.\n\n==================================================\nPART 1 \342\200\224 FIX AUTHENTICATION ARCHITECTURE\n==================================================\n\nThe current role switching behavior is incorrect.\n\nA CITIZEN must NEVER have a direct \342\200\234Switch to Municipal Staff\342\200\235 action while still authenticated as a citizen.\n\nThe correct security model is:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nNOT:\n\nCITIZEN\n\342\206\222 Switch to Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nSimilarly:\n\nGOVERNMENT\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\n==================================================\n1. REMOVE \342\200\234SWITCH TO CITIZEN\342\200\235 FROM GOVERNMENT\n==================================================\n\nRemove the current:\n\n\342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nbutton/action from the authenticated Government experience.\n\nIt must NOT exist inside:\n\n- Government profile menu\n- Government dashboard\n- Government navigation\n- Government settings\n\nA government user must also sign out before changing account type.\n\n==================================================\n2. REMOVE \342\200\234SWITCH TO MUNICIPAL STAFF\342\200\235 FROM CITIZEN\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT expose any direct citizen \342\206\222 government switching action.\n\nA citizen can only reach the Government Portal after:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\nThis is an intentional access-control requirement.\n\n==================================================\n3. REMOVE \342\200\234EXIT TO ROLE SELECTION\342\200\235\n==================================================\n\nCompletely remove:\n\n\342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235\n\nfrom the application.\n\nDo not replace it with another equivalent shortcut.\n\nThe ONLY normal way to leave an authenticated environment should be:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection / Login\n\n==================================================\n4. FIX SIGN OUT AT THE ROOT LEVEL\n==================================================\n\nThe existing Sign Out button still does not work.\n\nDo NOT patch the visual button.\n\nAudit the entire authentication and routing implementation.\n\nCreate one central authentication/session manager.\n\nUse:\n\ncitizenSession\ngovernmentSession\nactiveRole\n\nDo NOT use a single global:\n\nauthenticated\n\nstate for both roles.\n\n==================================================\n5. CITIZEN SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nCitizen:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\nAfter confirmation:\n\n1. Remove citizen session from memory.\n2. Remove citizen session from localStorage.\n3. Set citizenSession = null.\n4. Set activeRole = null / none.\n5. Update global authentication state.\n6. Replace current route with the ROLE SELECTION page.\n\nThen:\n\nRole Selection:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nThe user can now explicitly choose another environment.\n\n==================================================\n6. GOVERNMENT SIGN OUT\n==================================================\n\nGovernment:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Confirmation\n\nAfter confirmation:\n\n1. Remove government session from memory.\n2. Remove government session from localStorage.\n3. Set governmentSession = null.\n4. Set activeRole = null / none.\n5. Update global authentication state.\n6. Replace current route with ROLE SELECTION.\n\n==================================================\n7. ROLE SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nCreate/retain:\n\n/select-role\n\nDisplay:\n\nCrowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\n\nChoose your portal:\n\n[ Citizen ]\n\n[ Municipal Staff ]\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThis page must ONLY be reached from:\n- Initial application entry\n- Successful Sign Out\n\nIt must NOT be reachable as a \342\200\234switch account\342\200\235 shortcut while authenticated.\n\n==================================================\n8. GOVERNMENT LOGIN MUST BE RECOVERABLE\n==================================================\n\nI currently cannot reliably access the Government Portal.\n\nGuarantee the following path:\n\nOpen application\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Login\n\342\206\222 Continue as Demo Municipal Officer\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nDo not require real OTP.\nDo not require external authentication.\n\nUse the existing demo authentication mechanism.\n\nThe Government Login route must always be reachable from the Role Selection page after logout.\n\n==================================================\n9. PROTECTED ROUTES\n==================================================\n\nCitizen pages:\n\n/citizen/home\n/citizen/report\n/citizen/reports\n/citizen/profile\n\nmust require:\n\ncitizenSession != null\n\nGovernment pages:\n\n/government/dashboard\n/government/issues\n/government/map\n/government/analytics\n/government/settings\n\nmust require:\n\ngovernmentSession != null\n\nIf authentication does not exist:\n\nCitizen route\n\342\206\222 /citizen/login\n\nGovernment route\n\342\206\222 /government/login\n\nNever automatically recreate a session.\n\n==================================================\n10. BROWSER BACK BUTTON\n==================================================\n\nAfter logout:\n\nThe user must NOT be able to press browser Back and regain access to the authenticated dashboard.\n\nUse route replacement rather than normal navigation when logging out.\n\nProtected routes must also reject stale sessions.\n\n==================================================\n11. AUTHENTICATION TEST\n==================================================\n\nThe following exact sequence MUST work:\n\nSTART\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Demo Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Demo Municipal Officer\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Demo Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nRepeat this sequence multiple times without:\n- refreshing\n- restarting\n- clearing localStorage\n- reopening the browser\n\n==================================================\nPART 2 \342\200\224 FIX MANUAL MAP PIN\n==================================================\n\nThe manual map pin functionality currently does not work.\n\nOn the citizen Report Issue location screen:\n\nShow:\n\n\360\237\223\215 Current Location\n\nand:\n\n\342\200\234Adjust location\342\200\235\n\nWhen the user selects \342\200\234Adjust location\342\200\235:\n\nOpen a real interactive map.\n\nThe citizen must be able to:\n\n- Drag the map\n- Tap/click a location\n- Move a marker\n- Confirm the selected position\n\nAfter choosing a position:\n\nSave:\n\nlatitude\nlongitude\n\nUpdate the displayed address.\n\nExample:\n\nSelected Location:\n13.0827, 80.2707\n\nAddress:\nAnna Salai, Chennai\n\nButton:\n\n\342\200\234Use This Location\342\200\235\n\nThis button MUST actually update the report location and return to the report flow.\n\n==================================================\n3. MANUAL PIN FALLBACK\n==================================================\n\nIf GPS is unavailable or inaccurate:\n\nAllow:\n\nUse Current Location\n\nOR\n\nPlace Pin Manually\n\nManual pin placement must work independently of GPS.\n\n==================================================\n4. LOCATION CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nWhen the user manually moves the pin:\n\nUpdate:\n\nLatitude\nLongitude\nAddress\nCity\nState\n\nbased on the selected location.\n\nDo not leave the old address while the coordinates change.\n\n==================================================\nPART 3 \342\200\224 FIX STRAY CATTLE IMAGE\n==================================================\n\nThere is a data integrity problem.\n\nA report with:\n\nIssue:\nStray Cattle\n\nis displaying an image of a dog.\n\nThis is incorrect.\n\nAudit every existing mock report.\n\nThe image must correspond to the actual issue type.\n\nFor Stray Cattle:\n\nUse an image showing:\n- Cow\n- Cattle\n- Buffalo\n- Stray livestock\n\nDo NOT use:\n- Dog\n- Cat\n- Generic animal\n- Unrelated street scene\n\nLikewise verify all categories:\n\nPothole\n\342\206\222 pothole image\n\nGarbage\n\342\206\222 garbage image\n\nStreetlight\n\342\206\222 streetlight image\n\nDrain\n\342\206\222 drain image\n\nOpen Manhole\n\342\206\222 open manhole image\n\nStray Cattle\n\342\206\222 cattle image\n\nWater Leakage\n\342\206\222 water leakage image\n\nFallen Tree\n\342\206\222 fallen tree image\n\netc.\n\n==================================================\n5. IMAGE DATA VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nCreate a category-to-image validation mapping.\n\nBefore rendering an image, verify that the image belongs to the issue category.\n\nDo not randomly assign images.\n\nEvery mock record must have:\n\nissueType\nimage\nbeforeImage\nafterImage\n\nwith matching semantic content.\n\n==================================================\nPART 4 \342\200\224 GPS + STATE-BASED DEFAULT LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nThe default language must be determined by:\n\nUSER GPS LOCATION\n+\nINDIAN STATE\n\nDo NOT simply use browser language.\n\nDo NOT simply hardcode:\nIndia \342\206\222 English.\n\n==================================================\n6. LOCATION \342\206\222 STATE \342\206\222 LANGUAGE\n==================================================\n\nUse the user\'s approximate geographic location.\n\nDetermine:\n\nLatitude\nLongitude\n\342\206\223\nState\n\342\206\223\nDefault Language\n\nCreate a state-to-language mapping for major Indian states/regions.\n\nExamples:\n\nTamil Nadu\n\342\206\222 Tamil\n\nKerala\n\342\206\222 Malayalam\n\nKarnataka\n\342\206\222 Kannada\n\nAndhra Pradesh\n\342\206\222 Telugu\n\nTelangana\n\342\206\222 Telugu\n\nMaharashtra\n\342\206\222 Marathi\n\nGujarat\n\342\206\222 Gujarati\n\nWest Bengal\n\342\206\222 Bengali\n\nPunjab\n\342\206\222 Punjabi\n\nRajasthan\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nUttar Pradesh\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nMadhya Pradesh\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nBihar\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nDelhi\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nHaryana\n\342\206\222 Hindi\n\nand so on.\n\nIf a state has multiple commonly used languages, choose the most appropriate default but ALWAYS allow manual change.\n\n==================================================\n7. PRIORITY OF LANGUAGE SELECTION\n==================================================\n\nUse exactly this order:\n\n1. Previously saved user language preference\n2. Otherwise GPS-based state detection\n3. Otherwise English fallback\n\nExample:\n\nUser in Tamil Nadu\n\342\206\222 default Tamil\n\nUser changes language to Hindi\n\342\206\222 Hindi becomes persistent preference\n\nLater:\n\342\206\222 continue using Hindi\n\nManual user preference must ALWAYS override GPS.\n\n==================================================\n8. LOCATION PERMISSION FAILURE\n==================================================\n\nIf location permission is denied:\n\nDo NOT break the application.\n\nFallback to:\n\nEnglish\n\nThen allow manual language selection.\n\nDo not repeatedly ask for GPS permission.\n\n==================================================\n9. LANGUAGE SHOULD BE SELECTED SILENTLY\n==================================================\n\nDo not make the user manually choose a language during onboarding.\n\nThe application should automatically determine the default language.\n\nThe user can change it later through:\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Language\n\n==================================================\nPART 5 \342\200\224 FIX SCREEN / VIEWPORT CLIPPING\n==================================================\n\nThe screenshot shows the top portion of the citizen interface being cut off.\n\nAudit the entire citizen application for viewport and layout issues.\n\nThe following must NEVER be hidden behind the browser/device edge:\n\n- Header\n- Logo\n- Profile icon\n- Notification icon\n- Page title\n- First card\n- Navigation controls\n\n==================================================\n10. SAFE AREA + VIEWPORT\n==================================================\n\nEnsure the mobile citizen application respects:\n\n- Browser viewport\n- Mobile safe area\n- Header height\n- Bottom navigation height\n\nDo NOT allow content to render underneath the fixed header.\n\nUse appropriate top padding/margin.\n\nIf using:\n\nposition: fixed\n\nfor header/navigation:\n\nensure content has sufficient spacing.\n\n==================================================\n11. BOTTOM NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nThe bottom navigation must also remain fully visible.\n\nEnsure the page content has enough bottom padding so the final card is not hidden behind:\n\nHome\nReport\nMy Reports\nProfile\n\n==================================================\n12. RESPONSIVE TEST\n==================================================\n\nTest the citizen UI at:\n\n320px\n375px\n390px\n412px\n768px\n\nThe interface must remain usable.\n\nNo:\n\n- Cropped header\n- Hidden content\n- Horizontal page overflow\n- Cards extending beyond screen\n- Buttons cut off\n\n==================================================\nPART 6 \342\200\224 SECURE USER DATA DEMONSTRATION\n==================================================\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nI want the prototype to visibly demonstrate secure handling of sensitive identity information.\n\nDo NOT store or display a full Aadhaar number.\n\nDo NOT store real Aadhaar information.\n\nFor the frontend prototype, simulate secure storage using an irreversible cryptographic hash.\n\nUse an appropriate browser cryptographic API where available, such as:\n\nWeb Crypto API / crypto.subtle\n\nFor demonstration:\n\nAadhaar / phone input\n\342\206\223\nHashing\n\342\206\223\nOnly hash retained in the mock secure record\n\nDo NOT store:\n\nfull Aadhaar number\nraw OTP\nfull phone number\n\nin the simulated secure identity record.\n\n==================================================\n13. HASHING\n==================================================\n\nUse SHA-256 or another appropriate cryptographic hash for demonstration.\n\nPrefer:\n\ncrypto.subtle.digest()\n\nDo not manually implement SHA-256.\n\nDo not put sensitive values directly into:\n\nlocalStorage\n\nas plain text.\n\nFor the prototype:\n\nRaw input:\nNEVER displayed after verification\n\nStored representation:\nhashed identity value\n\n==================================================\n14. IMPORTANT DISTINCTION\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT claim:\n\n\342\200\234Aadhaar is encrypted with hashing.\342\200\235\n\nHashing is NOT encryption.\n\nUse correct UI terminology:\n\n\342\200\234Identity identifier hashed\342\200\235\n\nor:\n\n\342\200\234Sensitive identifier stored as a one-way hash in this prototype.\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\n15. SECURITY DEMONSTRATION PANEL\n==================================================\n\nAdd a small:\n\n\342\200\234Privacy & Security\342\200\235\n\nsection inside the citizen profile.\n\nShow something like:\n\nIDENTITY\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nAADHAAR\n\342\234\223 Identifier protected\n\342\200\234Stored as one-way hash\342\200\235\n\nPHONE\n\342\234\223 Protected\n\342\200\234Stored securely\342\200\235\n\nPHOTO PRIVACY\n\342\234\223 Faces will be protected before evidence sharing\n(Do not apply the currently removed fake blur effect.)\n\nDo NOT reveal the actual hash unless useful for the prototype.\n\nIf you show it, display only a shortened representation:\n\nHash:\na81f\342\200\24693c2\n\nThis is for demonstration only.\n\n==================================================\n16. GOVERNMENT VIEW OF CITIZEN IDENTITY\n==================================================\n\nGovernment users should NOT see:\n\nFull Aadhaar number\nRaw phone number\nSensitive authentication information\n\nThey should only see:\n\nCitizen:\nSathyendhar B\n\nVerification:\n\342\234\223 Verified Citizen\n\nCitizen ID:\nCIT-10482\n\nKeep sensitive identity data protected.\n\n==================================================\nPART 7 \342\200\224 GLOBAL DATA INTEGRITY AUDIT\n==================================================\n\nAudit ALL mock data.\n\nFor every report validate:\n\nIssue Type\nImage\nBefore Image\nAfter Image\nDescription\nLanguage\nCity\nState\nAddress\nLatitude\nLongitude\nJurisdiction\nAuthority\nDepartment\nStatus\n\nThey must be internally consistent.\n\nExamples:\n\nStray Cattle\n\342\206\222 cattle image\n\342\206\222 cattle description\n\nChennai\n\342\206\222 Chennai address\n\342\206\222 Chennai coordinates\n\342\206\222 Tamil report where appropriate\n\nDelhi\n\342\206\222 Delhi address\n\342\206\222 Delhi coordinates\n\342\206\222 Hindi report where appropriate\n\n==================================================\nPART 8 \342\200\224 DO NOT REINTRODUCE PREVIOUSLY REMOVED FEATURES\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT reintroduce:\n\n- Face blur overlays\n- Random blur circles\n- \342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n- \342\200\234Switch to Municipal Staff\342\200\235\n- \342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235\n- Automated jurisdiction routing\n- AI terminology on citizen screens\n- Internal government workflow on citizen screens\n\nThe citizen should remain simple.\n\n==================================================\nPART 9 \342\200\224 FINAL FUNCTIONAL TEST\n==================================================\n\nTEST AUTHENTICATION:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nRepeat several times.\n\nTEST ACCESS CONTROL:\n\nAuthenticated Citizen\n\342\206\222 No \342\200\234Switch to Municipal Staff\342\200\235\n\nAuthenticated Government\n\342\206\222 No \342\200\234Switch to Citizen\342\200\235\n\nNo \342\200\234Exit to Role Selection\342\200\235 anywhere.\n\nTEST MAP:\n\nReport Issue\n\342\206\222 Location\n\342\206\222 Adjust Location\n\342\206\222 Map\n\342\206\222 Place Pin\n\342\206\222 Move Pin\n\342\206\222 Confirm\n\342\206\222 Address updates\n\342\206\222 Report continues\n\nTEST LANGUAGE:\n\nLocation in Tamil Nadu\n\342\206\222 Default Tamil\n\nLocation in Hindi-speaking state\n\342\206\222 Default Hindi\n\nManual language change\n\342\206\222 Interface changes\n\nRefresh\n\342\206\222 Selected language persists\n\nTEST DATA:\n\nOpen Stray Cattle report\n\342\206\222 Cattle image\n\nOpen Pothole report\n\342\206\222 Pothole image\n\nOpen Garbage report\n\342\206\222 Garbage image\n\nVerify all existing records.\n\nTEST SCREEN:\n\nMobile width\n\342\206\222 Header fully visible\n\nMobile width\n\342\206\222 Bottom navigation fully visible\n\nNo content clipped.\n\nTEST SECURITY:\n\nSensitive identity information\n\342\206\222 Not displayed in raw form after verification\n\nStorage representation\n\342\206\222 One-way hash\n\nProfile\n\342\206\222 Shows verification status, not sensitive raw values.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL SUCCESS CONDITION\n==================================================\n\nThe citizen experience must be:\n\nOPEN\n\342\206\223\nAuthenticate once\n\342\206\223\nCamera\n\342\206\223\nTake Photo\n\342\206\223\nDescribe Problem\n\342\206\223\nLocation Automatically Detected\n\342\206\223\nAdjust Pin if Needed\n\342\206\223\nSubmit\n\342\206\223\nTrack\n\342\206\223\nVerify Resolution\n\nThe government experience must be:\n\nRole Selection\n\342\206\223\nMunicipal Staff\n\342\206\223\nGovernment Login\n\342\206\223\nGovernment Dashboard\n\342\206\223\nOperations\n\nAnd switching between environments MUST require logout:\n\nCitizen\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Municipal Staff Login\n\342\206\222 Government Dashboard\n\nGovernment\n\342\206\222 Sign Out\n\342\206\222 Role Selection\n\342\206\222 Citizen Login\n\342\206\222 Citizen Dashboard\n\nNo direct role switching while authenticated.\n\nFinally, preserve the exact official product name everywhere:\n\n\342\200\234Crowd Sourced Civic Issue Reporting and Resolution\342\200\235"
