    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prototype**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the user\'s request. My focus is on critical structural and functional fixes for the civic issue reporting prototype. I\'m starting by looking at the authentication architecture, specifically the removal of the direct switching between Citizen and Government roles. The goal is to streamline the login process and increase security.\n\n\n**Refining Role Management**\n\nI\'ve just refined the role management approach. I\'m removing direct role switching and implementing a forced sign-out/`select-role` system for enhanced security and streamlined access. This involves editing `GovApp.tsx` and `CitizenApp.tsx` to eliminate the old switching buttons and ensure that protected routes enforce this new pattern.\n\n\n**Implementing Role Separation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the role separation. I\'ve edited `Profile.tsx` to remove the role switch and enforce exit to role selection. In `AppContext.tsx`, I\'m removing the old swap commands, relying solely on `logoutCitizen` and `logoutGov` to redirect to `/select-role`. I will double check the protected routes in `App.tsx` for strict session matching.\n\n**Adding Manual Map Pin**\n\nNow I\'m working on the manual map pin task. The location step will feature a modal/inline map. I\'ll integrate Leaflet (`react-leaflet`) for a drag-able marker, converting coordinates to addresses using a mock reverse geocoding function.\n\n**Checking Mock Data Integrity**\n\nI\'m now checking data integrity. Reviewing `MOCK_ISSUES`, I\'m making sure \"Stray Cattle\" uses a cow image, and other categories are verified.\n\n\n**Integrating Geolocation Data**\n\nOkay, I\'m integrating geolocation data now. I\'ll use `navigator.geolocation` or a simulated location upon app start or language unset in `AppContext.tsx` or a hook to determine state. Then, I\'ll create a `stateToLanguage` mapping. English will be the fallback.\n\nI\'m also working on viewport clipping. I need to check header and bottom navigation padding in `CitizenApp.tsx` and ensure `pt-16` and `pb-16` are properly applied to the scrollable area.\n\nFinally, I\'m simulating Aadhaar hashing in `AuthFlow.tsx`, displaying \"Stored as one-way hash\" in Profile. Also, I\'ll add a \"Privacy & Security\" section in `Profile.tsx` and secure citizen identity representation (Sathyendhar B, Verified Citizen, CIT-10482) in issue views.\n\n\n"
