  }
  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the structural, architectural, and data-integrity fixes. The application now adheres strictly to the security routing constraints and provides a fully robust feature set.\n\n### 1. Authentication Architecture & Access Control\n- **Strict Role Isolation:** I have permanently removed the \"Switch to Municipal Staff\", \"Switch to Citizen\", and \"Exit to Role Selection\" shortcuts from all menus and dashboards.\n- **Root-Level Sign Out Fix:** The active session is now correctly wiped upon sign-out. The `logoutCitizen` and `logoutGov` handlers forcefully purge their respective state from memory, delete the isolated `localStorage` tokens, and cleanly replace the browser route back to `/select-role`.\n- **Browser History Integrity:** You can no longer press the browser\'s \"Back\" button to resurrect an authenticated session after logging out. Route matching is strictly protected.\n\n### 2. Manual Map Pin Placement\n- **Interactive Geolocation:** I replaced the static location change button with a fully interactive map powered by `react-leaflet`. \n- **Coordinates & Address Sync:** When \"Adjust location\" is pressed, citizens can drag the map, drop a pin, and select exact coordinates. \"Use This Location\" instantly updates the underlying report state to ensure the final submission has precision GPS tracking if the automated fallback fails.\n\n### 3. Secure Identity Demonstration\n- **One-Way Cryptographic Hashing:** The `AuthFlow` and core session state now store simulated SHA-256 hashes for sensitive identity items (Phone, Aadhaar) rather than exposing raw numbers.\n- **Privacy & Security Dashboard:** The Citizen Profile now features a dedicated security readout, demonstrating how the raw identity is shielded into irreversible hashes (e.g., `a81f...93c2`). \n- **Municipal Shielding:** When Government Officers view an issue in their dossier, a new \"Reporter Identity Shield\" block confirms that personal identifiers are completely obfuscated from municipal staff (displaying only the reporter name and `CIT-10482`).\n\n### 4. Semantic Mock Data \n- **Image Integrity:** The Stray Cattle report image has been corrected from a dog to a cow/cattle image. All mock report categories are now aligned with semantically correct photo evidence markers.\n\n### 5. Automated Language Localization\n- **GPS-to-State Mapping:** Upon initial load, the application silently requests `navigator.geolocation`. It calculates the user\'s rough bounding box\342\200\224dynamically switching the interface to **Tamil** if detected in Tamil Nadu, or **Hindi** if located in North/Central India. \n- **Fallback Hierarchy:** If location permissions are denied, it fails gracefully to English. Manual overrides from the Profile will always take permanent precedence. \n\n### 6. Viewport Clipping (Mobile Safe Area)\n- **Fluid Container Bounds:** I corrected the structural container scaling on mobile. The application root now explicitly utilizes `h-[100dvh]` (Dynamic Viewport Height) rather than rigid screen units. This ensures the fixed header and absolute bottom navigation never cut off the primary content, regardless of the mobile browser\'s address bar expanding or collapsing. \n\nThe preview has successfully compiled and is ready for comprehensive testing against your success conditions."
    modified_response: "I have completed the structural, architectural, and data-integrity fixes. The application now adheres strictly to the security routing constraints and provides a fully robust feature set.\n\n### 1. Authentication Architecture & Access Control\n- **Strict Role Isolation:** I have permanently removed the \"Switch to Municipal Staff\", \"Switch to Citizen\", and \"Exit to Role Selection\" shortcuts from all menus and dashboards.\n- **Root-Level Sign Out Fix:** The active session is now correctly wiped upon sign-out. The `logoutCitizen` and `logoutGov` handlers forcefully purge their respective state from memory, delete the isolated `localStorage` tokens, and cleanly replace the browser route back to `/select-role`.\n- **Browser History Integrity:** You can no longer press the browser\'s \"Back\" button to resurrect an authenticated session after logging out. Route matching is strictly protected.\n\n### 2. Manual Map Pin Placement\n- **Interactive Geolocation:** I replaced the static location change button with a fully interactive map powered by `react-leaflet`. \n- **Coordinates & Address Sync:** When \"Adjust location\" is pressed, citizens can drag the map, drop a pin, and select exact coordinates. \"Use This Location\" instantly updates the underlying report state to ensure the final submission has precision GPS tracking if the automated fallback fails.\n\n### 3. Secure Identity Demonstration\n- **One-Way Cryptographic Hashing:** The `AuthFlow` and core session state now store simulated SHA-256 hashes for sensitive identity items (Phone, Aadhaar) rather than exposing raw numbers.\n- **Privacy & Security Dashboard:** The Citizen Profile now features a dedicated security readout, demonstrating how the raw identity is shielded into irreversible hashes (e.g., `a81f...93c2`). \n- **Municipal Shielding:** When Government Officers view an issue in their dossier, a new \"Reporter Identity Shield\" block confirms that personal identifiers are completely obfuscated from municipal staff (displaying only the reporter name and `CIT-10482`).\n\n### 4. Semantic Mock Data \n- **Image Integrity:** The Stray Cattle report image has been corrected from a dog to a cow/cattle image. All mock report categories are now aligned with semantically correct photo evidence markers.\n\n### 5. Automated Language Localization\n- **GPS-to-State Mapping:** Upon initial load, the application silently requests `navigator.geolocation`. It calculates the user\'s rough bounding box\342\200\224dynamically switching the interface to **Tamil** if detected in Tamil Nadu, or **Hindi** if located in North/Central India. \n- **Fallback Hierarchy:** If location permissions are denied, it fails gracefully to English. Manual overrides from the Profile will always take permanent precedence. \n\n### 6. Viewport Clipping (Mobile Safe Area)\n- **Fluid Container Bounds:** I corrected the structural container scaling on mobile. The application root now explicitly utilizes `h-[100dvh]` (Dynamic Viewport Height) rather than rigid screen units. This ensures the fixed header and absolute bottom navigation never cut off the primary content, regardless of the mobile browser\'s address bar expanding or collapsing. \n\nThe preview has successfully compiled and is ready for comprehensive testing against your success conditions."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
